#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "How many of these places did the company build?"
msgstr "이 회사는 이런 장소를 몇 개나 지었나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Dozens, they told me.  Probably more by the end of it.  But they obviously "
"didn't say where or who for.  It was kind of a hot business and I think they"
" were some of the best doing it."
msgstr ""
"수십 개라고 하더군요. 아마 끝날 때쯤엔 더 많아졌을 거예요. 하지만 어디서, 누구를 위한 건지는 분명히 말씀 안 하셨죠. 꽤 핫한 "
"사업이었고, 그 분야에서는 그들이 최고였던 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
msgid "Right…"
msgstr "오른쪽…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Okay, listen… across the hall from the bedroom… by the pillars… it's a fake "
"wall.  Directly across the hall.  If you push in a little bit, the whole "
"thing kinda slides aside.  I hid some guns back there and a handful of "
"rounds, too.  I meant to bring a lot more - I had boxes on back order - but "
"it started getting hard to buy past a certain point.  Might as well share "
"now that we're here.  A spare bullet could save your life."
msgstr ""
"좋아, 들어봐... 침실 맞은편 복도에... 기둥 옆에... 가짜 벽이야. 복도 바로 건너편에 있어. 조금만 밀면 다 옆으로 미끄러져 "
"나가. 거기에 총 몇 자루랑 총알 몇 발 숨겨 뒀어. 원래는 훨씬 더 가져갈 생각이었거든. 주문이 밀려서 상자가 꽉 차 있었거든. 그런데"
" 어느 순간부터 사기가 힘들어졌어. 여기 왔으니 공유하는 게 좋겠어. 예비 총알이 네 목숨을 구할 수도 있잖아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "The wall thing is pretty nifty, I have to admit."
msgstr "벽이라는 게 꽤 멋진 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, but they put the secret room in their advertising.  Not really a "
"secret then, is it?"
msgstr "네, 하지만 광고에 비밀 방을 넣었잖아요. 그럼 사실 비밀은 아니잖아요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Hmm, good point."
msgstr "음, 좋은 지적이네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"What, like some secret Batcave?  Pull back the curtain and it turns out I'm "
"the communist <name_b> who brewed up a demon bio-weapon in their basement?  "
"I just gave you food, all the tools in my workshop, and the safest hole in "
"the ground in the county.  If I've got any secrets left, they're mine to "
"keep."
msgstr ""
"뭐, 비밀 배트케이브 같은 거? 커튼을 걷어내면 내가 바로 그 공산주의자 <name_b>라는 거야. 지하실에서 악마 생화학 무기를 "
"만들어낸 놈이지? 방금 너한테 음식이랑, 내 작업실에 있는 모든 도구랑, 이 지역에서 가장 안전한 구덩이를 줬어. 남은 비밀이 있다면, "
"다 내가 지킬 거야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
