#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"<lets_go>  I feel like it's useless worrying who they are when they're some "
"of the only friends we've got…"
msgstr "<lets_go> 그들이 우리의 유일한 친구일 텐데, 그들이 누구인지 걱정하는 건 쓸데없는 일인 것 같아요..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Once again, I'm staying out of the bone bullshit.  I hope the best for you "
"and the bone woman.  You definitely seem like you have things under control."
msgstr ""
"다시 한번 말하지만, 뼈 얘기는 꺼내지 않을게. 너랑 뼈 여자 잘 되길 바라. 너네는 확실히 상황을 잘 통제하고 있는 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Maybe I shouldn't have mentioned it…  Let's just get moving."
msgstr "아마 언급하지 말았어야 했을지도 몰라요... 바로 움직이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Honestly, it doesn't matter who opened up what portal to wherever.  "
"Extraterrestrial monster?  Engineered bio-weapon?  Three children standing "
"on each others' shoulders in an alien Halloween costume?  I'll blast 'em "
"either way."
msgstr ""
"솔직히, 누가 어디로 통하는 포탈을 열었는지는 중요하지 않아. 외계 괴물? 인공 생물 무기? 외계인 할로윈 의상을 입고 서로 어깨 위에 "
"서 있는 세 아이? 어쨌든 난 그들을 폭파할 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "'War of the Worlds', baby!  That's what I like to hear!  <lets_go>"
msgstr "'우주 전쟁'이라니! 내가 듣고 싶은 말인데! <lets_go>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"I refuse to believe things are just random.  Especially this!  The dead "
"don't start rising all over the world for no reason!"
msgstr "난 모든 게 그냥 무작위라고는 믿지 않아. 특히 이건! 죽은 자들이 아무 이유 없이 온 세상에서 부활하는 건 아니잖아!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Let's keep moving.  This is a topic for another day, when we've actually "
"found some answers…"
msgstr "계속해 봅시다. 이 주제는 나중에 몇 가지 답을 찾을 때 다시 이야기해 보도록 하죠…"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Check out that LMOE shelter"
msgstr "LMOE 쉼터를 확인해 보세요"

#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Maybe there's something left in that LMOE shelter you heard about."
msgstr "아마도 당신이 들었던 LMOE 보호소에 뭔가 남아 있을지도 몰라요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Any luck finding the LMOE shelter?"
msgstr "LMOE 보호소를 찾는 데 성공했나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Damn, can't believe we finally made it.  I was smart enough not to store "
"anything that might rot, so as long as nobody else already broke in, I bet "
"there's at least two weeks of good food just sitting there.  Pristine "
"workshop down there, too.  It cost me a pretty penny to get built.  I could "
"tell you all about it sometime if you ever wanted.  Anyway, thanks for "
"helping me get back here.  It sure ain't safe to travel on your own anymore."
msgstr ""
"젠장, 드디어 왔다는 게 믿기지 않아. 썩을지도 모르는 건 안 넣어둘 만큼 똑똑했으니까, 다른 사람이 먼저 훔쳐가지 않는 한 적어도 2주"
" 동안은 먹을 수 있는 좋은 음식이 저 안에 있을 거야. 게다가 저 아래엔 깨끗한 작업장도 있고. 만드는 데 꽤 돈이 들었어. 원하시면 "
"언젠가 다 얘기해 줄 수 있을 거야. 어쨌든, 여기로 돌아올 수 있게 도와줘서 고마워. 요즘 혼자 여행하는 건 정말 안전하지 않잖아."

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You approach the LMOE and do as you were told, prying back a thin piece of "
"metal atop the doorframe, revealing an opening.  You reach inside and grab a"
" handle attached to a wire, pull hard on it, and hear a heavy metal *clunk*."
"  The door is open."
msgstr ""
"LMOE에 다가가 시키는 대로 문틀 위의 얇은 금속 조각을 들어 올리자 문틈이 드러났다. 안으로 손을 넣어 전선에 연결된 손잡이를 잡고 "
"세게 당기자 묵직한 금속음(*쿵*)이 들렸다. 문이 열렸다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"Oh, man.  I thought I was ready.  I had it all planned out.  Bug out bags.  "
"Loaded guns.  Maps of escape routes.  Bunker in the back yard."
msgstr "얌마, 난 내가 준비됐다고 생각했어. 다 계획했다고. 탈출용 가방, 장전된 총, 탈출 경로 잔뜩. 뒷마당에 방공호까지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
