msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Forgot sommat?"
msgstr "추가하는 것을 잊으셨나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Forgot sommat?"
msgstr "추가하는 것을 잊으셨나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Forgot sommat?"
msgstr "추가하는 것을 잊으셨나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Ah, a returnin', an I'm ken."
msgstr "아, 돌아오는구나, 알았어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"&\"And a fine return, matey.\"  Rubik puts a hand on the countertop, and "
"gestures you closer with the other."
msgstr "&\"훌륭한 리턴이군, 친구.\" 루빅은 한 손을 조리대에 얹고 다른 한 손으로 당신에게 가까이 오라고 손짓한다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Fine and you still ain't dead.\"  Their gravelly voice is cheerful.  \"What "
"brings ye roun' Rubik's neckawoods?"
msgstr "좋아, 그리고 당신은 아직 죽지 않았군요.\" 그들의 쉰 목소리는 쾌활했다. \"루빅의 숲에 온 건 뭐야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Bright and sunny, you're back!\"  There's a bit of a friendly chuckle in "
"Rubik's gravelly voice.  \"Rubik's got goods for ye, if you got goods for "
"Rubik."
msgstr ""
"밝고 화창한, 돌아왔구나!\" 루빅의 쉰 목소리에 친근한 웃음소리가 살짝 섞여 있다. \"루빅이 네게 줄 선물이 있어, 네가 루빅에게 줄"
" 선물이 있다면 말이야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"&Before you stands a towering mass of metal, at least seven feet high, with "
"a large reflective glass plate in the center of its torso.  It turns as you "
"enter the room, and raises its hand in a surprisingly natural motion of "
"greeting.  A gravelly voice resonates from unseen speakers in the steel "
"frame.  Its tone is bizarrely normal, in complete contrast with everything "
"else around you.  \"Oy, you ain't dead.  Lookin' t'trade?\"  The accent "
"sounds vaguely British, but not familiar; like a terrible imitation of "
"Cockney."
msgstr ""
"당신 앞에는 높이가 최소 2미터는 되는 거대한 금속 덩어리가 서 있는데, 몸통 중앙에는 커다란 반사 유리판이 달려 있습니다. 방에 "
"들어서자 그 덩어리는 몸을 돌려 놀라울 정도로 자연스러운 인사 동작으로 손을 들어 올립니다. 철제 프레임 안의 보이지 않는 스피커에서 "
"걸걸한 목소리가 울려 퍼집니다. 그 목소리는 기묘할 정도로 평범해서 주변의 모든 것과는 완전히 대조적입니다. \"어머, 안 죽었어. "
"장사할 생각 있어?\" 영국식 억양이 살짝 들리지만, 익숙하지는 않습니다. 런던 사투리를 흉내 낸 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Who are you?  What is this place?"
msgstr "넌 누구야? 여긴 어디고?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Actually, I wanted to talk."
msgstr "얘기 좀 나누려고 왔어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Hell no, I'm out of here."
msgstr "제기랄, 여기서 나가야겠군."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Just popping in to say hi.  See you later, alligator."
msgstr "그냥 인사하러 들렀어. 나중에 봐."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "How is my buddy doing?"
msgstr "내 친구는 잘 지내고 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Fast, can you help this lad?"
msgstr "빨리, 이 젊은이를 도와줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We call ourselves the Exodii, eh?  And other things, but that's good.
#. This is our home, such as it is.  I'm called Rubik, and I've been assigned
#. to trade with you.  Are you looking to trade?  We're always looking for
#. scrap, metal and more.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Us call us the Exodii, eh?  An' other things, but that'n's good.  This're "
"our home, such as it.  This'n's monicked as Rubik, and tassed with a trade "
"an'.  You lookin' to trade?  Us'n's alay for the scrap, metal an' more as it"
" be."
msgstr ""
"우리를 엑소다이라고 부르지, 응? 다른 이름도 있지만, 괜찮아. 여기가 우리 집이야, 뭐 그런 거 말이야. 루빅이라고 불리고, 무역으로 "
"유명해. 거래할 생각 있어? 우리는 고철, 금속 따위를 사고파는 곳이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Good an' fine, then."
msgstr "그럼 좋고 훌륭하네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Have it as ye'll see."
msgstr "보시다시피 그렇게 하세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That was a good exchange.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "For a card an' a wink, eh?"
msgstr "카드 한 장이랑 윙크 한 번이면 충분하잖아?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"How come that dude is selling medieval gear in addition to all those guns?"
msgstr "저 친구가 총 외에 중세 장비도 팔고 있는 이유는 뭘까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"You seem to have a bunch of blueprints.  Can you tell me more about those?"
msgstr "청사진이 많던데, 다 뭐에 쓰는거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Have you anything more back there?"
msgstr "더 파는거 있어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It's a bit of a surprise, isn't it?  Before we came here, we were in a
#. place about 600 years earlier in time, or so.  We landed in the middle of a
#. war that turned wrong when the dead started joining back in.  Truth be
#. told, not a very unusual situation.  The Enemy makes us fight.  By and by,
#. we came in, and by then the killing fields were ready for us to harvest
#. their bronze.  It's not Avalonian steel, but it's a good strong metal for
#. stopping a nibbling mouth, so we kept some of their armor and weapons to
#. trade.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"That be a right welcher, eh?  Afore us'n were to this land, the preface were"
" on a half-score century by the reckonin'.  Landed us in amidst of a war'd "
"turned wrong, for an' as the dead had come back in.  By the butcher's block,"
" not much an unusual case, really.  The Enemy makes us fight.  By an' by, we"
" came in, an' by then the killin' fields were plump and ready to harvest the"
" bronze.  'Tain't no steel-of-the-lake, but 'tis a good dross metal for "
"holdin' off a nibblin' mouth, so we kept a few o' their vestments an' "
"stickers for to trade."
msgstr ""
"정말 대단하지, 그렇지? 우리가 이 땅에 오기 전, 서문은 50년 전의 일이었다. 우리는 잘못된 전쟁의 한가운데에 상륙했는데, 죽은 "
"자들이 다시 돌아왔다. 도살장에서 죽는 건 흔한 일이 아니었다. 적은 우리를 싸우게 한다. 그러던 어느 날, 우리는 도착했고, 그때쯤 "
"살육의 들판은 살이 쪄 청동을 수확할 준비가 되었다. 호수의 강철은 아니었지만, 갉아먹는 놈들의 입을 막기에는 좋은 찌꺼기 금속이었기에,"
" 우리는 그들의 옷과 스티커 몇 장을 교환용으로 남겨두었다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, you've got a discerning eye.  They're the result of many years of
#. work.  We've been fighting the Enemy for a long time, and over the years
#. we've worked out some armor for the job.  Keeps you going a bit longer in
#. the field, if you ask me.  I keep some of the parts in stock, but you'll
#. have to put it together yourself.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Ah, a real monger's eye, ye be.  Them's the mettle o' many a year of trials."
"  Us'n've been clashin wi' the Enemy for a long an' then, an' o'er the turns"
" us've worked out some vestments for the job.  Keep's a walker walkin' "
"longer, an I'm ken.  This'n keeps some o' the parst in an' around, but ye'd "
"be tassed to make the vestment with the grease o' your own brow."
msgstr ""
"아, 정말 대단한 사람이시군요. 수년간의 시련을 견뎌낸 용기가 바로 그것입니다. 우리는 오랫동안 적과 싸워 왔고, 그 과정에서 우리는 그"
" 임무에 맞는 제복을 만들어 왔습니다. 걷는 사람을 더 오래 걷게 하는 건, 제가 아는 사실입니다. 이렇게 하면 일부 부대를 제자리에 "
"가두어 둘 수 있겠지만, 자네는 자네 이마의 기름으로 제복을 만들어야 할 걸세."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What makes your specific armor so great?"
msgstr "너가 만드는 방어구가 그렇게 좋은 이유가 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Why do I have to make it myself?"
msgstr "왜 내가 직접 만들어야 하는데?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Why are your lockers full of medieval gear?"
msgstr "왜 보관함에 중세시대 장비로 가득 차 있는거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This and that, you know.  It's made for a traveling scavenger, you see.
#. What I mean is, it's well suited to carry around whatever you pick up in
#. the wastelands, without making it too hard to get around nor giving any
#. easy handholds for scrambling arms.  That, and I'd say it's as tough as
#. nails.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"This 'n that, an I'm ken.  It be made for a fine wander, beladen with the "
"goods o' the hunt, y'see.  By which I'm to say, 'tis well suited to carry "
"all ye can wrest from the cold arms o' the deadlands, without troublin' your"
" gait nor makin' it easy for the cold clutch o' the scrabblin' arm.  Be an' "
"it is tough as a tarket's nut, I'd razz."
msgstr ""
"이것저것, 그리고 난 알아. 사냥감들을 싣고 멋진 산책을 즐기기에 딱 맞는 가방이지. 그러니까, 차가운 사막의 팔에서 챙길 수 있는 모든"
" 것을 싣고 다니기에 딱 맞는 가방이라고 할 수 있지. 걸음걸이도 불편하지 않고, 허둥지둥하는 팔에 차가이 잡히는 것도 힘들지 않아. "
"그리고 이건 마치 표범의 견과류처럼 튼튼하다고, 내가 자랑하고 싶어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It's a simple matter of how we teleport.  Our clothes are often made from
#. cloth and hides from wherever we visit, and our teleporter tears living
#. stuff apart here and there when we travel.  Some can be saved if we take
#. care, but there's no room to store nearly enough extra.  That, and our
#. fabricators are always busy, no time to waste on stuff we don't need for
#. ourselves.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"'Tis as simple as comes to a wobble.  Our vestment be oft made from the fine"
" clothes and hides of the land, and our jibber tears the stuff o' life apart"
" here and there when us'n travel.  For as some can be saved if care be "
"taken, there be no case to store nigh enough o' this.  That, an' our manuc-"
"makers run as hot as a sunstone, no spit'n taste for that which we don't use"
" usselves."
msgstr ""
"비틀거리기라도 하듯 간단하죠. 우리의 옷은 흔히 그 땅에서 나는 좋은 옷과 가죽으로 만들어지고, 우리의 헛소리는 여행할 때마다 삶의 모든"
" 것을 찢어놓습니다. 조심하면 어떤 것들은 아낄 수 있지만, 이것들을 보관할 상자는 턱없이 부족합니다. 게다가 우리 제조업자들은 "
"태양석처럼 뜨겁게 달궈져서, 우리 스스로 쓰지 않는 것에는 침 뱉을 겨를이 없습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ HEH, you can't get enough of old Rubik's merchandise, eh?  Sure as hell,
#. come back after <restock_time_point>.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"HEH, ye c'nnae get enough o' ol' Rubik's merchandise, eh?  Sure as 'ell, "
"come back after <restock_time_point>."
msgstr "헤헤, 루빅스 상품은 이제 그만 사야지, 응? 그럼, <restock_time_point> 후에 다시 오렴."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You can surely try.  I'm not the greatest speaker, and I won't just chat
#. forever for free, you know.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sure as you c'n try.  Us're not the greatest yarker, nor do it all for "
"gratis, kennit."
msgstr "물론, 시도해 볼 수는 있겠죠. 우리는 최고의 야커도 아니고, 모든 걸 무료로 하는 것도 아니에요, 케닛."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Hey, can I ask you something first?
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Oy, c'n I bark you summat first?"
msgstr "아, 내가 먼저 뭐라고 소리쳐도 될까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Like, ask me a question?  Sure, I guess."
msgstr "어, 나한테 질문해도 되냐고? 물론, 당연하지."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Know where I can find any work?"
msgstr "뭐 도와줄 일 있을까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"No.  I'm too busy to answer your questions, you're supposed to answer mine."
"  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "아니요. 저는 너무 바빠서 당신의 질문에 답할 수 없어요. 당신이 제 질문에 답해야 해요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Of course, what can I do for you?
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sure as can,\" the gravelly voice takes on an unmistakeable 'customer "
"service' tone.  \"What'll ye tass this'n for?"
msgstr "\"물론이죠.\" 쉰 목소리에 틀림없이 '고객 서비스'라는 어조가 묻어났다. \"이걸 왜 샀어요?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I think I'm ready to try becoming a cyborg now."
msgstr "사이보그가 될 준비가 됐어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Any chance you could help me get some of those sweet bionic upgrades?"
msgstr "바이오닉 업그레이드 좀 도와줄 수 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Would you be willing to sell some of your robots?"
msgstr "여기에 있는 로봇 몇 대를 사고 싶어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Can you help me with CBM surgery?"
msgstr "바이오닉 수술 좀 해줘."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Can you turn me into a cyborg RIGHT NOW?  I'm a developer for this game, you"
" know."
msgstr "날 지금 당장 사이보그로 만들어줘. 지금 디버깅 중이거든."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Actually, I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "사실, 마음을 바꿨어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Business before pleasure.  What do you need?
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Aye, business afore, 'tis said.  What'll ye tass to ol' Rubik?"
msgstr "그래, 일은 끝났어. 루빅에 뭘 넣겠나?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Do the Exodii have any work I could do?"
msgstr "엑소다이에서 제가 할 수 있는 일이 있을까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I've brought the anesthetic for you.  Can you help me out?"
msgstr "마취제 가져왔어. 이제 시작해보자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I paid a visit to the bunker."
msgstr "벙커를 조사하고 왔어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I found the warehouse."
msgstr "창고를 찾았어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Nah, mate, still operatin'."
msgstr "아니, 친구야, 아직도 운영 중이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Ok.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "알겠습니다. <end_talking_bye>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Give me a second, and I'll bring them here.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Gimme spek, 'n  fetch 'em 'ere."
msgstr "베이컨을 줘, 여기로 가져와."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Of course, it is time for us to talk."
msgstr "물론, 이제 우리가 이야기할 시간입니다."

#. ~ Player sees NPC spawns in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Rubik leads a person to you."
msgstr "루빅은 사람을 당신에게 인도합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Let's see what I get."
msgstr "무슨 결과가 나올지 봅시다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "It is time to put this body to rest."
msgstr "이제 이 몸을 쉬게 할 때가 되었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Let me see.  Will do what I can for a coin.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Lemme poke.  Will tass what ye can for a shiny."
msgstr "찔러볼게. 반짝반짝하게 하려면 뭐든지 찔러볼게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[Prototype Cyborg] Can you help this guy it seems like they have lost their "
"mind?"
msgstr "[프로토타입 사이보그] 이 사람이 정신을 잃은 것 같은데 도와줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[Broken Cyborg] Can you save my buddy who looks a bit rough around the "
"edges, but they still haven't flatlined?"
msgstr "[부서진 사이보그] 좀 거칠어 보이는 친구를 구해줄 수 있나요? 아직은 펑크가 나지 않았어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Actually, forget it's not my problem."
msgstr "사실, 그건 내 문제가 아니라는 걸 잊어버려요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ For this one, I can pull out their CBM and give any working to you, or I
#. can just take out broken bits so that they will still be able to use the
#. rest of stuff in them.  Alternatively, why don't you just give them to me?
#. I surely can help them adjust to life as a cyborg.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Fer this 'un, I can yank out their bits 'n give 'em to ya, or I can jus' "
"take out the busted pieces so they can still use th' rest o' stuff in 'em. "
"Elsewise, why don't ya jest give 'im to me?  I reckon I can turn 'im into a "
"right useful worker."
msgstr ""
"이 녀석, 그 부품들을 빼내서 너한테 줄 수도 있고, 아니면 그냥 부서진 부품들만 빼서 나머지 부품들을 쓸 수 있게 해 줄 수도 있어. "
"아니면, 그냥 나한테 주는 게 어때? 내가 이 녀석을 아주 쓸모있는 일꾼으로 만들어 줄 수 있을 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[$300] Take everything from him and if there is something useful, put it "
"aside for me."
msgstr "[$300] 그에게서 모든 것을 빼앗아, 쓸모 있는 것이 있다면 나를 위해 따로 보관해 줘."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[200$] Just remove broken bits so they can control themselves."
msgstr "[200$] 부러진 부분만 제거하면 스스로 제어할 수 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[95$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  Just bring my buddy "
"back."
msgstr "[95$] 다 꺼내세요. 쓸 만한 건 가져가세요. 제 친구만 데려오세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "They are all yours.  [Adds 200$]"
msgstr "모두 당신 것입니다. [200달러 추가]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This one can't be saved, too much brain rotted.  But I can salvage bits
#. from them or repurpose them for walker, or just cut out rot and neural
#. interface so you can bury them proper.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"This 'unwon't be twitching', too much grey lost to dead.  But ye can salvage"
" bits from 'em or born 'em for a walker, or just cut out the rot 'n grey "
"link so ya can miss 'em proper."
msgstr ""
"이 '움찔거리지 않을' 놈은 죽은 놈들 때문에 회색이 너무 많이 사라졌어. 하지만 그놈들한테서 조각을 뜯어내거나, 워커한테 물려주거나, "
"아니면 그냥 썩은 회색 고리를 잘라내서 제대로 못 보게 할 수도 있어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[200$] Pull out CBM if he can't use it, I can."
msgstr "[200$] 그가 못 쓰면 CBM을 꺼내줘, 내가 쓸 수 있어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[25$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  He deserves a burial."
msgstr "[25$] 다 꺼내세요. 쓸 만한 건 가져가세요. 그는 장례를 치러야 할 사람입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "They are all yours.  [Adds 150$]"
msgstr "모두 당신 것입니다. [150달러 추가]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "'Ow long's it been since the mess happened?"
msgstr "'그 일이 일어난 지 얼마나 됐지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[Tell them.]"
msgstr "[그들에게 말해.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Thank ye.  When you an' Rubik first met, how long'd it been since the mess "
"begun?"
msgstr "고맙습니다. 당신과 루빅이 처음 만났을 때, 그 혼란이 시작된 지 얼마나 되었나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Lovely!  Benzete (this is a name) is going to be beside themselves,
#. that's for sure.  I mean, they'll be really happy.  This is their first
#. jump, and it's a lucky one.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Lovely!  Benzete's gonna be a pair, that's a track!  I mean, they'll be "
"right happy.  This is their first jump, and it's a flappin' duck."
msgstr "멋지다! 벤제테는 한 쌍이 될 거야, 트랙이잖아! 걔네는 정말 기뻐할 거야. 이게 걔네 첫 점프고, 펄럭이는 오리잖아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What makes it such a good jump?"
msgstr "평행세계 여행에 좋고 나쁘고가 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Who is Benzete?"
msgstr "벤제테가 누구야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ As I recall, we were talking about Benzete and how this is a great jump
#. for their first time.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"So 'twere an I recalt, us're yarkin' of Benzete an' their great first jump."
msgstr "그래서 저는 벤제테와 그들의 위대한 첫 점프에 대해 회상합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We've got to leave the old world before it gets too worn out, you see,
#. and find a nice fresh one on the other side.  Your deadland is as fresh as
#. it gets.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Us gotta leave the old world afore it's worn right to the gums, an y'ken, "
"and find a nice twitchy one on t'other side.  Your deadland be a brand shiny"
msgstr ""
"잇몸까지 닳아 없어지기 전에 낡은 세상을 떠나야 해, y'ken, 그리고 반대편에서 멋지고 switty한 세상을 찾아야 해. 네 죽음의 "
"땅은 반짝반짝 빛날 거야"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I'm not following that at all."
msgstr "…최상의 컨디션이라니? 무슨 말인지 이해가 안 가는데."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[INT 9] So you mean, we have a nice, freshly dead world for you to visit?"
msgstr "[지능 9] 그러면 여기가 너에겐 '신선한' 세계라는거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ No worries.  I mean, the Enemy is new here, and we have a bit of safe
#. time ahead of us before we have to jump away again.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Neverken.  Right and so, the Enemy is new here, and us'n have a few good "
"hours in the sun beforenext the jump."
msgstr "네버켄. 맞아요, 적은 여기 새로 왔고, 다음 점프 전에 햇볕 아래서 몇 시간 푹 쉬어야겠어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Oh, you mean you got here early in the Cataclysm.  Why is that so good?"
msgstr "네 말은 여기 대격변이 얼마 안 됐을때 왔다는 말이구나. 그게 왜 좋은데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's a part of it, sure, but this is nice for other reasons, and much
#. better than our last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are
#. really useful to us.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"That be a part an' switch, but this be'n nice for all, overtop the last jump"
" by heads.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings, us'n gets a fine change "
"on that."
msgstr ""
"그건 일부이고 전환점이지만, 이건 모두에게 좋을 거야. 마지막 점프를 앞지르는 것보다 훨씬 낫지. 다른 땅에서는 맹렬한 공격과 폭동이 "
"벌어지니까, 우리는 거기서 멋진 변화를 맞이하게 될 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I don't know what fusillies and mobbings are."
msgstr "금충이랑 역중이 뭔지 모르겠는데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's exactly it!  This is nice for many reasons, and much better than
#. our last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are really useful to
#. us.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"You kennit rightly!  That and this be'n nice for all, overtop the last jump "
"by heads.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings, us'n gets a fine change "
"on that."
msgstr ""
"네 말이 맞아! 그거랑 이거랑은 모두에게 좋을 거야. 마지막 점프보다 훨씬 더 잘할 수 있을 거야. 다른 나라들은 총격전과 폭동으로 가득"
" 차 있으니까, 우리도 거기서 멋진 변화를 맞이하게 될 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Wait, am I following this right?  You're from a place where this happened "
"before, and you escaped to our world?"
msgstr "잠깐, 내가 제대로 이해하는거 맞는거지? 너희는 이 재앙이 일어난 세계를 탈출해서 우리 세계로 온거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, yeah.  Lots of places have different words for those.  A fusilly is a
#. weapon that fires a bullet at high speeds using propellant.  A mobbing is a
#. big metal box that's moved around by an internal explosion.  Do you get it?
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Oh, rights.  Many lands be'd assert on thosun's.  A fusilly, she's a weapon,"
" shoots a shot at high speeds usin' bang.  A mobbing, he's a grand box o' "
"metal, pushed by burnin' and boomin' from wit'in, kennit?"
msgstr ""
"오, 맞아. 많은 땅이 저 태양 위에 있을 거야. 그녀는 무기처럼 맹렬하게, 쾅 소리를 내며 고속으로 총을 쏘지. 놈은 거대한 금속 "
"상자처럼, 안에서 타오르고 쿵쾅거리며 밀려나, 알겠지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[INT 7] Sounds like you mean a fusilly is a gun, and a mobbing is a car?"
msgstr "[지능 7] 금충은 총이고, 역중은 자동차 같은데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, I'll put that in the dictionary.  Here's a token of my gratitude
#. for your explanation.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Right so, us'n'll write it in the dicky.  Here, a shiny brass farthing for "
"crossin' the nation."
msgstr "좋아, 그럼 우리도 딕키에 적어두자. 자, 전국을 횡단하는 반짝이는 황동 동전 한 닢을 주마."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Now that we've sorted that out, I have to ask.  You're from a place where "
"this happened before, and you escaped to our world?"
msgstr "자 이제 해결됐으니, 이번엔 내가 질문할게. 너희는 이 재앙이 일어난 세계를 탈출해서 우리 세계로 온거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ They're an otherlander from around three jumps ago, a real optimistic
#. greenhorn.  They're really interested in how we do tracking, you see?
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Them's an otherlander from thrice jumps an' change, wide as the sky.  They's"
" got happily on sommat for the tracking, you ken?"
msgstr "그들은 세 번이나 뛰어올라 하늘만큼 넓은 타지인이야. 그들은 추적을 위해 소맷에 기꺼이 올라탔지, 알겠지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I… didn't really follow that."
msgstr "어… 무슨 말인지…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Like an apprentice to the old tracker.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Hmm.  They… planned out the last jump?  Like as an apprentice to the ol' "
"sexten."
msgstr "음. 그들이… 마지막 점프를 계획한 건가? 마치 옛날 섹스텐의 견습생처럼."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Oh, like a navigator?"
msgstr "항해사처럼?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Sure, that word is fine, I think.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Sure an' that's a fine enough word, an I'm ken."
msgstr "물론이죠. 꽤 좋은 단어예요. 저도 알아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "You said this was an especially good jump?"
msgstr "이번에 한 이동이 유난히 좋다고 했었지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, you could say that.  We're from otherlands, most of the time.  Not
#. otherworlds though.  Too risky bringing those monsters into our safe haven.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, you could call us as it.  Us're from otherlands mostlike.  Not "
"otherworlds though.  Too risky bringin' them squelchies into the fold."
msgstr ""
"그래, 그렇게 불러도 돼. 우리는 다른 나라에서 온 것 같아. 다른 세계는 아니지만. 그 놈들을 우리 편으로 끌어들이는 건 너무 위험해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I don't know the difference between otherlands and otherworlds."
msgstr "다른 세계와 다른 세상의 차이가 뭔지 모르겠는데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, that's a big question.  Otherworlds are how you got those ugly bug-
#. creatures around here, you know?  Walking plants, talking mushroom, stuff
#. like that.  Otherlands are closer related.  I'm from Earth, just a
#. different Earth.  You shouldn't be asking what the Exodii are doing in
#. Earth, because some of us are feeling pretty at home here, I think.  You
#. should be asking what we're doing hanging out in your part of town.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sure an that's a biggun'.  Otherworlds be the wherefore o' them uggo buggers"
" you got round and here, eh?  Walkin' plants and talkin' mushrooms and "
"whatlike.  Otherlands be tassed more of a kinship.  I be from Earth, but my "
"Earth be differed.  So you's shouldno be asked what the Exodii is doin' on "
"Earth, because some is feelin' of us fine an' fine at home, an I'm ken.  "
"You's should be askin' what the Exodii is doin' razzin up your green and "
"brown."
msgstr ""
"물론이지. 그건 큰일이야. 다른 세계가 너희가 여기 있는 그 놈들의 이유일지도 모르지, 응? 걸어다니는 식물, 말하는 버섯, 뭐 그런 "
"것들 말이야. 다른 세계는 더 친족 관계처럼 느껴질 거야. 난 지구 출신이지만, 내 지구는 달라. 그러니 엑소다이가 지구에서 뭘 하고 "
"있는지 너희한테 묻지 마. 어떤 사람들은 우리가 집에 있는 게 괜찮다고 생각하고, 나도 알아. 너희는 엑소다이가 너희 녹색과 갈색을 "
"뒤흔들고 있는 걸 물어봐야 해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "OK then, what are you meaning with 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "그럼 우리 땅에서 뭐하는거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Tell me about your own world."
msgstr "너가 살던 세상을 알려줘."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah.  Home.  That's a long time gone, you know?  Yours isn't too
#. different.  I… don't think I want to talk about it.  I've changed too much
#. between then and now.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"*becomes distant for a moment.  \"Ah.  Home.  It were a long time gone, "
"kennit.  Your'n be not too far.  This'n… I don't think I want to talk 'bout "
"it.  Too much metal atwixt now an' then.\""
msgstr ""
"*잠시 멀어진다. \"아. 집. 오래전에 떠났었지, 케닛. 그리 멀지 않을 거야. 이건… 그 얘기는 하고 싶지 않아. 지금과 그때 사이에"
" 메탈이 너무 많아.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "That's rough, maybe we should talk about something else."
msgstr "미안해. 주제를 바꾸자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What are you meaning with 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "궁금해서 물어보는건데, 우리 땅에서 뭐하는거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "How did you come to be made of metal like this?"
msgstr "넌 왜 이렇게… 강철로 둘러싸인거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I realized that it was a no-brainer question.  There was only one other
#. option, you see, if I didn't join the Exodii.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Us'n saw this were a pidgeon's road, I'd razz.  Only one way, I'm ken, if "
"I'm not to join the rank an' file."
msgstr "이게 비둘기 길이라면, 난 화를 낼 거야. 내가 일반 대열에 합류하지 않으려면, 단 한 가지 방법밖에 없어, 난 알아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"I think I know what you mean.  The only way to survive is to… \"upgrade\".  "
"Can you help me with that?"
msgstr "무슨 말인지 알겠네. 살아남으려면… \"업그레이드\"를 해야한다는 거지. 나도 해줘."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Robot?  What does that word mean?  Hang on.  …Ah, an automate?  No, I'm
#. as flesh and blood as you are, encased in a shell of metal and wire.  Not
#. as much flesh as there used to be.  The wire is mixed and woven into the
#. flesh, all as one, you see.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Robot?  What assert is f'r it?  Ahold…\"  Rubik stops for a moment, as if "
"thinking.  \"Ah, an automate?  No, this'n be flesh 'n blood as ye be, "
"encased in a shell o' metal an' wire.  Not so much flesh as there were.  The"
" wire is amixed an' afloat with the flesh, all as one, kennit."
msgstr ""
"로봇? 무슨 주장이야? 아홀드…\" 루빅은 잠시 생각에 잠긴 듯 멈췄다. \"아, 자동화? 아니, 이건 마치 너희처럼 살과 피가 있는 "
"존재야. 금속과 철사 껍질에 싸인 존재 말이야. 살이 많은 존재는 아니지만. 철사는 살과 섞여 떠다니고, 모두 하나처럼 말이야, 케닛."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[INT 9] So you're a cyborg of some kind?  That's awesome.  How do I become a"
" cyborg?"
msgstr "[지능 9] 그럼 사이보그라는 소리야? 쩌는데? 나도 사이보그가 되고 싶어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"I don't have any idea what you mean.  You're kind of a robot, but you're "
"also flesh and blood?"
msgstr "무슨 말을 하려는지 모르겠어. 넌 로봇인데, 피와 살이 붙은 로봇이라는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What are you meaning 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "궁금해서 물어보는건데, 우리 땅에서 뭐하는거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, that's the basic explanation.  A bit of both now, but I used to be
#. just like you.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, that be the soggy leaves, an I'm ken.  A bit o' both, but Rubik were "
"once as a kin, to you be."
msgstr "응, 그건 축축한 잎 때문이고, 나도 알아. 둘 다 조금씩은 있지만, 루빅은 한때 너와 친족이었지."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "This is confusing.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "이건 혼란스럽네요. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ A junker base, obviously.  A jury-rigged mess.  We'll pack it up and
#. leave eventually.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"A junker base, innit?  Pile o' gamp.  Us'll pack it up and sing along soon "
"enough."
msgstr "쓰레기 기지, 그렇지? 덩치 큰 놈들아. 곧 짐 싸서 따라 부르자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Pack it up?  How can you pack up something like this?"
msgstr "짐 싸고 여길 떠난다고? 여길 통째로?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Soon?  How long will you still be here?"
msgstr "여기에 얼마나 더 오래 있을건데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ The otherlands we were in before had only little time left, so we can't
#. say for sure.  But this land is as fresh as it can be.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Yon aforetime otherland, 'twere a right soggy biscuit.  This'n be crisp an' "
"fresh yet.  Us'n'll try as might stay a fair tick."
msgstr "예전에는 다른 나라에서 비스킷이 축축했었어요. 이건 아직도 바삭하고 신선해요. 최대한 공정하게 유지하려고 노력할게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Good to know you will be here for a while."
msgstr "그래도 여기에 오래 있는다는 거네. 알려줘서 고마워."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ To understand how, you've gotta think eleven-dimensionally.  We'll open
#. up a gate and teleport out, the same as we came.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"For an' how, ye be needin' to think wi' them elevens o' directions, kennit?"
"  Us'll open a gate an' wibble-an-wobble.  Same as us came."
msgstr "그리고 어떻게, 그 11개 방향으로 생각해야 하는 거야, 케닛? 우리가 문을 열고 흔들흔들 흔들거릴 거야. 우리랑 똑같아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, good question.  Enough cybernetic implants can keep someone from
#. coming back as a zombie, but it's not a sure thing.  Some come back anyway,
#. and some just don't have enough cybernetics.  Most of them aren't full
#. Exodii like old Rubik, they're more our friends - like you.  Sooner or
#. later we'll get out there, put them down, and bring their parts back for
#. cleaning.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"'Tis a good an' yark, sooth.  Them as can have the metal deep in, can be "
"saved for the risen, but it b'ain't a sure course.  Some as comes back "
"anyway, an' some be too much flesh.  The grander lot are no Exodii like ol' "
"Rubik, most be friends more kin to thyself.  Us'll hearken out and trundle "
"home the pieces for a scrub-and-bucket."
msgstr ""
"정말 좋은 물건이야. 쇠가 깊숙이 박힌 것들은 부활을 위해 아껴둘 수 있지만, 확실한 길은 아니야. 어떤 것들은 어차피 다시 돌아오고, "
"어떤 것들은 살이 너무 많아. 더 훌륭한 것들은 늙은 루빅처럼 엑소다이가 아니야. 대부분은 너와 더 가까운 친구들이지. 우리는 귀 기울여"
" 듣고 조각들을 모아서 문지르고 양동이에 담아 갈게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"So you use these cybernetics to prevent zombification, but they don't work "
"perfectly?  Why not?"
msgstr "바이오닉이 다시 되살아나는걸 막는데, 왜 완벽하게 막지 못하는거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I don't think I'm the best to explain that, but I'll do my best.  Our
#. technology might seem pretty high-tech and well made to you, but on the
#. inside I'm still mostly human meat bound up in wires and steel.  Nobody's
#. left that remembers exactly how it all goes, and much of it is cobbled
#. together from a few different dimensions.  It's a miracle they work as well
#. as they do, but somehow it's actually pretty functional.  Still, it can be
#. hard to know exactly what could go wrong.  The ones who come back as
#. zombies, they're generally less well made than me.  Some even did their own
#. cybernetic conversions, and didn't exactly follow best practices.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Rubik's not the finest dandy to yark it, an I'm ken, but this'n'll do best "
"as can.  Ol' Rubik an' the stompy-clanker gang be shiny an' fine as can be, "
"for y'see so well, but on the wind-up, the guts be nigh so fleshy as they "
"were afore, twixt as they be with wire and steel.  Ain't none so left as "
"remembers precise how it all goes, and much is boggled from bits and drabs "
"o' a dozen elsewheres.  'Tis a marked fine they work at all, though work "
"they do, and nicely.  Still, 'tis hard to know what'll crumple out from the "
"can.  Those as return, they be… less well made as ol' Rubik.  Some as did "
"work themselves, even, and mayhap against the good old ways."
msgstr ""
"루빅은 다루기엔 그다지 멋진 녀석은 아니지만, 나도 잘 알지만, 이게 제일 나을 거야. 늙은 루빅과 쿵쿵거리는 놈들은 반짝반짝 빛나고 "
"아주 정교해. 잘 보이잖아. 하지만 태엽을 감으면 철사와 강철로 감싼 것처럼 속은 예전처럼 두툼해. 모든 게 어떻게 돌아가는지 정확히 "
"기억하는 사람은 아무도 없고, 다른 데서 뜯어낸 조각들로 많은 걸 알아내지. 어쨌든 잘 돌아가긴 하지만, 제대로 작동하고, 또 잘 "
"굴러가긴 해. 하지만 캔에서 무엇이 구겨질지는 알기 어려워. 다시 말해, 늙은 루빅만큼 잘 만들어지지는 않을 거야. 심지어 스스로 "
"작동하는 것도 있고, 어쩌면 옛날 방식에 어긋나는 것도 있을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"You seem to have a lot of standardized robotic helpers, like those quads.  "
"Is that a different thing?"
msgstr "뭔가 다른 로봇들도 있는거 같던데. 저 다리 네 개 달린 커다란 것들 말이야. 저것들은 다른거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"*'s tone changes slightly, sounding a bit pained.  \"Ah, them be an in-"
"between, more machiner.  Us'n use the softer bits o' other critters for "
"them, an' there be a manufactory for the walker.  A hard but needed "
"choice.\""
msgstr ""
"*의 어조가 살짝 바뀌며, 약간 고통스러워하는 듯 들린다. \"아, 그들은 중간쯤 되는 기계가 될 거야. 다른 생물들의 부드러운 부분을 "
"그들에게 쓰도록 하고, 워커를 위한 공장도 만들어야지. 힘들지만 필요한 선택이었어.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "How long does it take you to make one of these walkers?"
msgstr "저 기계들을 만드는 데 얼마나 오래 걸려?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Can I buy one of your machines?"
msgstr "저 기계 중 하나를 사도 될까?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Faster than you might guess, but it can still take a while, the hardest
#. part is sourcing the materials for one.  We've got printers that make the
#. body, and others that make the tools and equipment the walker will use.
#. Some of the special parts have to be manufactured by hand, so we have a
#. small team that does that.  Right now, it's very slow, we're still setting
#. up our operations.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Blinker than a bat, but downer than a cat.  Razzin' up the bits be a trick "
"and some.  The draw-make automates can manufactorize the outer shell, and "
"there be automates for the most o' the tools.  Some bits be more a breakfast"
" o' rats, an' for them, us'n has some artisanals.  Us'n b'ain't on the solid"
" now, so 'tis a longer down."
msgstr ""
"박쥐보다 눈은 번쩍거리지만 고양이보다 더 우울해. 부품을 다듬는 건 꽤 어려운 일이야. 드로 메이크 자동 기계로 외피를 제작할 수 있고,"
" 대부분의 도구에는 자동 기계가 있어. 어떤 부품은 쥐들의 아침밥에 가깝고, 그런 부품들을 위해 우리는 장인 기술을 가지고 있지. 지금은"
" 견고한 상태가 아니니, 더 긴 시간이 필요해."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I don't know about that.  Each one we make is very important to our
#. operations here, and they're extremely expensive.  I might be able to sell
#. you one later, but not right now.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"*sounds thoughtful.  \"This'n can't make a call o' the quarter.  The "
"stompers be a king's necklace, and the manufactory don't run on dreams.  "
"Mayhap when us'n be more on the solid, but for the tick and tumble, no.\""
msgstr ""
"*생각에 잠긴 듯. \"이건 25센트를 깎아내릴 수 없어. 스톰퍼는 왕의 목걸이고, 공장은 꿈으로 돌아가지 않아. 우리가 더 견고한 "
"쪽으로 갈 수 있을지도 모르지만, 똑딱거리고 넘어지는 건 안 돼.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, we're always in need of some help around here.  Here's the list
#. I've got for stuff like this.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"*pulls out a sheaf of mismatched papers, and leafs through the pages for a "
"second.  Their broad metallic fingers look surprisingly deft and delicate, "
"and incongruous on the otherwise unremarkable looseleaf.  \"Aye, an' there's"
" room for a pop-an-work roun' here.  Rubik's got tassed a lissy, right and "
"clean"
msgstr ""
"*서로 어울리지 않는 종이 뭉치를 꺼내 잠깐 페이지를 넘긴다. 그 넓은 금속 손가락은 놀라울 정도로 능숙하고 섬세해 보이는데, 별 특징 "
"없는 낱장 용지와는 어울리지 않는다. \"그래, 그리고 여기 잠깐 놀 공간 있어. 루빅이 리시를 제대로 닦았어.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ".  Right and so, mayhap ye should first see about that escoltin'.\""
msgstr ". 그렇군요. 그럼, 아마도 먼저 그 에스코트에 대해 알아보시는 게 좋을 겁니다.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ", but for the right-an-quick, this'n has nothin' t'be tassed for ye.\""
msgstr "하지만 오른쪽과 빠른 사람을 위해 이건 당신에게 적합하지 않습니다.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
".  How'd ye be twigged by a pop-an-squeak?  Or as y'r tassed, a treasure "
"hunt?\""
msgstr ". \"펑 하고 끼익거리는 소리에 어떻게 반응할 수 있어? 아니면, 보물찾기라도 하는 거지?\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
".  How'd ye be twigged by a quick an' round, a nice escoltin' out to a place"
" sommat of curiosity?\""
msgstr ". 호기심을 불러일으키는 곳으로 재빨리 가서 구경하는 건 어때요?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sounds like you're saying a job?  That's what I'm looking for.  Tell me "
"more."
msgstr "일거리가 있나보네. 어떤건지 말해줘."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I'm not interested in anything right now.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "지금은 아무것도 관심없어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Sure you can, at least a bit.  I'll do my best to speak your Anglic, but
#. seeing as we're from otherlands and all, it's not that simple.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sure as ye can, at least sommat.  Us'n'll try as we might to parley your "
"Anglic, but so ye kennit as us be from otherlands and all, it ain't that "
"simple."
msgstr ""
"물론이죠, 적어도 몇 가지는요. 우리는 당신의 영어 실력을 최대한 끌어내려고 노력하겠지만, 우리가 다른 나라에서 왔다는 걸 알고 있으니 "
"그렇게 간단한 일은 아니죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[INT or PER 7] How come you speak English, or uh, 'Anglic' like that?"
msgstr "[지능/지각 7] 너는 왜 말하는게… 그런거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, right and so.  Each and every.  We wander, we make do.  It's a "
"livin'."
msgstr "아, 맞아. 매번. 우리는 돌아다니고, 해결해. 그게 삶의 방식이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What drove you out?"
msgstr "떠도는 이유가 뭐야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Same as you, I'd guess.  The Enemy.  The dead.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Same as you will be, an I'm ken.  The Enemy.  The dead."
msgstr "너도 그럴 거고, 나도 알아. 적. 죽은 자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Just so, aye.  Again an' again, this'n has seen it.  Too many times."
msgstr "그렇죠. 또, 또, 또, 이런 일이 반복되죠. 너무 많이요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Do you know what's going on?  What caused all this?"
msgstr "혹시 왜 이런 일이, 아니, 도대체 어떤게 이 짓을 저지른지 알고 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Is it always like this?  What's going to happen to us?"
msgstr "원래 이런거야? 우리는 어떻게 되는거지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You want to get religious, eh?  I can't tell you for sure, but the people
#. who claim to know, they talk about the Enemy.  Most folks have a fairy tale
#. like that, I think.  A monster from ancient memory, returned.  I don't know
#. much about that, but something makes those bodies walk and moan, and it
#. doesn't seem to be anything human.  How it gets in, well, that's anyone's
#. guess.  It can come the way we came, through a portal, but it doesn't
#. always.  How it was for your world, I can't tell you.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"F'r to wax religious, eh?\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik pauses for a while.  When they start talking again, their voice is slow and more serious than usual.*\n"
"\n"
"This'n can't tell ye, rightly, but those what have a bottle an' a cork what fits it, they yark about the Enemy.  Most folks got a story like that in their ol' hearth-tales, an I'm ken.  A bad way, from times old, come back.  Ol' Rubik don't know much about that, but something makes them bodies walk and moan, and it don't seem to be somethin' of the way o' our kin.  How it gets in, well, that be anyone's for a guess.  It can come the way we came, wibbling and wobbling, but it don't always.  How it be'd the end for your deadland, Rubik can't say for ye."
msgstr ""
"종교에 젖어들려고, 응?\n"
"\n"
"*루빅은 잠시 멈춘다. 그들이 다시 말을 시작하자, 목소리는 평소보다 느리고 진지해진다.*\n"
"\n"
"이건 네가 정확히 무슨 뜻인지 알 수 없지만, 병과 코르크 마개를 가진 자들은 적에 대해 떠든다. 대부분의 사람들은 옛날 난로 이야기에서 그런 이야기를 들었고, 나도 안다. 옛날부터 나쁜 방식으로 돌아온다. 늙은 루빅은 그것에 대해 잘 모르지만, 무언가가 그들의 몸을 걷고 신음하게 만드는데, 우리 친척들의 방식과는 다른 것 같다. 그것이 어떻게 들어오는지는, 글쎄, 그건 누구도 추측할 수 없다. 우리가 온 방식대로 비틀거리며 들어올 수도 있지만, 항상 그런 것은 아니다. 루빅은 네 죽음의 땅이 어떻게 끝났는지 말할 수 없다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Wait, it can come like you did?  Did you bring this here?!"
msgstr "잠깐만, 너희가 이동하듯 올 수도 있다고? 너희들이 이 짓을 한거야?!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"No!  Bluster an' clouds, no!\"  Rubik's voice comes haltingly, as if they "
"are picking their words with unusual care for clarity.  \"We done a few "
"things what Rubik don't like to pickle an'… to think about, but never that!"
"  We came after the fall, long after.  Always."
msgstr ""
"안 돼! 허세 부리고 구름 껴도 안 돼!\" 루빅의 목소리가 멈칫거렸다. 마치 그들이 말을 고르는 데 남다른 주의를 기울이는 듯했다. "
"\"우리는 루빅이 피클처럼 생각하고 싶지 않은 일을 몇 번 했지만, 그런 일은 절대 없었어! 추락 후에, 한참 후에야 왔지. 항상 "
"그랬어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is a deadland, you see.  Take a moment and look around, know what I
#. mean?  What's left for you?  The dead will be in the fields, the forests,
#. all over the world.  Anything that walks, they'll make it so it doesn't,
#. and most will come back as undead.  Those that don't, the Enemy will change
#. them as well.  Every deadland is the same.  You've years and more to go,
#. but one way or another, this place is dead.  Though, as far as I can see,
#. you've got quite a few years to go yet.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"This be a deadland, kennit.  Spend a farthing at the pastor's house, d'ye "
"razz?  What be left for ye?  The dead'll be in the fields, the forests, all "
"around the green and brown.  Anything what walks, they'll salt 'n fallow, "
"and most'll rise up and rejoin.  Those what don't, the Enemy twists and "
"turns as well.  Every deadland be the same.  Ye've turns and twain, but come"
" as it may, this land be dead.  Though, an I'm ken, ye've quite a few turns "
"and twain to go yet."
msgstr ""
"여긴 죽은 땅일 거야, 케닛. 목사님 댁에서 한 푼이나 써, 이 멍청아? 너희에게 남은 건 뭐야? 죽은 자들은 들판과 숲, 온통 푸르고 "
"갈색일 거야. 움직이는 건 뭐든 소금기 띤 채로 묵혀둘 테고, 대부분은 일어나 다시 합류할 거야. 움직이지 않는 자들은 원수가 뒤틀고 "
"뒤틀어. 모든 죽은 땅은 똑같아. 네게는 뒤틀리고 뒤틀리는 게 있지만, 어쨌든 이 땅은 죽은 땅이야. 하지만, 내가 알기로는, 아직 꽤 "
"많은 뒤틀리고 뒤틀려야 해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"What then?  What happens after the whole planet dies?  Could it spread to "
"other worlds from here?"
msgstr "그러면 이 세계가 완전히 끝장나면 어떻게 되는거야? 다른 세계로 퍼질수도 있는거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"That's pretty hopeless talk.  I've killed a lot of zombies, I can beat this "
"'Enemy' too."
msgstr "너무 절망적인 얘기인걸. 난 좀비를 많이 죽여봤는데, 이 사태의 원흉도 이겨낼 수 있을거야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Spread, yes, through the portals, but we don't know how.  After the world
#. is down to dust, I'm long gone.  Once or twice we've send back a probe to
#. the deadlands we left behind, but none have returned.  As far as I know,
#. there's only one way it goes from here.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Spread, aye, through the wibbles, but we ain't ken on how.  After the green "
"an' brown be to grey and black, so t'speak, Rubik be long gone.  On a "
"moment, we folk've sent back a lover's robe or so t'the deadlands what left,"
" but narry have returned.  An I'm ken, there be only one course from here."
msgstr ""
"그래, 위블을 통해 퍼져나가지만, 어떻게 될지는 모르겠어. 녹색과 갈색이 회색과 검은색으로 변한 후, 말하자면 루빅은 오래전에 사라졌지."
" 한때 우리는 연인의 옷이나 그 정도를 죽음의 땅으로 돌려보냈지만, 아무도 돌아오지 않았어. 그리고 난 알아, 여기서부터는 오직 한 "
"길뿐일 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"So traveling off-world is definitely an option.  Or getting to the ISS, "
"maybe stepping off from there."
msgstr ""
"그러니 우주를 벗어나 여행하는 것도 분명 선택지 중 하나입니다. 아니면 국제 우주 정거장에 가서 거기서 내리는 것도 좋은 방법일 수 "
"있겠죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"It sounds like a secure base with a safe perimeter could last a long time.  "
"Maybe forever."
msgstr "튼튼한 기지만 있으면 오래 버틸 수 있을 것 같은데. 어쩌면 평생 버티기도 할 것 같고."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"I haven't seen many zombies underground.  Seems like it might be possible to"
" make a safe base down there."
msgstr "생각해보니 지하에는 좀비들이 별로 없는 것 같아. 지하에 기지를 두면 안전할 것 같은데?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "So what do you do, then?  How do you get out, and how do I do that?"
msgstr "그러면 너는? 어떻게 살아남는거야? 나도 살아남을 수 있을까?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ If you want to try it, I won't stop you.  In fact, I'll sell you
#. equipment that might help.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"If ye be champed t'try, this'n won't stop ye.  Right so, Rubik'll sell ye "
"the pieces ye might use t'do."
msgstr "만약 네가 도전할 용기가 있다면, 이건 너를 막을 수 없을 거야. 그래, 루빅이 네가 쓸 만한 조각들을 팔 거야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You do that then.  I'll cheer for you when you stand over the vanquished
#. corpse of the devil himself.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine.  Rubik'll clarion for ye when ye stand o'er the garried trick"
" o' Anubine hisself."
msgstr "좋아, 좋아. 아누빈이 직접 만든 속임수 위에 서면 루빅이 분명하게 들릴 거야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I'm a lowlife from old Upper Landing, this is my way of talking.
#. Everyone from where I come from talks like this.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Be an' as us're a dock climber from ol' Upper Landin', this'll be our way o'"
" yarkin'.  All an' all from our green an' brown yark like this'n."
msgstr "어퍼 랜딩에서 온 부두 등반가처럼, 이 길로 야크를 향해 나아가자. 이런 푸르고 갈색 야크에서 모든 걸 다 해내다니."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Tell me about \"ol' Upper Landing\".  What was your home like?"
msgstr "어퍼랜딩에 대해 말해줘. 네 고향은 어땠어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ha!  A new part of our crew.  Signed up early on in the world we were in
#. before.  He's a really tough guy, and the node appreciates his grit.
#. (Recites some poetry), as it were.  I think he's pretty good as a military
#. commander.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Ha!  A new string and beans, an I'm ken.  Latched and keyed in the bright "
"shine o' the deadland afore this'n.  He be a thing o' fire and bronze, an' "
"the node appreciates his grit.  \"A cnight of old, clade in shining steel, "
"leading the hoste onward to glorie,\" as 'twere.  This'n finds him an apt "
"one to give rede.  To command in battle, that's t'yark."
msgstr ""
"하! 새 끈과 콩, 그리고 나는 안다. 이 전에 죽은 땅의 밝은 빛에 걸고 열쇠로 잠갔다. 그는 불과 청동으로 된 존재였고, 노드는 그의"
" 투지를 높이 평가했다. \"빛나는 강철을 두른 늙은 기사가 군대를 영광으로 이끌었다.\" 그는 전장에서 지휘하는 데 적합한 인물이었다."
" 전투에서 지휘하는 것이 바로 t'yark였다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"You know, every so often you talk normally and I realize you could probably "
"drop the whole accent if you wanted to."
msgstr "그러고 보니, 굳이 이런 억양이 아니더라도 말을 제대로 할 수 있을 것 같은데."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"I think I've had about enough of trying to figure out what you're talking "
"about, see you later."
msgstr "이해하다가 시간 다 가겠네. 나중에 봐."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Maybe, but where's the fun in that?  Besides, quoting poetry is one
#. thing, but changing the way I speak all the time takes a lot of practice.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Mayhap, but where'd be the fun in that?  Asides, quoth poetry is one thing, "
"but changin' this'n's whole yark for always takes a lot o' practice."
msgstr ""
"어쩌면 그럴 수도 있겠지만, 그게 무슨 재미가 있겠어? 덧붙이자면, 시를 쓰는 건 괜찮지만, 이 모든 걸 바꾸는 건 항상 엄청난 연습이 "
"필요하잖아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What was it you were saying before, about the mission you had for me?"
msgstr "다시 일 얘기로 돌아가자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Well, a person can get sick of trying to piece it together.  "
"<end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "글쎄요, 사람들은 그것을 조각조각 맞춰보려고 노력하는 데 지칠 수 있죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Right.  You see, it's when two compatible people randomly happen into
#. each other and take a liking to one another.  It's a bit of Anglic slang.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Aye.  Ye kennit, when two of a sort happen upon each other as per chance, "
"an' find a liking to another?  'Tis a bit o' Anglic yark."
msgstr "네. 그렇죠, 우연히 같은 두 사람이 만나서 서로에게 호감을 느끼는 거요? 영국식 농담이죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's what I thought it meant, just… nevermind.  What were you saying"
" about the job?"
msgstr "에, 무슨 말인지는 알았지만, 그… 아니다. 다시 일 얘기로 돌아가자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I don't know what kind of game you're playing, but I'm out for a bit."
msgstr "말 장난 할 시간 없어. 나중에 봐."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That takes me way back.  That's a bit of the old King's Landing right
#. there, you know, calling back from when I was just little.  It… ah, it's
#. really hard for me to think about those old days.  Maybe another time.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"*seems to become wistful for a moment.  \"Harks this'n yonder, right so.  "
"'Tis a bit o' t'ol' King's Landing right there, kennit, yarkin' from back "
"when Rubik were nigh smaller than a kelpie.  It…\"  Rubik's gravelly voice "
"falters.  \"Ah, 'tis mightily tassed to hearken back yonder.  Mayhap another"
" time.\""
msgstr ""
"*잠시 그리워하는 듯하다. \"저기, 저기 떠드는 소리, 맞아. 저기 킹스랜딩이 좀 오래된 곳이야, 케닛. 루빅이 켈피보다 훨씬 작았던 "
"시절 이야기지. 그게…\" 루빅의 거친 목소리가 떨렸다. \"아, 저기 떠드는 소리가 너무 듣기 좋네. 다음에 또 들릴지도 몰라.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Maybe later then.  What were you saying about the job?"
msgstr "그러면 나중에 얘기하자. 나한테 일거리가 있다고 했지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "You know, I think it'd be best if I just got going."
msgstr "어, 그러면 난 이제 가볼게."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Making do, making do, same as you I'd imagine.  Our last home got too
#. dead and putrid around the edges, basically.  It happens to the best of
#. them.  We caught some news that brought us along to your place here, fired
#. up the engines, and boom!  Now, quick as can be, here we are.  We got a
#. good timing this time, seems to me you'd only been dead a few days when we
#. got here.  Freshest corpse I've seen in a while.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Makin' do, makin' do, same as you, an I'm ken.  Last home got a bit too dead"
" 'n putrid roun' the edges, like.  Happens to the best of 'em.  Caught a "
"jibber that made us ken 'bout your place here, fired up the ol' wibble-"
"wammles and boom!  Now it's all tick-tock on a zimmer, here we be.  Got a "
"good timing this time, I razz you only been dead a few days when we wobbled "
"in.  Freshest corpse this'n's seen in a kitchen sink."
msgstr ""
"해내, 해내, 너랑 똑같아, 나도 켄이야. 지난번 집은 너무 썩어서 주변이 썩었어. 뭐든 잘하는 집이니까. 걔네 집이 여기 있는 줄 알게"
" 된 거지. 낡은 위블웜을 켜니까 펑! 이제 똑딱똑딱 소리가 나. 여기 왔네. 이번엔 타이밍이 딱 좋았어. 우리가 비틀거리며 들어왔을 때"
" 네가 죽은 지 며칠밖에 안 됐다고. 부엌 싱크대에서 본 것 중 가장 신선한 시체지."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "…what?"
msgstr "…뭐?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[INT or PER 9] Where did you come from then?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[지능/지각 9] 그럼 넌 어디서 온거야? 너희들은 외계인 같은거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Is there anything else you want from this place?"
msgstr "여기에 왜 온거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We're just here to survive, you understand?  Our last world got too
#. overrun with undead.  So, we came to a new world.  This one.  If I'm not
#. mistaken, it's not so long dead around here just yet.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Us're here to live and breathe, kennit?  After our last otherland got a li'l"
" too dead an' all.  So, us'n came to a new place.  This'n.  An I'm ken, it's"
" not so long dead round here jus' yet."
msgstr ""
"우리는 여기서 살고 숨 쉬려고 온 거야, 켄닛? 지난번 다른 땅이 너무 죽어서 다 죽어버렸거든. 그래서 우리는 새로운 곳에 온 거야. "
"여기. 그리고 켄, 여기는 아직 죽은 지 오래되지 않았어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[INT or PER 7] Otherland?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[지능/지각 7] 저번 세계라니? 너희들은 외계인 같은거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Aside from just having a safe place to live?  We're here to mine, you
#. understand.  Picking the scraps, seeing if this world has any tech worth
#. reverse engineering.  No sense letting good scraps go to waste.  If we're
#. lucky, maybe we'll get some new Exodii before we teleport out.  Pickin' up
#. the pieces of our sweet, shattered dreams, such as they are.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Aside from jus' livin' in such a cozy nook?  Us be minin', ye kennit.  "
"Pickin' the scraps, seein' if for your otherland has any tech worth an "
"upside-down.  No sense lettin' good scraps go to waste.  If we're lucky, "
"pickin' a few new Exodii afore we wobble out.  Pickin' up the pieces of our "
"sweet, shattered dreams, suchlike."
msgstr ""
"Aside from jus' livin' in such a cozy nook?  Us be minin', ye kennit.  Pickin' the scraps, seein' if for your otherland has any tech worth an upside-down.  No sense lettin' good scraps go to waste.  If we’re lucky, pickin' a few new Exodii afore we wobble out.  Pickin' up the pieces of our sweet, shattered dreams, suchlike.\\\"\\\n"
"\\\n"
"[해석:] \\\"뜯어갈 게 있나 찾는거지. 잔해를 줍고, 이 세상에 역공학할 만한 기술이 있는지 살펴보는 거야. 낭비하는 건 질색이거든. 운이 좋으면 텔레포트해서 나가기 전에 새로운 일원들을 데려갈 수도 있겠지. 그렇게 해서 우리의 달콤한, 부서진 꿈의 조각들을 주워 모으는 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"What do you mean 'go to waste'?  The zombies aren't using the scrap, and "
"there's plenty to go around."
msgstr "낭비라니? 널린 게 물건이고, 좀비들은 물건을 쓸 줄도 모를텐데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is a deadland, don't you see?  You've already got an infestation and
#. it's not going away.  There's no cure for the zombies.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"This'n be a deadland, an I'm ken.  You gots you a case o' the willies ain't "
"gonna sing along.  No cure for these rats and fleas."
msgstr ""
"여긴 죽음의 땅이 될 거야, 나도 알아. 네가 가진 건 으스스한 냄새 때문에 따라 부르지도 못할 거야. 쥐랑 벼룩은 치료법이 없어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "What the hell does that mean?"
msgstr "그게 도대체 무슨 말이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"[INT 8] Are you saying you think we're doomed?  Why would you have come here"
" if there wasn't some way to survive?"
msgstr "[지능 8] 정해진 운명이라고? 그러면 왜 여기로 온거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It means what it means.  Your land's dead already, it's just still
#. kicking is all.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Means what it means.  Your land's a deadun', still kickin' is all."
msgstr "그게 무슨 뜻인지 알겠지. 네 땅은 죽어가고 있고, 그저 여전히 살아있을 뿐이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Are you saying you think we're doomed?  Why would you have come here if "
"there wasn't some way to survive?"
msgstr "우리 모두 다 끝장이라는 거야? 그러면 왜 여기로 온거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, we can teleport along as we need to.  We send the scrap along, then
#. the food, and shake off some baddies, you understand.  It's no good for you
#. though, it won't take too much flesh and bone.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Oh, us can wobble along as needs.  Sends the scrap back, brings in the "
"foods, and shakes off a willie or three, kennit.  No good for you, won't "
"take too much meat-an'-bone."
msgstr ""
"오, 우리는 필요에 따라 비틀거리며 나아갈 수 있어. 찌꺼기는 돌려보내고, 음식은 가져오고, 괜히 쑤셔넣고, 케닛. 너한테는 안 돼, "
"뼈랑 살이 너무 많이 들어가니까."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Well… could you help me fix that?"
msgstr "흠… 사이보그가 되면 문제가 없지 않을까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Wait.  I thought you were still flesh and bone, under that metal."
msgstr "잠깐만, 너도 어떻게 보면 뼈와 살이 있지 않아? 겉이 철로 된 것 뿐이지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Haha, not mostly, mate.  It's not worth risking the side effects, you
#. see?  I keep the parts of me that make me Rubik, but the rest is all solid.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Haha, not mostly, mate.  Not worth riskin' the willies, innit?  I keep "
"what's Rubik, but the rest is all solid."
msgstr "하하, 대부분 그렇지 않아, 친구. 괜히 겁먹을 필요는 없잖아, 안 그래? 루빅큐브는 갖고 있지만 나머지는 다 괜찮아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"What?  I mean, really, it seems like you're being hard to understand on "
"purpose.  What are the 'willies'?"
msgstr "뭐? 아니, 너가 말하는 걸 보면 일부러 이해하기 힘들게 하는 것 같아. 부작용을 감수하다니?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, sure, that's a fair assessment.  I mean, I do get a bit of a laugh
#. out of the look on your face sometimes.  What I'm saying is, if my body
#. were flesh and bone, the device we use to travel around dimensions would
#. rip up the meat and leave me quite a mess.  We can take a bit, but too
#. much… one time, I felt a bit of that, and I'm not in any rush to try it
#. again.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Oh, sure an it's bagged in a coffer an' all that.  That is t'say, this'n "
"does get a wipe o' a grinny t'see the perplexion upon a visage, an I'm ken.*"
"  You're pretty sure you hear a faint chuckle in the metallic voice.  *What "
"I be meanin' is at, for my body were t'be meat-an'-bone, the tool what we be"
" usin' for t'travel to an' fro, it rips up the meat an' leaves it a right "
"mess.  A bit can come along for a right fun, but too much… on a time, an "
"earlier Rubik felt a spot o' those willies, an' this'n be not in the "
"farrier's hut for t'try it again."
msgstr ""
"아, 물론이고 금고에 봉지에 넣어서 그런 거요. 그러니까, 이건 얼굴에 나타난 당혹감을 보고 웃음이 터져 나오는 거고, 저는 알아요.* "
"금속성 목소리에서 희미한 웃음소리가 들리는 게 분명해요.* 제가 말하고 싶은 건, 제 몸이 뼈와 살덩어리, 즉 우리가 이리저리 여행할 때"
" 쓰는 도구라면, 살덩어리를 찢어서 엉망으로 만든다는 거예요. 재밌게 놀려면 조금은 따라올 수 있겠지만, 너무 많은 걸… 예전에 루빅이 "
"그 녀석들의 곤경을 느꼈던 적이 있는데, 이건 말발굽장이 오두막에서 다시 시도할 일이 아니죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"What?  I mean, really, it seems like you're being hard to understand on "
"purpose."
msgstr "뭐? 아니, 너가 말하는 걸 보면 일부러 이해하기 힘들게 하는 것 같아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Not to me it doesn't.  We didn't get it from around here though.  I bet
#. it looks pretty nice to you.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Not to me it don't.  We ain't tassed from around here though.  Looks fine "
"an' fine to you I'd razz."
msgstr "내 생각엔 그렇지 않아. 하지만 이 근처에서는 냄새를 맡지 않았어. 너한테는 괜찮아 보이고, 내가 욕할 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "[INT or PER 7] Not from around here?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[지능/지각 7] 여기 세계에서 얻은 게 아니라고? 너희들은 외계인 같은거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ If you've got what I need, I'm happy to call ahead and make the
#. arrangements, for a fee.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"If'n you're full an' plenty, this'n's happy to make the call, for a shiny "
"farthing."
msgstr "만약 당신이 배불리 먹고 충분하다면, 빛나는 1파딩을 위해 기꺼이 전화를 걸겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I've got some stuff I'd like to install."
msgstr "바이오닉을 설치하고 싶어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Would you be able to take out one of my implants?"
msgstr "바이오닉을 제거해줄 수 있어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Mayhaps this gear will do you better than it did the scuffers wot trained "
"with it. [$400]"
msgstr "어쩌면 이 장비가 그것으로 훈련받은 스커퍼보다 더 나을지도 몰라요. [$400]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "I'll buy it."
msgstr "내가 사겠어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Any chance I can buy gear this on layaway?"
msgstr "이 장비를 할부로 살 수 있는 방법이 있을까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"If'n you survive, we can give you a fortnight and six odd days to pay us'n "
"back."
msgstr "만약 당신이 살아남는다면, 우리는 당신에게 2주 6일의 시간을 주어서 우리에게 돈을 갚게 할 수 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Thanks Rubik, I'll be back with your payment soon."
msgstr "루빅, 고맙습니다. 곧 결제를 진행하겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid ""
"Right and done, don't let whatever you are going after turn you into a pork "
"loin well done.  I's expectin' you back."
msgstr "좋아, 됐어. 네가 쫓는 게 뭐든 간에, 잘 익힌 돼지고기 등심으로 변하지 마. 다시 돌아올 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
msgid "Here's the money to pay off that debt."
msgstr "빚을 갚을 돈이 여기 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Sure an' I can make you a cyborg, here an' now, since you're a developer an'"
" all."
msgstr "디버깅 중이라고? 지금 당장 해줄게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "[Install CBM Interface] Let's do it."
msgstr "[CBM 인터페이스 설치] 시작해 보겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "I changed my mind.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "마음이 바뀌었어요. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "마음이 바뀌었어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh HO!  Well, now you're speaking my language.  We can fix you up good,
#. if you're willing to pay us back.  I'll say it as clearly as I can.  If you
#. help us kill the undead, we can help you get fixed up like us, yeah.  Stuck
#. right into your flesh and bone and wired into your brain.  You understand?
#. If not, we'll ask the Great Grey to help clear it up.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Oh HO!  Well, well.  Now you're yarkin' the King's Anglic.  Aye, us'n can "
"fix ye good, if'n ye're tassed to repay it in kind.  Us'll speak it as "
"clear-like as this Rubik can.  If ye'n use it to put the dead back in the "
"ground, us'n can fix ye with some goods like this, aye.  Stuck in the flesh "
"and to the bone, wired into the brain.  Ye kennit?  If no, us'll speak to "
"the Great Grey for a pint o' the ol' clarity-draught."
msgstr ""
"오호! 뭐, 뭐. 이제 킹스 앵글릭을 들고 다니시네. 그래, 우리가 네놈들을 고칠 수 있어. 네가 그 대가를 치르도록 노력한다면 말이지."
" 이 루빅큐브처럼 또박또박 말할 수 있을 거야. 이걸로 죽은 놈들을 땅속에 묻어 버린다면, 이런 좋은 걸로 고칠 수 있을 거야. 살과 "
"뼈에 꽂힌 채 뇌에 꽂힌 채로 말이지. 알겠나? 모르면 그레이트 그레이한테 가서 그 옛날 맑은 생맥주 한 파인트 사오도록 하지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, well.  I'll file that away, so to speak.  Maybe you could bring us a
#. little more trade, and we'll fix you up as soon as possible.  The Exodii
#. won't turn away a willing convert.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Ah, well.  Us'll put that into the key and lock, if'n you're ken.  Mayhap "
"you could bring us a mite and trade, and we'll see if we can fix you good "
"soon and soon.  Let no Exodii turn away a willin' Benny, and so it is."
msgstr ""
"아, 뭐. 네가 알면 열쇠랑 자물쇠에 넣어줄게. 혹시 돈 좀 가져와서 교환해 줄 수 있다면, 곧 고쳐줄 수 있을지 알아보자. 어떤 "
"엑소다이도 베니의 부탁을 거절할 순 없지. 그렇게 될 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"If I just keep on killing zombies, you'll help turn me into a cyborg?  Why "
"are we still yarkin', then?  Sign me the heck up."
msgstr "좀비만 계속 죽이면 사이보그로 만들어 주겠다고? 두말할 것 없지, 당장 하자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"On second thought, I'm not sure I want to let a bunch of unfamiliar alien "
"robots do brain surgery on me."
msgstr "어, 다시 생각해보니 외계 사이보그들한테 내 뇌를 만지게 하고 싶진 않네."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "Maybe try that clarity-draught?"
msgstr "그레이… 어쩌구가 대신 답해줬으면 해. 이해가 안돼."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "OK, well, I've got some stuff I could trade right now."
msgstr "지금 거래하자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "OK, maybe I'll come back when I've traded a bit more."
msgstr "알았어. 그럼 나중에 다시 얘기해보자고."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Hmm.\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik's voice becomes mechanical and distant for a moment, as if a computer takes over speaking.*\n"
"\n"
"In exchange for the guarantee that you will use these gifts to combat the Great Enemy, this Exodii Node is willing to provide you with a bionic module command plexus, a power supply, and all the necessary infrastructure to obtain further upgrades with standardized CBMs - compact bionic modules.  We will require only a token fee for this service.  We will provide further upgrades as purchased.  Your personal improvement serves our mutual benefit.\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik's voice takes over again.*\n"
"\n"
"Clear as a draught?"
msgstr ""
"흐음.\n"
"\n"
"*갑자기 컴퓨터가 루빅을 조종하듯 루빅의 목소리가 어색하고 기계적으로 변합니다.\n"
"\n"
"위대한 적과의 전투에 이를 사용하는 것을 보장한다면, 우리 엑소다이는 바이오닉 모듈 커맨드 플렉서스, 전원 공급장치 및 표준 바이오닉으로 추가 업그레이드를 위한 모든 필수 인프라를 제공할 준비가 되어 있습니다. 우리는 이 서비스에 대한 상징적인 수수료만 필요로 할 것입니다. 추가 업그레이드는 구매한 대로 제공될 것입니다. 당신의 발전은 우리의 상호 이익을 위해 봉사합니다.\n"
"\n"
"*루빅의 목소리가 다시 돌아옵니다.*\n"
"\n"
"Clear as a draught? (이해했어?)"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Why can't you talk that clearly all the time?  You have no idea how hard it "
"is to understand your accent, let alone your words."
msgstr "그렇게 명확하게 얘기 할 수 있는데 왜 그러는거야? 네가 말하는거 이해하기 진짜 힘들어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ MY accent?  You've obviously never had to listen to yourself talk.  Great
#. Grey has more important work to do, get it?  I have to keep myself useful
#. and keep Great Grey doing what it's supposed to.  Besides, talking to the
#. locals keeps me young and shines my chrome, as I see it.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"THIS'n's accent?  Ye've never egged y'r own yark, an' that's a fine fiddle."
"  Great Grey has a bit o' work on it, kennit?  This'n has to keep usselves "
"useful, an' keep Great Grey doin' what it's tassed.  Asides, yarkin' to the "
"local brights keeps us young an' shines our chrome, an I'm ken."
msgstr ""
"이게 악센트라고? 자기네 야크에 계란 뿌린 적 없잖아, 그거 진짜 좋은 놈이지. 그레이트 그레이도 좀 썼잖아, 안 그래? 이게 우리 "
"스스로 쓸모 있게 지내야 하고, 그레이트 그레이도 자기 할 일을 해야지. 덧붙이자면, 동네 명문가에 가서 야크하면 젊음도 지키고, 우리도"
" 빛나잖아, 나도 알아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Fine, whatever.  It doesn't matter, if you're gonna turn me into a "
"horrifying fusion of machine and human, sign me the heck up."
msgstr "됐다, 상관 없어. 이 흉측한 허물을 벗고 더 흉측한 기계로 만들 수 있다면 당연히 하겠어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"The more I talk to you, the more I'm not sure I want to let a bunch of "
"unfamiliar alien robots do brain surgery on me."
msgstr "너랑 얘기할수록 외계 사이보그들한테 내 뇌를 맡길 마음이 싹 사라져."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "OK, OK.  What was it you said?  I was distracted by the voice change."
msgstr "알았어, 알았어. 뭐라고 했었지? 갑자기 목소리가 바뀌어서 약간 넋이 나갔었어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  Your job
#. is to bring us a bit of good tea.  Not literally 'tea' of course.  That's
#. my Anglic street slang.  I mean the stuff that puts you to sleep for
#. surgery.  The Great Grey says your word for it is 'anesthetic'.  You bring
#. us a thousand units of anesthetic, we'll fix you up with a wire and
#. everything.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine, an' fine an' fine!  Ha!  Us'll rubber up the ol' gristle "
"mill.  Yer tassed wi' bringin' us a nip o' good tea.  Not 'tea', o'course.  "
"I'm yarkin dockside Anglic here.  Us means the stuff what puts y'to sleep "
"f'r a chirurgery.  The Great Grey says y'r assert for it is 'anus fetick'.  "
"You bring us a thousand unit of 'anus fetick', us'll fix'n ye up with a wire"
" an' a tiff."
msgstr ""
"좋아, 좋아, 좋아, 좋아! 하! 우리가 그 오래된 연골 공장을 고무로 만들어 줄 거야. 좋은 차 한 모금 가져다주겠다고 했잖아. 물론 "
"'차'는 아니야. 난 여기서 부두에서 영국인이야. '우리'는 수술 때문에 졸리게 만드는 그런 걸 말하는 거야. 그레이트 그레이는 네가 "
"주장한다고 해. '항문 페틱'이라고. 네가 '항문 페틱' 천 개를 가져오면, 우리가 철사랑 티프(tiff)로 해결해 줄 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"One thousand units of, uh, anesthetic, coming up.  "
"<done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "마취제 1,000유닛이 곧 도착합니다. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"One thousand units of, uh, anesthetic, coming up.  I'd better start looking."
msgstr "어, 마취제… 곧 대령하겠사옵니다. 난 찾으러 가볼게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Something's weird, I shouldn't have ever reached this dialogue option.  I'd "
"better go file a bug report."
msgstr "뭔가 이상하네요. 이 대화 상자에 들어가면 안 되는 거였어요. 버그 신고하는 게 나을 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  You just
#. come along with old Rubik.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine, an' fine an' fine!  Ha!  Now as us've got the good tea, us'll"
" rubber up the ol' gristle mill.  You jus' set along with ol' Rubik."
msgstr ""
"좋아, 좋아, 좋아, 좋아! 하! 이제 좋은 차가 있으니, 그 오래된 연골 분쇄기를 고무로 만들어 볼까. 넌 그냥 오래된 루빅이랑 같이 "
"해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "[Install CBM Interface] All right.  Let's do this."
msgstr "[CBM 인터페이스 설치] 좋습니다. 시작해 볼까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "Hold on.  I need to rethink it again."
msgstr "잠깐만, 한번 더 고민해봐야겠어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's a fine choice, I understand.  If you change your mind, old Rubik's
#. going to be here for a while.  You'll get to know us better, we'll get to
#. know you better, and that's going to be good all around.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"An' that's a fine choice, I'd razz.  If'n ye change mind, ol' Rubik's here "
"for the long an' short.  You get to know us'n better, us'n get to know you "
"better, an' that's a good tassin'."
msgstr ""
"그리고 그건 좋은 선택이야, 내가 욕할게. 만약 네가 마음이 바뀌면, 늙은 루빅이 여기 있어. 넌 우리를 더 잘 알게 될 거고, 우리는 "
"널 더 잘 알게 될 거야. 좋은 경험이지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"*makes a stiff, bowing gesture and leads you out of the shop and down a stone pathway towards one of the larger buildings in the compound.  A thick steel door slides aside to reveal a gloomy, rust-dusted corridor.  At the end of the corridor is a clean appearing surgical suite, not too different from any other surgical suite aside from the dim lighting and the surgeon itself.  At the head of the surgical table is a contraption reminiscent of an upside-down spider, its multiple glistening medical limbs curling gently in eager anticipation of your approach.  You have little time to question your choices before you feel a sharp pinch in your left shoulder, and the world drifts away.\n"
"\n"
"You awaken on a comfortable bed, your chest and throat sore but otherwise well.  As the haze of anesthesia fades, you notice several tiny, sore wounds on your chest and arms.  A humanoid cyborg, not Rubik, notices that you are awake and wordlessly gestures you to follow, leading you back to Rubik's store.\n"
"\n"
"\"Ah, an' you're with the stars 'n lights again, an I'm ken.  'Tis grand.  Those wee CBMs will do ye little an fine, but they are a start.  Now us'n can sell you all you like, an' help with install, should ye wish.\""
msgstr ""
"*뻣뻣하게 고개를 숙이는 듯한 몸짓을 하며 당신을 수술실 밖으로 이끌고 나와 돌길을 따라 건물 안의 큰 건물 중 하나로 향합니다. 두꺼운 철문이 열리자 어둡고 녹슨 복도가 드러납니다. 복도 끝에는 깨끗해 보이는 수술실이 있는데, 어둑한 조명과 외과 의사를 제외하면 다른 수술실과 크게 다르지 않습니다. 수술대 머리맡에는 거꾸로 된 거미를 연상시키는 장치가 놓여 있는데, 반짝이는 여러 개의 의료용 팔다리가 당신의 접근을 간절히 기다리는 듯 부드럽게 말려 있습니다. 당신은 선택에 대해 고민할 틈도 없이 왼쪽 어깨에 날카로운 조임이 느껴지고, 세상은 멀어져 갑니다.\n"
"\n"
"당신은 편안한 침대에서 깨어났습니다. 가슴과 목이 뻐근했지만 그 외에는 괜찮았습니다. 마취의 안개가 걷히자 가슴과 팔에 작고 아픈 상처들이 여러 개 있는 것을 발견했습니다. 루빅이 아닌 인간형 사이보그가 당신이 깨어 있는 것을 알아채고는 말없이 따라오라고 손짓하며 루빅의 가게로 데려갑니다.\n"
"\n"
"\"아, 그리고 당신은 다시 별과 빛과 함께 있고, 저는 켄입니다. 정말 멋지네요. 저 작은 CBM들은 당신에게 별로 도움이 되지 않겠지만, 시작일 뿐입니다. 이제 우리는 당신이 원하는 모든 것을 판매할 수 있고, 원한다면 설치도 도울 수 있습니다.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "So I'm a cyborg now?  I don't really feel much different."
msgstr "나도 이제 사이보그야? 별 차이가 느껴지지는 않는데."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Thanks for the brain implants.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "<end_talking_leave> 뇌 이식 수술에 감사드립니다. <end_talking_bye>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is what you'd call a 'starter package', if I understand it.
#. Suitable to get you started, but for the really sweet parts you're going to
#. want what I'm selling.  As we get to know each other better, I'll be able
#. to get access to even more stuff.
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"This're what ye'd razz a 'starter package', an I'm ken.  Tassed to get ye "
"started, but for the real lemony tarts you'd be wantin' what this'n's got "
"for sale.  As us'n can come to see you clairly-like, this'n can be tassed to"
" offer more an' more."
msgstr ""
"이게 바로 '스타터 패키지'라고 할 만한 거고, 나도 알아. 시작은 맛있지만, 진짜 레몬 타르트를 원한다면 여기 있는 걸 사야 할 거야."
" 우리가 당신을 보러 와서 똑똑하게 볼 수 있으니까, 여기 가서 맛보면 더 많은 걸 제공할 수 있어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
msgid ""
"So you can sell me more bionics, and as I get to know you better you'll have"
" more?  Mind showing me what you've got right now?"
msgstr "그 말은 내가 너와 신뢰를 쌓으면, 더 좋은 물건을 주겠다는 거지? 지금 뭘 팔고 있는지 보여줘."

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
msgid "Nine"
msgstr "아홉"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
msgid "Weaponmaster"
msgstr "무기 마스터"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
msgid "Cyborg, type 9"
msgstr "사이보그, 9형"

#. ~ Mutation name
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
msgid "Exodii cyborg framework - style 9"
msgstr "엑소다이 사이보그 프레임워크 - 스타일 9"

#. ~ Description of mutation "Exodii cyborg framework - style 9"
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
msgid ""
"Your entire body is covered by a rectangular frame, that has numerous "
"supporting arms and manipulators, with decent stability.  The price of this "
"is that the weight of the entire frame is enormous, which causes the user to"
" either use dedicated tracked treads to move around, or stay immobile for a "
"large amount of time."
msgstr ""
"몸 전체는 직사각형 프레임으로 덮여 있으며, 이 프레임에는 여러 개의 지지대와 조종 장치가 있어 안정적인 자세를 유지합니다. 하지만 "
"프레임 전체의 무게가 엄청나게 나가기 때문에 사용자는 전용 트랙을 사용하거나 장시간 움직이지 않고 있어야 합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&What you see looks like the back of a mechanical spider, with at least a "
"dozen crude but polished metal arms coming from the enormously wide spine "
"and shoulders.  The spine of the creature, meanwhile, sits in an awkward-"
"looking chair, manipulating tools and geegaws on a wide, brightly lit "
"workbench.  The creature seems to be busy with something."
msgstr ""
"&당신이 보는 것은 기계 거미의 등처럼 보입니다. 엄청나게 넓은 척추와 어깨에서 적어도 열두 개는 되는 투박하지만 윤이 나는 금속 팔이 "
"뻗어 있습니다. 한편, 그 생물의 척추는 어색해 보이는 의자에 앉아 넓고 밝은 작업대에서 도구와 장난감을 다루고 있습니다. 그 생물은 "
"무언가에 열중하는 듯합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "[Wait a bit.]"
msgstr "[잠깐만요.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "&It doesn't react to your presence at all."
msgstr "&그것은 당신이 존재하는 데 전혀 반응하지 않습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "[Wait for longer.]"
msgstr "[더 기다려 보세요.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "&It seems to not hear you at all."
msgstr "&전혀 당신의 말을 듣지 못하는 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "[Wait in silence.]"
msgstr "[조용히 기다리세요.]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "Hello!?"
msgstr "안녕하세요!?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&A few seconds later, they seem to finish whatever they were busy with and "
"turn their chair towards you.  Their front looks no less exotic than their "
"back; the abundance of metal arms are even more extraordinary next to the "
"clear lack of any legs.  What you initially thought to be a chair is simply "
"a rotating platform, sturdy enough to support the weight of the entire body "
"of the creature.  A number of cameras, which seem to be a replacement for "
"eyes, look at you motionlessly, while the forehead of the creature has the "
"surprisingly familiar sign \"IX\" painted on."
msgstr ""
"몇 초 후, 그들은 하던 일을 끝내고 의자를 당신 쪽으로 돌립니다. 앞모습도 등받이만큼이나 이국적으로 보입니다. 다리가 없는 모습에 비해"
" 금속 팔걸이가 훨씬 더 특이합니다. 처음에는 의자라고 생각했던 것은 그저 회전하는 플랫폼일 뿐인데, 생물의 온몸 무게를 지탱할 만큼 "
"튼튼합니다. 눈을 대체한 듯한 여러 대의 카메라가 당신을 미동도 없이 바라보고 있고, 생물의 이마에는 놀랍게도 익숙한 \"IX\"라는 "
"글자가 그려져 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "Who-…  Wha-…  What are you?"
msgstr "누구-… 뭐-… 너는 뭐야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&Still completely mute, it shows you something you had initially missed.  "
"The entire wall behind the workbench is full of various weapons; some as big"
" as modern rifles, a few as large as the machine guns installed on aircraft,"
" and one that looks like a dismantled tank turret.  Melee weapons were not "
"forgotten, from moderately-sized swords and clubs to war hammers twice the "
"height of a human, and what you can describe only as \"boots for mecha\".  "
"Then it points to a sign near you that shows three things: the carved "
"pictograms of coins, some sign you are not familiar with, and a pictogram of"
" a bullet - all things considered, this creature is either a weaponmaster, "
"or a weapon merchant."
msgstr ""
"&아직 완전히 침묵한 채, 그것은 당신이 처음에 놓쳤던 무언가를 보여줍니다. 작업대 뒤편 벽 전체는 다양한 무기로 가득 차 있습니다. "
"어떤 것은 현대식 소총만큼 크고, 어떤 것은 항공기에 장착된 기관총만큼 크고, 어떤 것은 해체된 전차 포탑처럼 보입니다. 근접 무기도 "
"잊지 않았습니다. 적당한 크기의 검과 곤봉부터 사람 키의 두 배는 되는 전쟁 망치, 그리고 \"메카용 부츠\"라고밖에 표현할 수 없는 "
"것까지. 그리고 그것은 당신 근처의 표지판을 가리킵니다. 동전 모양의 조각상, 낯선 표지판, 그리고 총알 모양의 그림입니다. 이 모든 "
"것을 고려해 볼 때, 이 생물은 무기 장인이거나 무기 상인입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "Woah.  Can I buy one?"
msgstr "와. 하나 살 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "&They do not move and do not say anything."
msgstr "&그들은 움직이지 않고 아무 말도 하지 않습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid "Hey?  Do you understand me?"
msgstr "야? 내 말 이해해?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&They clearly do not understand you.  It seems they do not hear you either."
msgstr "& 그들은 분명히 당신을 이해하지 못하는 것 같습니다. 당신 말도 듣지 못하는 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"[You pull off your backpack, and start to pull out items you deem worthy of "
"trading.  The weaponmaster finally looks interested.]"
msgstr ""
"[당신은 배낭을 벗어 던지고, 거래할 가치가 있다고 생각되는 물건들을 꺼내기 시작합니다. 무기 전문가가 마침내 관심을 보이는 듯합니다.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be tinkering on something, but turns their chair "
"to you as you approach."
msgstr "&무기 마스터는 무언가를 손보고 있는 듯하지만, 당신이 다가가자 의자를 당신에게 돌립니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be cleaning some sort of weapon, but as you "
"approach them, they signal to a bystanding worker to take the weapon, and "
"turn to you."
msgstr ""
"무기 전문가는 어떤 무기를 청소하는 듯하지만, 그들에게 다가가자 그들은 주변에 있던 작업자에게 무기를 가져가라는 신호를 보내고 당신에게 "
"돌아선다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be polishing some armor, but they turn towards "
"you the second you enter the room."
msgstr "&무기 마스터가 방어구를 닦고 있는 듯하지만, 방에 들어서자마자 그들은 당신을 향해 돌아선다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
msgid ""
"[With a familiar movement, you place a variety of valuables onto the "
"counter, proposing a trade.]"
msgstr "[익숙한 동작으로 다양한 귀중품을 카운터 위에 올려놓고 거래를 제안합니다.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&You see a human-like robot walking nearby."
msgstr "&사람 형태의 로봇이 걷고 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&You see a mechanical humanoid moving somewhere in a hurry."
msgstr "&바쁘게 움직이고 있는 사이보그가 보입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&You see some sort of robot walking in a hurry."
msgstr "&바쁘게 일하는 로봇이 보입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&This robot doesn't seem to be very busy."
msgstr "&한가해 보이는 로봇입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "[Move away.]"
msgstr "[자리를 떠난다.]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&They seem to completely ignore you."
msgstr "&당신을 완전히 무시하고 있는 듯 합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&They ran past you, completely ignoring your presence."
msgstr "&당신을 완전히 무시하듯 당신 옆을 달려가며 지나칩니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&They don't seem to want to talk to you."
msgstr "&당신과 이야기하고 싶지 않은 것 같습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "&They seem to greet you, but that's it."
msgstr "&당신에게 눈길로 인사를 주는 듯 합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
msgid "How rude."
msgstr "무례하기 짝이 없네."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
msgid "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgstr "표지판의 그림 문자가 가르키는 곳으로 가기"

#. ~ Description of mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
msgid ""
"I found a weird pictographic sign that seemed to point towards someone "
"willing to trade."
msgstr "거래를 표현한 그림 문자가 적힌 표지판에 무슨 지도같은 게 그려져 있었다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
msgid ""
"This is a sign with a series of simple line-art pictograms showing what "
"appears to be a basic trade transaction.  A pair of hands offers a piece of "
"some kind of junk, and another pair of hands offers a small pouch in return."
msgstr ""
"거래하는 모습을 표현하는 듯한 그림이 그려진 표지판입니다. 한 쪽에는 무언가 고물을 건네는 손이, 다른 한쪽에는 작은 주머니를 건네는 "
"손이 그려져 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"[v0.1 info] Okay I'm just gonna drop my dialect for this, it's way too much for Anglic.  The Labyrinthine Structure (LS) is planned to be a sprawling procedurally generated dungeon where you can fight advanced monsters and loot cybernetics, both regular and weird artifact versions.  It is currently far from that state.  Playtest information on the general layout and the monster balance would be helpful.\n"
"\n"
"In the long run, the goal is to have a number of 'biomes' that you can reach as you travel further from the origin point.  When you leave and return, the dungeon resets, although in the future the devs want to have a stable 'home base' you can upgrade.\n"
"\n"
"In its final form, if it ever gets there, it would have enough content that you could spend an entire playthrough just exploring the labyrinth and getting weird unique items that only work down there, something like the backrooms mod but for mainline."
msgstr ""
"[v0.1 정보] 음, 제 방언은 여기서 그만 쓰겠습니다. Anglic에는 너무 과해서요. 미궁 구조물(LS)은 광활한 절차적 생성 던전으로, 고급 몬스터와 싸우고 사이버네틱스(일반 유물과 기괴한 유물 모두)를 전리품으로 얻을 수 있습니다. 현재는 그런 상태와는 거리가 멉니다. 전반적인 구조와 몬스터 밸런스에 대한 플레이테스트 정보가 도움이 될 것입니다.\n"
"\n"
"장기적으로는 원점에서 더 멀리 이동할수록 도달할 수 있는 다양한 '생물 군계'를 만드는 것이 목표입니다. 던전을 나가고 돌아오면 던전이 초기화되지만, 개발진은 향후 업그레이드할 수 있는 안정적인 '거점'을 만들고 싶어 합니다.\n"
"\n"
"최종적으로는 미궁을 탐험하고 그 아래에서만 사용할 수 있는 기묘한 고유 아이템을 얻는 데만 플레이스루 전체를 사용할 수 있을 만큼 충분한 콘텐츠가 포함될 것입니다. 메인 라인용 백룸 모드와 비슷한 것이죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Let's stop breaking the fourth wall and get back to the normal conversation."
msgstr "네 번째 벽을 깨는 것은 그만두고 정상적인 대화로 돌아가자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&You see a strangely mundane black computer screen, with a blinking green cursor awaiting input.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"& 입력을 기다리는 녹색 커서가 깜빡이는, 이상하리만치 평범한 검은색 컴퓨터 화면이 보입니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Activate exit protocol"
msgstr "종료 프로토콜 활성화"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > skill -EXIT -@User\n"
"<color_light_green>Really exit?  You will not be able to return to the same place."
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > 스킬 -EXIT -@User\n"
"<color_light_green>정말 나가시겠어요? 같은 장소로 돌아갈 수 없습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Unlock connected doors"
msgstr "연결된 문 잠금 해제"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Lock connected doors"
msgstr "연결된 문 잠금"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Now all the doors are *gone*, what the hell."
msgstr "이제 모든 문이 *사라졌는데*, 뭐 별거 아니죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors unlocked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Thank you for using TempleOS.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>명령이 수락되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>근처 문이 잠금 해제되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>TempleOS를 사용해 주셔서 감사합니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=lock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors locked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Warning: What is done cannot be undone.  This does not represent a return to how things were.  You can never go back.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=lock\n"
"<color_light_green>명령이 수락되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>근처 문이 잠겼습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>경고: 실행된 작업은 되돌릴 수 없습니다. 이는 이전 상태로 돌아가는 것을 의미하지 않습니다. 절대 이전 상태로 돌아갈 수 없습니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Bad command or file name.\n"
"<color_light_green>What is done cannot be undone.  Please see prior user warning.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>잘못된 명령 또는 파일 이름입니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>실행한 작업은 취소할 수 없습니다. 이전 사용자 경고를 참조하십시오.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "There must be some way to force the computer to do it."
msgstr "컴퓨터가 그렇게 하도록 강제할 방법이 있을 겁니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock --force\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: Insufficient  confidence.\n"
"<color_light_green>Aborted: No forceable process.\n"
" @User > sudo doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Oh, is that how it will be?  Very well.\n"
"<color_light_green>Blood tax requested.\n"
"A drawer on the side of the terminal slides open, revealing a small, thin needle.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock --force\n"
"<color_light_green>오류: 신뢰도가 부족합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>중단됨: 강제 실행 가능한 프로세스가 없습니다.\n"
"@User > sudo doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>아, 그렇게 되는 건가요? 좋습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>혈세 요청합니다.\n"
"단말기 옆면의 서랍이 미끄러지듯 열리면서 작고 가느다란 바늘이 드러납니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "[ Prick yourself on the needle ]"
msgstr "[ 바늘에 찔리다 ]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&As it enters your skin, the thin needle seems to pulse, greedily gulping from your offered hand, and you feel abruptly dizzy and lightheaded.  It feels like it took a *lot* of blood.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > Inflict --damage=lifeblood\n"
"<color_light_green>Processing contribution of reality ||||||||| 100%\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors unlocked.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&피부에 꽂히자 가느다란 바늘이 맥박을 치며 내민 손에서 게걸스럽게 빨아들이는 듯했고, 갑자기 어지럽고 어지러움을 느꼈다. *엄청* 많은 피를 빨아들인 것 같았다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > --damage=lifeblood 적용\n"
"<color_light_green>현실 기여 처리 중 |||||||||| 100%\n"
"<color_light_green>근처 문 잠금 해제됨.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --list\n"
"<color_light_green>12 drwxr-xr-x 1 @User\n"
"<color_light_green>File lost or deleted.\n"
"<color_light_green>A new, stronger reality has supplanted the previous.  Thank you for using TempleOS.\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --list\n"
"<color_light_green>12 drwxr-xr-x 1 @User\n"
"<color_light_green>파일이 손실되었거나 삭제되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>새롭고 강력한 현실이 이전 현실을 대체했습니다. TempleOS를 사용해 주셔서 감사합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Enter the Thief's Passcode to extend the bridge."
msgstr "다리를 연장하려면 도둑의 비밀번호를 입력하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Enter the Circle of Wings Passcode to extend the bridge."
msgstr "다리를 연장하려면 Circle of Wings 패스코드를 입력하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Enter the Hard Nails Passcode to extend the bridge."
msgstr "브릿지를 연장하려면 하드 네일 패스코드를 입력하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Enter the Laughing Man Passcode to extend the bridge."
msgstr "다리를 연장하려면 웃는 남자 패스코드를 입력하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Try to extend the bridge to the treasure room."
msgstr "다리를 보물방까지 확장해보세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "Retract the bridge"
msgstr "브릿지를 수축하다"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid "[Computers] Try to find a way to force it."
msgstr "[컴퓨터] 강제로 실행할 방법을 찾아보세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: No PASSCODE or CONFIDENCE.\n"
"<color_light_green>If you have a PASSCODE, please enter using syntax --pass=\"your password\"\n"
"<color_light_green>If you have not been granted a PASSCODE, contact your system obelisk for help.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend\n"
"<color_light_green>오류: 비밀번호 또는 신뢰도가 없습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>비밀번호가 있는 경우 --pass=\"your password\" 구문을 사용하여 입력하세요.\n"
"<color_light_green>비밀번호가 부여되지 않은 경우 시스템 오벨리스크에 문의하여 도움을 받으세요.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode0>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Extending bridge.\n"
"<color_light_green>Watch your step.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode0>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>명령이 수락되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>브리지를 확장합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>발밑을 조심하세요.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode1>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Extending bridge.\n"
"<color_light_green>You are free.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode1>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>명령이 수락되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>브리지를 확장합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>자유입니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode2>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Extending bridge.\n"
"<color_light_green>Kick some ass.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode2>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>명령을 수락했습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>브리지를 확장합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>멋지게 해 보세요.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode3>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Extending bridge.\n"
"<color_light_green>Asshole.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=extend --pass=\"<ls_passcode3>\"\n"
"<color_light_green>명령 수락됨.\n"
"<color_light_green>브리지 확장 중.\n"
"<color_light_green>멍청이.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=retract\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: Insufficient confidence.\n"
"<color_light_green>What is done cannot be undone.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > bridge --update=retract\n"
"<color_light_green>오류: 신뢰도가 부족합니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>실행한 작업은 취소할 수 없습니다.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > help --retract\n"
"<color_light_green>Help?  @User help request logged.\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: \"Help\" - implied payment|cost detected.\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: Payment|cost not implemented.  Try again some day.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > help --retract\n"
"<color_light_green>도움이 필요하신가요? @User 도움 요청이 기록되었습니다.\n"
"<color_light_green>오류: \"도움말\" - 암묵적 결제|비용 감지됨.\n"
"<color_light_green>오류: 결제|비용이 구현되지 않았습니다. 나중에 다시 시도해 주세요.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ EOC option name in effect in EoC "EOC_XE_ED_RIDDLE_5"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/eocs/eoc_riddles.json
msgid "Leader"
msgstr "지도자"

#. ~ Job description of "Leader" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I am the leader of the New England Church Community."
msgstr "저는 뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체의 지도자입니다."

#. ~ Job description of "Guard" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I'm protecting stuff."
msgstr "저는 물건을 보호하고 있어요."

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "Member"
msgstr "회원"

#. ~ Job description of "Member" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Dorm leader" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Hunter" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Clergyman" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I am a member of the New England Church Community."
msgstr "저는 뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체의 일원입니다."

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "Joinee"
msgstr "참여자"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "Dorm leader"
msgstr "기숙사장"

#. ~ Refusal reason for a shop item group
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "<npcname> will never sell this"
msgstr "<npcname>(은)는 이 물품을 절대 팔지 않을 것입니다"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "Clergyman"
msgstr "성직자"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json data/json/npcs/godco/npcs.json
msgid "joinee"
msgstr "가입자"

#. ~ Job description of "Member" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I am a member of the group."
msgstr "나는 그 그룹의 일원이에요."

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/obsoletion_and_migration_0.I/obsolete_npc_class.json
msgid "Trader"
msgstr "상인"

#. ~ Job description of "Trader" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I'm collecting gear and selling it at a high interest."
msgstr "저는 장비를 수집해서 높은 이자로 판매하고 있습니다."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Picky Meals"
msgstr "절임의 날"

#. ~ Description of mission "Picky Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find 15 pounds (2000 units) of salt."
msgstr "소금 15파운드(2000단위)를 찾으세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need a supply of salt."
msgstr "소금이 필요해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I know this doesn't sound important, but I am running low on salt.  We don't"
" just need it as a seasoning, it's also vital for food preservation.  Could "
"you find about 15 pounds of salt for me?"
msgstr ""
"별로 중요한 얘기는 아니지만, 소금이 부족해요. 양념으로만 필요한 게 아니라 식품 보존에도 필수적이에요. 소금 7kg 정도 구해 "
"주시겠어요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In the absence of life"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Mi-go biology"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "Don't forget to tell me when you have them."
msgstr "가지고 돌아오면 나에게 말해주는 거 잊지마."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "It's okay, I can do without them.  Just let me know if you reconsider."
msgstr "괜찮아, 없으면 없는대로 살아야지 뭐. 혹시 생각 바뀌면 다시 이야기해줘."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"There's a lot of places to look.  They are common in house kitchens, "
"restaurants or grocery stores."
msgstr "찾을만한 곳은 많이 있을거야. 주택 주방, 레스토랑, 아니면 식료품점 같은 곳들에 흔해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "How is the search going?  Have you found 'em?"
msgstr "수색은 좀 어때? 뭔가 찾았어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"I really appreciate your help.  Don't worry, you won't leave empty-handed."
msgstr "정말 고마워. 걱정 마, 보답도 없이 내쫓지는 않을테니까."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Picky Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gallon Jugs"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Burnt Out CBMs"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "Don't worry about it, it's not that important."
msgstr "걱정하지마, 그렇게 중요한 거 아니야."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Pickled Meals"
msgstr "김장의 날"

#. ~ Description of mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find 40 glass jars (3 L)."
msgstr "유리병(3L) 40개를 찾으세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need several glass jars."
msgstr "유리병이 좀 필요해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"This task is bit more serious.  I don't have enough jars to preserve "
"perishables for the future, and we can't just store everything in salt.  We "
"could do our own canning if we had some more glass jars.  I think 40 jars "
"should be enough."
msgstr ""
"이 작업은 좀 더 심각해요. 상하기 쉬운 음식을 보관할 병이 부족하고, 모든 걸 소금에 그냥 보관할 수도 없잖아요. 유리병이 좀 더 "
"있다면 직접 통조림을 만들 수도 있을 것 같아요. 병 40개면 충분할 것 같아요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thanks for accepting this task.  It'll take a load off my shoulders.  I "
"finally won't have to worry about this problem anymore."
msgstr "도와주겠다니 고마워. 덕분에 짐을 좀 내려놓은 기분이야. 이제 이 일을 더 걱정하지 않아도 되겠어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bread"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "Just let me know if you change your mind."
msgstr "생각이 바뀌면 다시 말해줘."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Glass jars are not that hard to find.  I'd look for them in residential "
"areas."
msgstr "유리병은 구하기 어렵지 않아요. 주택가에서 찾아보세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Have you found the jars?"
msgstr "유리병은 찾았어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you for your help.  Here's your reward.  I have one more task to do."
msgstr "도와줘서 고마워. 여기 네 보상이야. 그리고 맡길 일이 하나 더 있는데…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pickled Meals"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bread"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "It's not a big deal, it isn't that urgent."
msgstr "별일 아니야, 그렇게 급하지 않아."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Prickled Meals"
msgstr "김장의 날"

#. ~ Description of mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find a butcher knife."
msgstr "푸주칼 찾기."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need something sharper."
msgstr "뭔가 날카로운 게 필요해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I don't have any butcher knives in here.  It's difficult to cut anything "
"hard without it.  It's good to have one, even though I won't use it that "
"often.  Could you get me one, or anything similarly suitable?"
msgstr ""
"여기 정육점 칼이 하나도 없어요. 정육점 칼이 없으면 딱딱한 건 자르기 힘들어요. 자주 쓸 일은 없겠지만 정육점 칼이 있으면 좋죠. 혹시"
" 정육점 칼이나 비슷한 거 구해 주실 수 있을까요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Thank you for accepting.  I can't cut anything with this dull knife."
msgstr "고마워. 칼이 너무 무뎌서 뭘 자를 수가 없거든."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I guess I have to cut them with my steak knife."
msgstr "내 스테이크 칼로 잘라야 할 것 같네."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Butcher knives are not that rare to find.  They are commonly found in "
"kitchens."
msgstr "푸주칼은 그렇게까지 귀하지는 않을 거야. 부엌에서 보통 찾을 수 있지."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Do you have that knife now?"
msgstr "칼은 가져왔어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Prickled Meals"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I am grateful for the help you've done."
msgstr "도와줘서 정말 고마워."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Busy While Working"
msgstr "일하는 동안 바쁘다"

#. ~ Description of mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find 3 mystery novels."
msgstr "추리소설을 3권 가져오세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'd like to read some mystery novels."
msgstr "추리소설이 필요해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Sometimes it gets a little bit boring up here, and I like to read something "
"to take my mind off of things.  Problem is, I've run out of books.  I've "
"been wanting to read some mystery novels as of late, so could you get me "
"three of them?"
msgstr ""
"가끔 여기 위가 좀 지루할 때가 있는데, 그럴 땐 뭔가를 읽고 생각을 정리하고 싶어. 그런데 문제는 책이 다 떨어졌다는 거야. 요즘 "
"미스터리 소설을 좀 읽고 싶은데, 세 권이나 구해 줄 수 있어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Just bring them to me when you have it."
msgstr "그것이 있으면 내게 가져오세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Nevermind then.  I hope you'll change your mind."
msgstr "신경쓰지 마. 혹시 생각 바뀌면 이야기해주고."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'd loot libraries and bookstores."
msgstr "나라면 도서관이나 서점을 찾아보겠어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "So, have you found the books?"
msgstr "그래서, 책은 가져왔어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you.  This will keep me busy for a while.  Please take this as a token"
" of my gratitude."
msgstr "고마워. 이제 한동안 지루하지는 않겠네. 별건 아니지만 내 성의표시야."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Could you give them to me?"
msgstr "나한테 줄 수 있어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Busy While Working"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Fine.  I can read something else."
msgstr "그래, 다른걸 읽지 뭐."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Canning Startup"
msgstr "캐닝 스타트업"

#. ~ Description of mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find 100 medium tin cans to can with."
msgstr "캔에 넣을 중간 크기의 깡통 100개를 찾으세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'd like to have some cans to store food in."
msgstr "음식을 보관할 캔이 좀 있으면 좋겠어요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Now that we have some canning pots from Helena, we can start storing "
"foodstuffs more easily around here.  Recycling our old tin cans is great and"
" all, but if we get a big influx of new foods, then we can't properly store "
"it all.  As such, if you could find about 100 more empty medium tin cans for"
" me, I'd really appreciate it."
msgstr ""
"헬레나에게서 캔닝 용기를 몇 개 구했으니 이제 우리 주변에 식품을 더 쉽게 보관할 수 있게 됐어요. 오래된 깡통을 재활용하는 건 좋지만,"
" 새로운 식품이 대량으로 유입되면 제대로 보관하기가 어려워지죠. 그래서 혹시 중간 크기 빈 깡통 100개 정도 더 구해 주시면 정말 "
"감사하겠습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Just bring it to me when you have it."
msgstr "얻게되거든 가져다줘."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I'd look anywhere there's food waste or scrap piles.  We can wash out the "
"cans when we get them."
msgstr "음식물 쓰레기나 고철 더미가 있는 곳이면 어디든 찾아볼게요. 캔이 오면 씻어서 버리면 되니까요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "So, have you found the cans?"
msgstr "그럼, 캔을 찾았나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you, now we won't have to worry about running out of food in the "
"winter."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 이제 겨울에 식량이 부족할까 봐 걱정할 필요가 없어졌습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Canning Startup"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Fine.  I'll get them myself."
msgstr "좋아요. 제가 직접 가져올게요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
msgstr "The Modern Trapper 사본을 찾으세요"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper so Eddie can learn how to lay traps."
msgstr "에디가 함정을 놓는 법을 배울 수 있도록 The Modern Trapper를 구하세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'd like to read some trapping guides."
msgstr "트래핑 가이드를 읽어보고 싶습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Since we've got all the stuff to store away food, I figure that it's time we"
" get some more.  I've been talking it over with Russell, and I think setting"
" out animal traps is a good way to go.  The problem is, nobody here knows "
"how to do it.  I've heard that The Modern Trapper is a good place to start, "
"so if you could get me a copy, I'd really appreciate it."
msgstr ""
"식량을 보관할 물건은 다 마련했으니, 이제 좀 더 사야 할 때라고 생각해요. 러셀이랑 얘기해 봤는데, 동물 덫을 놓는 게 좋은 방법인 것"
" 같아요. 문제는 여기 아무도 어떻게 하는지 모른다는 거예요. 'The Modern Trapper'라는 책이 좋은 시작점이라고 들었는데,"
" 혹시 한 권 구해 주시면 정말 감사하겠습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Too trivial for you?"
msgstr "너한테는 너무 사소한 일인가?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "So, have you found it?"
msgstr "그럼, 찾으셨나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Thank you, me and Russell will start studying it soon."
msgstr "감사합니다. 러셀과 저는 곧 공부를 시작하겠습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of The Modern Trapper"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Where is it?"
msgstr "어디에 있나요?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Store Up Your Grain"
msgstr "곡물을 저장하세요"

#. ~ Description of mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Find 5,398 pounds of sheet metal (408 units) to help Eddie build a "
"warehouse."
msgstr "에디가 창고를 짓는 데 도움이 될 5,398파운드의 판금(408개)을 구하세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'd like to have better food storage."
msgstr "더 나은 식량 저장 공간을 갖고 싶습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I've been drawing up some plans to expand our food storage around here.  Now"
" that we won't starve to death anytime soon, our old crates just aren't "
"cutting it, so we're going to build a small warehouse to store everything, "
"and I've gathered a crew to build it.  We've got most of the materials "
"covered, but we don't have enough sheet metal to make the shelves.  If you "
"could get us about 5,000 pounds of the stuff, I'll pay you handsomely with "
"what we have.  How does that sound?"
msgstr ""
"여기 식량 저장고를 확장할 계획을 세우고 있었어요. 이제 곧 굶어 죽지는 않을 것 같은데, 낡은 상자로는 도저히 버틸 수가 없어서 모든 "
"걸 보관할 작은 창고를 짓기로 했고, 작업반도 모집했어요. 자재는 대부분 확보했지만, 선반을 만들 판금이 부족해요. 5,000파운드(약 "
"2,227kg) 정도 구해 주시면, 지금 있는 걸로 두둑하게 드릴게요. 어떠세요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Alright, I'll find someone else."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 다른 사람을 찾아보겠습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "If you can find a steel mill, I'd look there."
msgstr "제철소를 찾을 수 있다면 거기로 가보세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the sheet metal?"
msgstr "금속판을 가지고 있나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I can't thank you enough, here's the pay for it.  Here in a while, we'll "
"have a spot to put all of our food."
msgstr "정말 고마워요. 여기 돈 좀 주세요. 곧 여기 우리 음식을 다 보관할 곳이 생길 거예요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Alright, where's it all at?"
msgstr "좋아요, 그게 다 어디에 있는 거죠?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Store Up Your Grain"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Sorry, I had to find someone else since you didn't come through."
msgstr "미안하지만, 당신이 오지 않아서 다른 사람을 찾아야 했어요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Obtain a guitar string"
msgstr "기타줄을 구하다"

#. ~ Description of mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find a length of tempered steel wire to be used as a guitar string."
msgstr "기타 줄로 사용할 강화 강철 와이어를 찾으세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need a new guitar string."
msgstr "새로운 기타줄이 필요해요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"One of my guitar strings busted from where I smacked a zombie.  If you could"
" get me a new string, I can fix my guitar."
msgstr "좀비를 때려서 기타 줄이 하나 끊어졌어. 새 줄을 구해 주시면 기타를 고칠 수 있을 것 같아."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Thanks.  I'll give you a performance when you get back with it."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 돌아오시면 공연 보여드릴게요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I guess I'll just skip that note."
msgstr "아마 그 부분은 건너뛰겠습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I read that musical wire is made of tempered steel.  Music shops should have"
" some, or you could take apart a piano."
msgstr "악기용 줄은 강화 강철로 만든다고 읽었어요. 악기점에 가면 구할 수 있을 거예요. 아니면 피아노를 분해해서 쓸 수도 있고요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Thank you so much!  This should last for a while."
msgstr "정말 감사합니다! 한동안은 괜찮을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a guitar string"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Don't worry about it, I'll do it myself."
msgstr "걱정하지 마세요. 제가 직접 해드릴게요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Well Construction"
msgstr "우물 건설"

#. ~ Description of mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find eight pipes for Darryl Johnson."
msgstr "Darryl Johnson의 파이프 8개를 찾으세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need eight pipes to start construction."
msgstr "공사를 시작하려면 파이프 8개가 필요합니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Now that's some enthusiasm, pal.  Ever since our water supply shut off, "
"we've been using the nearby river for most of our water needs.  Who knows "
"how many bloated corpses have decayed in that.  I want to construct a well, "
"but I'm missing some building materials - eight pipes to be exact."
msgstr ""
"정말 열정적이네, 친구. 상수도가 끊긴 이후로 우리는 필요한 물의 대부분을 근처 강에서 얻어 쓰고 있어. 그 강에서 얼마나 많은 시체가 "
"썩어가고 있는지 누가 알겠어? 우물을 만들고 싶은데, 건축 자재가 좀 부족해. 정확히는 파이프 여덟 개나 필요해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I wish you the best, pal.  I appreciate it."
msgstr "잘 되길 바라, 친구. 정말 고맙다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Come back when you get a chance."
msgstr "기회가 되면 다시 오세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Try disassembling some lockers.  Just don't destroy our furniture, we'll be "
"needing it."
msgstr "사물함 좀 분해해 봐. 다만 가구는 망가뜨리지 마. 나중에 필요할 거야."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Well, do you have them?"
msgstr "그럼, 당신은 그것들을 가지고 있나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Well Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Great, I can finally start constructing this thing."
msgstr "좋아요. 마침내 이걸 만들어 볼 수 있겠네요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Water Pump Construction"
msgstr "워터 펌프 구조"

#. ~ Description of mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Find a mechanical pump for Darryl Johnson."
msgstr "Darryl Johnson을 위한 기계식 펌프를 찾아보세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need a mechanical pump to finish construction."
msgstr "공사를 마무리하려면 기계식 펌프가 필요합니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"It's less like a well, and more like a covered pit currently.  I'll need you"
" to find a mechanical pump, one that will make this <freaking> thing work."
msgstr ""
"지금은 우물이라기보다는 덮인 구덩이에 가깝습니다. 기계식 펌프를 찾아주세요. 이 <freaking>을 작동시킬 수 있는 펌프요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Take care of yourself out there."
msgstr "밖에서도 자신을 잘 돌보세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 36 bandages"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Arc Welders"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 110lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
msgid "Come back when you get a chance.  We need skilled survivors."
msgstr "생각있으면 오라고. 뛰어난 생존자는 늘 필요하거든."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Try disassembling another well."
msgstr "다른 우물을 분해해보세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Managed to find that pump?"
msgstr "그 펌프를 찾았나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Water Pump Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Much obliged, survivor.  Thanks to you, we don't need to worry about where "
"our water's gonna come from.  Here, take this as a token of our gratitude."
msgstr "정말 고마워요, 생존자님. 덕분에 우리는 물을 어디서 구할지 걱정할 필요가 없어졌어요. 자, 이걸 감사의 표시로 받아주세요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Chicken Coop Construction"
msgstr "닭장 건설"

#. ~ Description of mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Get 150 nails for Darryl."
msgstr "다릴에게 못 150개를 주세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need nails to build a chicken coop"
msgstr "닭장을 짓기 위해서는 못이 필요합니다"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Now that we've got a steady supply of water, I've been thinking about "
"raising some livestock.  I'm starting with some chickens I found on a farm "
"the other day, but I don't have a coop for them.  If you can get me 150 "
"nails, I can start building one."
msgstr ""
"이제 물이 안정적으로 공급되니 가축을 좀 키워볼까 생각 중이에요. 며칠 전 농장에서 발견한 닭 몇 마리로 시작하려고 하는데, 닭을 위한 "
"닭장이 없어요. 못 150개만 구해 주시면 닭장 하나 만들어 볼게용."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Its a simple job."
msgstr "간단한 일이에요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "You could take apart some furniture in town, or make them yourself."
msgstr "마을에서 가구를 분해할 수도 있고, 직접 만들 수도 있습니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Got the nails?"
msgstr "손톱은 준비됐어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Chicken Coop Construction"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you.  I should have some eggs in a week, once I finish the coop.  Come"
" back and buy some!"
msgstr "고마워요. 닭장 정리가 끝나면 일주일 안에 계란을 좀 구할 수 있을 거예요. 다시 와서 사 오세요!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Trophy Hunt I"
msgstr "트로피 헌트 I"

#. ~ Description of mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Help Russell Connelly expand his trophy collection by gathering three hunks "
"of slime glob."
msgstr "러셀 코넬리가 슬라임 덩어리 3개를 모아 트로피 컬렉션을 확장하도록 도와주세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Relic Recovery"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bible Belt"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I need your help…"
msgstr "당신의 도움이 필요해요…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"I have the location for an alien crash site.  I want you to investigate and "
"bring me anything you'd find interesting."
msgstr "외계인 추락 지점의 위치를 알고 있습니다. 조사해서 흥미로운 게 있으면 가져오세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Good luck out there!"
msgstr "행운을 빌어요!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "That's all right.  Not everyone is cut out for this."
msgstr "괜찮아요. 모든 사람이 이런 일을 할 수 있는 건 아니니까요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Worst case scenario you'll be covered in slime.  There's nothing to fear, I "
"hope."
msgstr "최악의 경우 온몸이 슬라임으로 뒤덮일 거예요. 걱정할 것 없어요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Any luck, survivor?"
msgstr "운이 좋았나요, 생존자?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Good one!  Survivor, you have just passed my test.  I knew you could do it."
"  Your work shall be rewarded!"
msgstr "잘했어! 생존자, 방금 내 시험을 통과했구나. 네가 할 수 있다는 걸 알고 있었어. 네 노고는 보상받을 거야!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt I"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "You liar!"
msgstr "거짓말쟁이야!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Trophy Hunt II"
msgstr "트로피 헌트 II"

#. ~ Description of mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Continue the quest for trophies by finding an unhatched spider egg."
msgstr "부화하지 않은 거미 알을 찾아 트로피를 향한 탐구를 계속하세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"<the_cataclysm> didn't spare us humans.  Our former selves would look at us "
"in disgust at the things we do for survival.  At least, that's what I was "
"told.  I heard reports of arachnids deep in the woods.  I can't exactly "
"pinpoint where their webs are, but I'm sure you'll figure it out once you're"
" stuck in them.  I'd like me a spider egg!"
msgstr ""
"<the_cataclysm>(은)는 우리 인간을 살려두지 않았어. 예전의 우리들은 우리가 생존을 위해 하는 짓들을 혐오스럽게 바라보았을 거야. 적어도 내가 들은 바에 따르면 말이야. 숲 깊숙한 곳에 거미가 있다는 소문을 들었어. 거미줄이 정확히 어디 있는지는 모르겠지만, 거미줄에 갇히면 금방 알아낼 수 있을 거야. 거미 알 하나 주세요! \n"
" \n"
" "

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Thanks, make sure you're ready for whatever beast is waiting for you."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 여러분을 기다리고 있는 어떤 괴물이든 대비할 준비를 하세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Don't worry <name_g>, I wouldn't send you on a suicide mission, would I?"
msgstr "걱정하지 마세요, <name_g>. 제가 당신을 자살 임무에 보내지는 않을 겁니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Managed to succeed, survivor?"
msgstr "성공했나요, 생존자?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt II"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Nice catch!  Friend, you've proven yourself to be an extraordinary survivor."
"  Maybe there's still hope for humanity.  I'll take that egg, thank you very"
" much.  Here's your reward and some bullets for your effort."
msgstr ""
"잘 잡았네! 친구, 자네는 뛰어난 생존자임을 증명했군. 어쩌면 인류에게 아직 희망이 있을지도 모르지. 그 알은 내가 가져갈게. 정말 "
"고맙군. 자네의 노고에 대한 보상으로 총알 몇 발과 함께 말이야."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Trophy Hunt III"
msgstr "트로피 헌트 III"

#. ~ Description of mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Bring one last trophy to Russell Connelly.  Harvest a sting from a bee."
msgstr "러셀 코넬리에게 마지막 트로피 하나를 가져다주세요. 벌침을 채취하세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"It feels like I'm doing this for revenge.  I have one last mission for you."
"  Ever seen those ginormous bee hives?  Well, I can tell you where the "
"closest one is.  Just kill off one stray bee, harvest its stinger and bring "
"it to me."
msgstr ""
"복수하려는 것 같아. 마지막 임무가 하나 있어. 저 거대한 벌집 본 적 있어? 음, 가장 가까운 벌집이 어디 있는지 알려줄 수 있어. 길"
" 잃은 벌 한 마리를 죽이고 침을 뽑아서 내게 가져오면 돼."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I wish you the best of luck, may God guide your path."
msgstr "행운을 빌고, 신이 당신의 길을 인도하시길 바랍니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "This passion of mine may just be getting to me…"
msgstr "이런 열정이 나를 괴롭히는 것 같아요..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"If I were you, I'd bring a gun and a butcher knife.  I don't think bug spray"
" work anymore."
msgstr "내가 당신이라면 총과 정육점 칼을 가져갈 거예요. 살충제는 이제 효과가 없는 것 같아요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "How is the hunt going, survivor?  Any luck?"
msgstr "생존자님, 사냥은 어떻게 되어가고 있나요? 운이 좋으세요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Well, partner, this might just be the end of the road.  I hope you enjoyed "
"it as much as I have.  In the meantime… here's your reward, a handful of "
"icons, that's all I have left.  Spend them all, I think you've deserved it."
msgstr ""
"음, 파트너, 이제 끝이겠네. 나만큼 재밌게 즐기셨길 바라. 그동안… 보상은 여기, 아이콘 몇 개야. 남은 건 이게 전부야. 다 써버려."
" 네가 받을 만한 가치가 있다고 생각해."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Trophy Hunt III"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"You give up now?  This country fell apart because no one could find a good "
"man to rely on… might as well give up, I guess."
msgstr "이제 포기하는 거야? 이 나라는 아무도 의지할 좋은 사람을 찾지 못해서 무너졌어… 차라리 포기하는 게 나을 거야."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "End The Nightmare"
msgstr "악몽을 끝내라"

#. ~ Description of mission "End The Nightmare"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "End The Nightmare"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Kill whatever's keeping Zachary up at night."
msgstr "밤에 Zachary를 잠 못 이루게 하는 것이 무엇이든 죽여라."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "End The Nightmare"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Any luck with that horror?"
msgstr "그 공포스러운 일이 어떻게 해결될까요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "End The Nightmare"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid ""
"Oh thank you!  Now I can finally get a nights sleep.  Here, I've got some "
"icons saved up, I want you to have them."
msgstr "아, 고마워요! 이제 드디어 밤에 잘 수 있겠네요. 여기, 아이콘 몇 개 저장해 놨는데, 가져가 주시면 좋겠어요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "End The Nightmare"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I can still hear it, crying out in the night."
msgstr "나는 아직도 밤에 울부짖는 소리를 들을 수 있다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "End The Nightmare"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "I'm not gonna go and fix this <freaking> mess."
msgstr "난 이 <freaking> 엉망진창을 수습하러 갈 생각이 없어."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Fungus Among Us"
msgstr "우리 사이의 곰팡이"

#. ~ Description of mission "Fungus Among Us"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/godco_missions.json
msgid "Purge the cultists in exchange for <reward_count:icon> icons."
msgstr "<reward_count:icon>개의 아이콘과 교환하여 컬티스트를 정화하세요."

