"It's nice to meet you too, survivor.  It's a tragedy what's become of the "
"New England Church Community, perhaps it'll flourish again someday."
msgstr ""
"저도 만나서 반갑습니다, 생존자님. 뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체가 어떻게 되었는지는 비극이지만, 언젠가는 다시 번성할 수 있을지도 모릅니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Nice meeting you."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave> 만나서 반가워요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I heard what it's like out there.  You must be weary from exploring this "
"unforgiving wasteland.  I'm sorry that you're leaving us this soon."
msgstr "바깥 세상이 어떤지 들었어. 이 험난한 황무지를 탐험하느라 지치셨을 거야. 이렇게 빨리 떠나시다니 안타깝네."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for "
"your neighbors and we'll get along just fine, okay?"
msgstr ""
"우리는 모두 이곳에서 신의 보호 아래 있습니다. 모든 도덕적 문명과 마찬가지로 우리 공동체에도 규칙이 있습니다. 십계명을 지키고 이웃을 "
"존중하면 우리는 잘 지낼 수 있을 겁니다. 알겠죠?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "What is the Decalogue?"
msgstr "십계명이란 무엇인가?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Its also called the Ten Commandments, if you've heard it by that.  A long "
"time ago, Moses lead the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt, towards the "
"Promised Land.  They broke their Covenant with God, and were cursed to "
"wander the desert for forty years, as opposed to the nineteen days it would "
"normally take.  On the way there, Moses went atop Mount Sinai to speak with "
"God.  He saw a burning bush, and heard the voice of the Lord; who engraved "
"the Decalogue on two tablets of stone."
msgstr ""
"십계명이라고도 불립니다. 혹시 들어보셨나요? 오래전, 모세는 이스라엘 백성을 이집트의 노예 생활에서 이끌어 약속의 땅으로 향했습니다. "
"그들은 하나님과의 언약을 어기고, 보통 19일 걸리는 광야 생활을 40년 동안 방황하는 저주를 받았습니다. 그곳으로 가는 길에 모세는 "
"하나님과 대화하기 위해 시나이 산에 올랐습니다. 그는 불타는 떨기나무를 보고 주님의 음성을 들었습니다. 주님께서는 두 돌판에 십계명을 "
"새겨 주셨습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat."
"  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of"
" the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall "
"not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in"
" heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water "
"under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain."
"  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your "
"mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall "
"not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You "
"shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, "
"for future reference."
msgstr ""
"젬마는 잠시 깊고 조용한 생각에 잠긴 후 목을 가다듬었다. \"그들은 이렇게 읽었습니다. '나는 너를 애굽 땅, 종살이하던 땅에서 "
"인도하여 낸 너의 하나님 여호와이다. 너는 나 외에는 다른 신들을 네게 있게 하지 말라. 너는 너를 위하여 새긴 우상을 만들지 말고, "
"위로 하늘에 있는 것이나 아래로 땅에 있는 것이나 땅 아래 물속에 있는 것의 어떤 형상도 만들지 말라. 너는 너의 하나님 여호와의 이름을"
" 망령되이 일컫지 말라. 안식일을 기억하여 거룩히 지키라. 네 부모를 공경하라. 살인하지 말라. 간음하지 말라. 도둑질하지 말라. 네 "
"이웃에 대하여 거짓 증언하지 말라. 네 이웃의 집을 탐내지 말라.' 이 말씀들은 나중에 참고할 수 있도록 출애굽기 20장 1-17절에 "
"기록되어 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"You are most welcome here.  In the good old days we would've held a ceremony"
" for you.  Oh well, times have changed.  Accept this blanket, you may choose"
" either bed by the window.  If you're hungry, you can go see Simon for a "
"meal, up to one per day."
msgstr ""
"환영합니다. 옛날에는 당신을 위해 예식을 열었을 거예요. 아, 시대가 변했군요. 이 담요를 받아주세요. 창가 쪽 침대를 선택하셔도 "
"됩니다. 배가 고프시면 사이먼에게 식사하러 가실 수 있어요. 하루에 한 끼까지요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Gemma."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 또 봐요, 젬마."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "My story?  It's been told a thousand times."
msgstr "제 이야기가요? 수천 번이나 이야기됐잖아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I always have things on the go: tidying, organizing, cleaning, but I don't "
"complain.  I never complain."
msgstr "저는 항상 할 일이 많아요. 정리하고, 정리하고, 청소하는 거죠. 하지만 불평하지 않아요. 절대 불평하지 않아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "There sure is.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "물론이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I'm feeling great!  Even if the world's over, I always have myself and God "
"above."
msgstr "기분이 너무 좋아요! 세상이 끝나도 저와 신은 항상 저 위에 있어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm feeling alright, just working away."
msgstr "저는 괜찮아요, 그냥 열심히 일하고 있을 뿐이에요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm happy to hear that, Gemma.  I'd best be going."
msgstr "그 말을 들으니 기쁘네요, 젬마. 저는 이제 가봐야겠어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_bye>"
#. ~ Avatar response indicated that the conversation is over via TALK_DONE.
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_avatar.json
msgid "I'll see you around."
msgstr "다음에 또 봐요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"My flowers look a bit dehydrated, I'd appreciate it if you watered them for "
"me.  These indoor plants are the most calming reminders of life before "
"<the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""
"제 꽃들이 좀 말라 보이는데, 물 좀 주시면 정말 감사하겠습니다. 이 실내 식물들은 <the_cataclysm> 이전의 삶을 떠올리게 "
"하는 가장 차분한 이미지예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I meant \"Are there any jobs you know of?\""
msgstr "제가 말하고 싶었던 건 \"당신이 아는 직업이 있나요?\"였습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Sure.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "물론이죠. <end_talking_bye>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"You certainly have the marks of one.  I don't understand how you can go "
"walking around looking like an abomination, cursed by God, and think "
"everything's alright.  I'm not interested in learning, either, so be gone "
"with you."
msgstr ""
"당신은 분명 그런 자질을 갖추고 있군요. 어떻게 신의 저주를 받은 혐오스러운 모습으로 돌아다니면서 모든 게 괜찮다고 생각하는지 이해가 안"
" 갑니다. 저도 배우는 데 관심 없으니, 당신과 함께 가세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to know the truth, I;m quite upset with how you've been "
"acting as of late, and I don't want to talk to you.  Now please, leave me "
"be."
msgstr ""
"정말 진실을 알고 싶다면, 요즘 당신의 행동에 꽤 화가 났어요. 당신과 이야기하고 싶지 않아요. 제발, 이제 저를 내버려 두세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Get away from here, sinner, we don't want your kind here."
msgstr "여기서 나가세요, 죄인아. 우리는 당신과 같은 사람을 원하지 않아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Get away from here, sinner, we don't want your kind here."
msgstr "여기서 나가세요, 죄인아. 우리는 당신과 같은 사람을 원하지 않아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Get away from here, sinner, we don't want your kind here."
msgstr "여기서 나가세요, 죄인아. 우리는 당신과 같은 사람을 원하지 않아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"What brings you here <name_b>?  You know we don't want anything to do with "
"you."
msgstr "<name_b>, 여기 무슨 일로 오셨어요? 우리가 당신과 아무 상관도 하고 싶지 않다는 건 알잖아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Blessings to you."
msgstr "축복이 있기를."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Bless you, <u_name>."
msgstr "축복합니다, <u_name>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Stranger, what brings you to our holy home?"
msgstr "낯선 사람이여, 당신은 무슨 일로 우리의 성지에 오셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Good to see you again."
msgstr "또 만났군."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Why might that be?"
msgstr "왜 그럴까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I can't talk right now."
msgstr "지금은 통화할 수 없습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Fine then."
msgstr "그럼 좋아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm Helena, the caretaker of this flock.  Who might you be, wanderer?"
msgstr "저는 이 양 떼의 관리인 헬레나입니다. 당신은 누구일까요, 방랑자여?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm not doing much wandering, I'm staying here."
msgstr "나는 별로 돌아다니지 않고 여기에 머물 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm just passing through.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "저는 그냥 지나가는 길에 들렀을 뿐입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Just like all the sinners, roaming through Hell."
msgstr "지옥을 헤매는 모든 죄인과 마찬가지다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "It certainly seems like it."
msgstr "확실히 그럴 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "See ya later, crazy lady."
msgstr "나중에 봐, 미친 여자야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "여기까지 오셔서 다행입니다. 주님께서 자비를 베푸시길 기도합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "여기까지 오셔서 다행입니다. 주님께서 자비를 베푸시길 기도합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "여기까지 오셔서 다행입니다. 주님께서 자비를 베푸시길 기도합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you, I hope he shares that sentiment."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 그도 그런 감정을 공유했으면 좋겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "감사합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr "필요한 게 뭐지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Corrie and I have finished that solar cart."
msgstr "코리와 나는 태양열 카트를 완성했습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Olwen's finished the radio transmitter she was working on."
msgstr "올웬은 자신이 작업하던 라디오 송신기를 완성했습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the "
"righteous judgment of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He "
"passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous "
"banner."
msgstr ""
"저는 제 삼촌처럼 예언자입니다. 삼촌은 <the_cataclysm>, 즉 하나님의 의로운 심판을 목격하시고 우리를 구원할 방주를 "
"준비하셨습니다. 삼촌은 자신의 환상이 실현되기 전에 세상을 떠났고, 이제 저는 삼촌의 의로운 깃발을 들고 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"He had many visions, and he had many secrets.  I don't know all of them, but"
" there was one he was highly vocal about, regarding <the_cataclysm>, that "
"according to him \"The spawn of Satan shall descend upon the Earth, and all "
"will be consumed in death and destruction\".  He never said much else about "
"it, and always had a mortified face whenever someone brought it up."
msgstr ""
"그는 수많은 환상과 비밀을 품고 있었습니다. 전부 다 아는 건 아니지만, <the_cataclysm>에 대해 그가 아주 노골적으로 말한 "
"게 하나 있었습니다. 그의 말에 따르면 \"사탄의 자손이 지구에 내려올 것이고, 모든 것이 죽음과 파괴 속에 소멸될 것이다.\" 그는 그"
" 외에는 별다른 말을 하지 않았고, 누군가 그 이야기를 꺼낼 때마다 항상 굴욕적인 표정을 지었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Thanks to my uncle's forethought, we've been blessed by God.  We have plenty"
" of food for ourselves, safety from the hordes of Hell, and the continued "
"protection of the Lord our God."
msgstr ""
"삼촌의 선견지명 덕분에 우리는 하나님의 축복을 받았습니다. 우리는 풍족한 식량을 누리고, 지옥의 무리로부터 안전하게 지내며, 주 우리 "
"하나님의 끊임없는 보호를 받고 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"They denied us, they labeled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones "
"at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was"
" on our side."
msgstr ""
"그들은 우리를 부인하고, 종말론적 사이비 종교로 낙인찍고, 막대기와 돌을 던졌지만, 그럼에도 우리는 꿋꿋이 버텼습니다. 왜냐고요? "
"하나님께서 우리 편이라는 것을 알았기 때문입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for "
"your neighbors and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a "
"bed, if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."
msgstr ""
"우리는 모두 이곳에서 신의 보호 아래 있습니다. 모든 도덕적 문명과 마찬가지로 우리 공동체에도 규칙이 있습니다. 십계명을 지키고 이웃을 "
"존중하면 우리는 잘 지낼 수 있습니다. 젬마나 줄리안에게 침대가 있으면 찾아주세요. 하지만 우리 방주에는 공간이 제한되어 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that later."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 나중에 알아보겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "알겠습니다. 알아보겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the "
"Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  "
"You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a "
"carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that "
"is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall"
" not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, "
"and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder."
"  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear "
"false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors "
"house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr ""
"헬레나는 성경을 넘기다가 멈췄다. \"그 구절에는 '나는 너를 애굽 땅, 종살이하던 집에서 인도하여 낸 너의 하나님 여호와라. 나 외에는"
" 다른 신들을 네게 있게 말지니라. 너를 위하여 새긴 우상을 만들지 말고, 위로 하늘에 있는 것이나 아래로 땅에 있는 것이나 땅 아래 "
"물속에 있는 것의 어떤 형상도 만들지 말며, 너의 하나님 여호와의 이름을 망령되이 일컫지 말며, 안식일을 기억하여 거룩히 지키며, 네 "
"부모를 공경하라. 살인하지 말며, 간음하지 말며, 도둑질하지 말며, 네 이웃에 대하여 거짓 증언하지 말며, 네 이웃의 집을 탐내지 "
"말지니라'라고 기록되어 있다.\" 이 구절들은 나중에 참고할 수 있도록 출애굽기 20장 1-17절에 기록되어 있다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"I like what you and Corrie's put together.  I did promise payment for a "
"proof-of-concept, what'll it be?"
msgstr "너랑 코리 씨가 만든 거 정말 마음에 들어. 개념 증명에 대한 대가를 지불하겠다고 약속했는데, 어떤 걸로 할 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'll have some icons."
msgstr "몇 가지 아이콘을 가져갈게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I want Corrie to have some extra rations."
msgstr "나는 코리에게 여분의 식량을 좀 주고 싶다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Let's negotiate some other time."
msgstr "다음에 다시 협상합시다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Here's your money.  Don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "여기 돈이 있습니다. 한곳에 다 쓰지 마세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"A generous soul, are we?  That's not what I was expecting, but I'll see to "
"it."
msgstr "우리 정말 관대한 사람들이죠? 제가 기대했던 건 아니었지만, 제가 알아서 할게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group"
" of people living out in an old evacuation center, who consider themselves "
"merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, "
"perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""
"네, 방금 그 소식을 들었습니다. 그리고 그녀가 옛 대피소에 사는 많은 사람들을 발견했다고도 들었는데, 그들은 스스로를 상인이라고 "
"여겼습니다. 그곳이 우리가 진실을 전파하기 시작하기에 좋은 장소일 겁니다. 어쩌면 <the_cataclysm> 이전에 신실했던 다른 "
"사람들을 찾을 수도 있을 겁니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I presume you want me to pay a visit?"
msgstr "제가 방문하길 원하시는 건가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Oh, I've met them before!"
msgstr "아, 저는 그들을 전에 만난 적이 있어요!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Let's change the subject."
msgstr "대화 주제를 좀 바꿀까."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Yes, you seem like a good fit for the job.  I'll pay you a small sum for "
"getting some information about them."
msgstr "네, 그 일에 딱 맞는 것 같습니다. 그들에 대한 정보를 얻는 대가로 소정의 금액을 지불하겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Alright, I'll go and see what's up."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 가서 무슨 일인지 알아보겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Really?  I'd pay a small sum for information about them."
msgstr "정말요? 저는 그들에 대한 정보를 얻는 데 소액의 돈을 지불할 겁니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Well, they're…"
msgstr "글쎄요, 그들은…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"You've been nothing but a leech and a stain on us, we don't want you here "
"anymore nor your \"services\" you might provide.  Now get out."
msgstr ""
"넌 우리에게 거머리이자 오점일 뿐이야. 더 이상 네가 여기 있는 것도, 네가 제공할지도 모르는 \"서비스\"도 원치 않아. 이제 나가."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Need any help?"
msgstr "도움이 필요하신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Could you provide any medical services?"
msgstr "의료 서비스를 제공해 주실 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I might have some medicine for the community.  Anything you're missing?"
msgstr "지역 주민들에게 줄 약이 있을지도 몰라요. 혹시 놓치신 게 있으신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Are you taking care of Arturo?"
msgstr "아르투로를 돌봐주고 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you want to come with me?"
msgstr "나랑 같이 갈래?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "&Jane glaces at you, scowls, and ignores your presence."
msgstr "제인은 당신을 흘끗 쳐다보고, 찡그린 표정을 지으며, 당신의 존재를 무시합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
msgid "How can I help you?"
msgstr "내가 어떻게 도와줄까?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "<u_name>, what can I do for you?"
msgstr "<u_name> 님, 무엇을 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Oh, I don't think we've met before.  My name's Jane, I'm the local doctor."
msgstr "아, 우리 전에 만난 적이 없는 것 같아요. 제 이름은 제인이고, 동네 의사예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Jane."
msgstr "저도 만나서 반가워요, 제인."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Hi, Jane.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "안녕, 제인. 시간 좀 있어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "외부인 친구를 만나는 건 언제나 기분 좋은 일이죠. 어떻게 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "외부인 친구를 만나는 건 언제나 기분 좋은 일이죠. 어떻게 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "외부인 친구를 만나는 건 언제나 기분 좋은 일이죠. 어떻게 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Sure, I don't see why not.  I've gotta keep my mind off stuff anyway."
msgstr "물론이죠. 안 될 이유가 없잖아요. 어차피 다른 생각을 떨쳐버려야 하니까요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'm doing somewhat well, thanks to my occupation.  The other joinees, well, "
"they're barely scraping by.  It's been tense, and I'm not seeing it change "
"for the better."
msgstr ""
"저는 제 직업 덕분에 꽤 잘 지내고 있어요. 다른 사람들은, 뭐, 간신히 버티고 있어요. 긴장감이 감돌고, 나아질 기미가 보이지 않네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I was a physician, one of the more unfortunate people who didn't call in "
"sick during the riots.  I remember it all so clearly, the cuts, bruises, "
"deep bites, then those oily black eyes, caustic yellow blood, spastic fungal"
" growths… it was terrible gnarly.  Then things descended into all-new levels"
" of fucked up, and some of my coworkers were preparing to just get the hell "
"out.  I followed them."
msgstr ""
"저는 의사였는데, 폭동 당시 병가를 내지 않은 불운한 사람 중 하나였습니다. 그 모든 게 생생하게 기억납니다. 베인 상처, 멍, 깊게 "
"물린 상처, 그리고 기름진 검은 눈, 부식성 노란 피, 경련성 곰팡이 균… 정말 끔찍했습니다. 그러다가 상황이 완전히 새로운 국면으로 "
"접어들었고, 몇몇 동료들은 그냥 도망칠 준비를 하고 있었습니다. 저는 그들을 따라갔습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Were you evaced'?"
msgstr "당신은 대피했나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "No, not by the government."
msgstr "아니요, 정부에서는 아닙니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"No, not really.  I came here after I was split from my friends by a horde of"
" <zombies>.  They let me in after I gave away some food I found.  The church"
" distrusts my profession; I get by helping Kostas."
msgstr ""
"아니, 그렇지 않아. <zombies> 무리 때문에 친구들과 헤어진 후에 여기 왔어. 내가 찾은 음식을 나눠주고 나서야 들어갈 수 "
"있었지. 교회에서는 내 직업을 믿지 않아. 코스타스 돕느라 고생이 많아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I really don't, actually.  Even my help is thankless here.  Bandaging cuts, "
"setting bones, disinfecting wounds; who needs all that when they can pray "
"anything away?"
msgstr ""
"사실, 정말 없어요. 여기서는 제 도움조차 감사할 줄 몰라요. 베인 상처에 붕대 감고, 뼈 맞추고, 상처 소독하는 일, 기도로 뭐든 "
"해결할 수 있는데 누가 그런 게 필요하겠어요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you have any work available?"
msgstr "구할 수 있는 일자리가 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Would you like to buy any supplies?"
msgstr "물품을 구매하고 싶으신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I do what I can, but he's mostly beyond my skillset.  Coke's a <freaking> "
"<name_b>, really messes a person up.  Arturo was on it for several years "
"before he tried to get help, now he has auditory hallucinations; hears "
"voices from nowhere.  Traumatic experiences have a harsher effect on "
"recovering addicts, but <the_cataclysm> is worse than anything we've gone "
"through before."
msgstr ""
"할 수 있는 건 다 하지만, 그놈은 대부분 내 능력 밖이야. 코카콜라는 <freaking> <name_b>, 사람을 정말 엉망으로 "
"만들어. 아르투로는 도움을 청하기 전에 몇 년 동안 코카콜라를 마셨는데, 지금은 환청이 들려. 어디선가 들려오는 소리가 들리지 않아. "
"외상 경험은 회복 중인 중독자들에게 더 가혹한 영향을 미치지만, <the_cataclysm>은 우리가 지금까지 겪어본 어떤 것보다 더 "
"심각해."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Thorazine would go us a long way, but Arturo's having trouble getting it.  "
"They think he's the key and that my help would obstruct him.  Regardless, "
"there's just so much anti-medical sentiment here that I've given up on "
"prescribing anything."
msgstr ""
"토라진은 우리에게 큰 도움이 될 텐데, 아르투로가 그걸 구하는 데 어려움을 겪고 있어. 걔네들은 그가 열쇠라고 생각하고, 내 도움이 "
"방해가 될 거라고 생각해. 어쨌든, 여기 반의학적 정서가 너무 심해서 처방을 포기했어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "What about Kostas?  The Church seems to trust him."
msgstr "코스타스는 어떻습니까? 교회는 그를 신뢰하는 것 같습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"He's an alright physician, but the Church massively overrates him.  They "
"think his 'natural medicine' can cure anything, like he's a magic medicine "
"man.  God created everything, so what on Earth isn't natural?!"
msgstr ""
"그는 괜찮은 의사지만, 교회는 그를 엄청나게 과대평가해요. 마치 그가 마법의 주술사라도 되는 것처럼, 그의 '자연 의학'이 무엇이든 "
"치료할 수 있다고 생각하죠. 신이 모든 걸 창조했는데, 도대체 자연스럽지 않은 게 뭐가 있겠어요?!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "How do you feel about him personally?"
msgstr "당신은 그에 대해 개인적으로 어떻게 생각하시나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Personally, I like him.  We've worked together for a few cases, but most "
"people refuse to let me work; they only want to see him."
msgstr ""
"개인적으로 저는 그를 좋아합니다. 몇 건의 사건을 함께 처리했지만, 대부분의 사람들은 제가 일하는 것을 허락하지 않아요. 그저 그를 보고"
" 싶어 할 뿐이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I've got some supplies on hand, just give me a minute and you'll be "
"right as rain.  It'll cost three icons."
msgstr "네, 제가 준비한 게 좀 있어요. 잠깐만 기다려 주세요. 금방 해결될 거예요. 3아이콘이요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I can pay for quality work.  Here it is."
msgstr "고품질 작업에 대한 비용을 지불할 수 있습니다. 여기 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'm up for it, Arturo's got enough medicine for two-and-half months.  It's "
"thankless work around here, so let's blow this joint."
msgstr ""
"나도 할 수 있어. 아르투로가 두 달 반 동안 먹을 약을 충분히 가지고 있거든. 여기선 돈 안 되는 일이니까, 이 마리화나 한 대 "
"피우자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to leave, but I've got to take care of Arturo.  He's always low or "
"nearly out of antipsychotics, so I do what I can."
msgstr ""
"떠나고 싶지만, 아르투로를 돌봐야 해요. 그는 항상 항정신병 약물이 부족하거나 거의 다 떨어져 있어서 제가 할 수 있는 일을 다 해요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Alright.  Wanna chat?"
msgstr "좋아요. 이야기 나눌래요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I could always use more bandages, disinfectant, and the like.  What do you "
"have?"
msgstr "붕대, 소독제 등이 더 필요해요. 뭐가 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "지금은 아무것도 없습니다. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  I'll come back with something later."
msgstr "지금은 아무것도 없어요. 나중에 뭔가 가지고 돌아올게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I have <topic_item>."
msgstr "<topic_item>이 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Fuck off <name_b>.  I've had it with your tormenting antics, I don't want "
"anything to do with you right now."
msgstr "꺼져 <name_b>. 네 괴롭힘에 지쳤어. 지금은 너랑 아무 상관도 하고 싶지 않아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Fine then, have it your way."
msgstr "좋습니다. 원하는 대로 하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "What's your take on the situation here?"
msgstr "여기 상황에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your parents like?"
msgstr "당신의 부모님은 어떤 분이세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your plans after <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "<the_cataclysm> 이후에는 어떤 계획이 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Were could I find work around here?"
msgstr "이 근처에서 일자리를 구할 수 있는 곳은 어디인가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are you doing around here <name_b>?  Get lost."
msgstr "<name_b>, 여기서 뭐 하는 거야? 꺼져."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, look who's back."
msgstr "이봐, 누가 돌아왔는지 봐."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Hey again."
msgstr "또 만나네."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey again <u_name>."
msgstr "안녕하세요 <u_name>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "Oh, hey, it's you again."
msgstr "오, 야, 너 또 왔구나."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Oh, uh… you look new.  Didn't think we'd see new people here.  Hey."
msgstr "아, 어… 새로 오신 것 같군요. 새로운 분들이 오실 줄은 생각 못 했어요. 안녕하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm just a traveler, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr "난 그냥 여행자일 뿐이야, 꼬마야. 여기 오래 머물지는 않을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm not exactly new here, kid."
msgstr "난 여기 새로 온 사람이 아니야, 꼬마야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "안녕, 제리. 무슨 일이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "What's with the attitude?"
msgstr "이런 태도는 왜 있는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, kid.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 꼬마야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I have a name, you know.  It's Jeremiah, but people just call me Jerry."
msgstr "제 이름은 있죠. 제레미아인데, 사람들은 그냥 제리라고 불러요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "미안해, 제리. 무슨 일이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jeremiah.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "미안해요, 제레미아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I thought asking about each other's emotions went out of style after "
"<the_cataclysm>.  Uhm, okay then.  I'm fine, I guess."
msgstr ""
"<the_cataclysm> 이후로 서로 감정에 대해 묻는 건 촌스럽다고 생각했는데. 음, 그럼 알겠어. 난 괜찮은 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I noticed you're holding a D&D handbook.  Do you play much?"
msgstr "D&D 핸드북을 들고 계시는군요. 자주 플레이하시나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I've convinced Kostas to take you on."
msgstr "나는 코스타스를 설득해 당신을 데려가기로 했습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"My take?  You already know how things are.  People are dead, my friends are "
"dead, so yeah.  At least there's no school, the adults just love reminding "
"me that.  You know what?  I kinda miss school."
msgstr ""
"내 생각? 세상이 어떤지 이미 알잖아. 사람들은 죽고, 내 친구들도 죽고, 그러니까, 맞아. 적어도 학교는 없잖아, 어른들이 그걸 "
"상기시켜 주는 걸 좋아하거든. 있잖아? 학교가 좀 그리워."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I was in high school, like anyone else my age.  Then out of nowhere, my mom "
"pulled me out of school to \"save me\".  I got packed into a bus with my "
"parents and their old-timey friends.  We've been stuck here ever since.  "
"Actually, it's not all that bad.  I'm studying to be a herbalist like "
"Kostas, which is cool I guess."
msgstr ""
"저도 제 또래 친구들처럼 고등학생이었어요. 그런데 갑자기 엄마가 저를 학교에서 끌어내셔서 \"구해 주겠다\"고 하셨어요. 부모님과 "
"부모님의 옛 친구들과 함께 버스에 탔죠. 그 이후로 계속 여기 갇혀 있었어요. 사실, 그렇게 나쁘지는 않아요. 코스타스처럼 약초 전문가가"
" 되려고 공부하고 있는데, 괜찮은 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Tell me about your parents."
msgstr "당신의 부모님에 대해 말해주세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I play.  I ran a campaign for a while with some of my friends, we'd "
"play after school.  I don't know where they are now, though.  Do you wanna "
"play some?"
msgstr ""
"응, 나 했어. 친구들 몇 명이랑 한동안 캠페인을 했었는데, 방과 후에 같이 했어. 근데 지금 어디 있는지는 모르겠어. 너도 같이 할래?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sure, I'm up for it."
msgstr "물론이죠. 저는 그걸 할 겁니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "괜찮습니다. <end_talking_leave>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"&Jeremiah leans his head towards your ear, speaking in a low whisper.  \"To "
"be honest with you, I don't like my mom at all.  She's like a <freaking> "
"helicopter, always telling me what to do, where to go, who I can be with.  "
"She never thinks of me as an individual, only some idea of who she thinks I "
"am.  My dad's alright, he's the chef around here.\""
msgstr ""
"&제레미아가 당신 귀에 머리를 기대며 낮게 속삭였다. \"솔직히 말해서, 전 엄마가 전혀 싫어요. 마치 <freaking> 헬리콥터 "
"같아요. 항상 뭘 해야 하고, 어디로 가야 하고, 누구랑 같이 있어야 하는지 지시하시죠. 저를 한 개인으로 생각하지 않고, 그저 제가 "
"어떤 사람인지에 대한 생각만 하세요. 아빠는 괜찮아요. 이 동네 셰프이시니까요.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I don't know, exactly.  I think I'll stay here and do what I can for the "
"community."
msgstr "정확히는 모르겠어요. 아마 여기 남아서 지역 사회를 위해 제가 할 수 있는 일을 할 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to study herbology with Kostas, it seems like a useful skill these "
"days.  I do feel bad for Jane though, she's a skilled doctor and nobody here"
" cares, they all just think any illness can be prayed away."
msgstr ""
"코스타스와 함께 약초학을 공부하고 싶은데, 요즘 유용한 기술인 것 같아. 그런데 제인은 좀 안쓰러워. 실력 있는 의사인데 여기 사람들은 "
"아무도 신경 안 써. 다들 기도로 모든 병을 고칠 수 있다고 생각하는 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "When do you plan on starting that apprenticeship?"
msgstr "언제부터 견습을 시작할 계획이신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Well…  Kostas is a bit unsure about teaching me, for some reason.  If you "
"could change his mind, I'd pay you some \"icons\", what we've started using "
"for money around here."
msgstr ""
"음... 코스타스가 왠지 가르쳐 줄까 말까 고민 중이야. 마음을 돌릴 수만 있다면, 우리가 여기서 돈으로 쓰기 시작한 \"아이콘\"을 좀"
" 줄게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "아니요. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do for you."
msgstr "제가 당신을 위해 무엇을 할 수 있는지 알아보겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "That's great!  Thanks <name_g>, here's the money."
msgstr "좋네요! 고맙습니다 <name_g>, 돈은 여기 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "천만에요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Darryl should have something for you to do if you like gardening, Jane could"
" use some medical supplies, too.  If you like to be bossed around, Helena "
"probably has a few things that need doing.  I'd just ask around, really."
msgstr ""
"정원 가꾸는 걸 좋아하신다면 대릴이 도와줄 수 있을 거예요. 제인도 의료용품 좀 필요할 거예요. 남의 지시에 휘둘리는 걸 좋아한다면 "
"헬레나가 해야 할 일이 좀 있을 거예요. 그냥 주변 사람들에게 물어보는 게 좋을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Is there anything you need?"
msgstr "필요한 게 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"You know very well what I'm upset about.  Now do like I said earlier and get"
" lost."
msgstr "내가 왜 화가 났는지 잘 알잖아. 이제 아까 말했듯이 꺼져."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Fine, whatever."
msgstr "좋아, 뭐든."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "What are the advantages of being a dorm leader?"
msgstr "기숙사 관리인이 되는 것의 장점은 무엇인가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Heard you and Olwen were some kind of lovebirds?"
msgstr "당신과 올웬이 연인이었다는 걸 들었나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "How did Olwen receive the rings?"
msgstr "올웬은 어떻게 반지를 받았나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Did Olwen like the dress?"
msgstr "올웬은 그 드레스를 좋아했나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Why did you join the Church?"
msgstr "왜 교회에 들어오셨나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Hey…  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  Are you… planning on "
"sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr "안녕… 난 줄리안이야. 이 방을 맡고 있어. 혹시… 여기 남아 있을 거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Why are you still around, don't you have someone else to bother?"
msgstr "왜 아직도 살아있니? 도와줄 사람도 없니?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, <name_g>."
msgstr "안녕, <name_g>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Good to see you again <u_name>."
msgstr "다시 만나서 반갑습니다 <u_name>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Hey, a new face.  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  You're "
"planning on sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr "안녕, 새로운 얼굴. 난 줄리안이야. 이 방을 맡고 있는 사람이야. 혹시 여기 계속 있을 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "만나서 반가워요, 줄리안. 그냥 지나가는 길에 들렀어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "만나서 반갑습니다, 줄리안. 저는 망명을 요청하고 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm a joinee actually.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "사실 저도 가입했어요. 만나서 반갑습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey, good to see you again."
msgstr "여, 또 보네."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nope, just me and you pal.  What's the attitude about?"
msgstr "아니, 나랑 너 둘 뿐이야. 무슨 태도야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Hello, Julian.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕하세요, 줄리안."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "If you have complaints, please don't tell anyone."
msgstr "불만 사항이 있으면 아무에게도 말하지 마세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "You're still staying here, joinee?"
msgstr "아직도 여기 머물고 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Need anything, joinee?"
msgstr "뭐 필요한 거 있나요, 참여하세요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Need anything?"
msgstr "무엇이 필요하신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Go on…"
msgstr "계속해서…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
