msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Oh well, yet another sinner.  Don't talk to me."
msgstr "아, 또 죄인이군. 나한테 말 걸지 마."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Please go away, I'm not in the mood to talk right now."
msgstr "제발 가세요. 지금은 이야기할 기분이 아니에요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "<u_name>, bless you."
msgstr "<u_name>, 축복합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Oh well, yet another survivor.  Welcome to our group, I'm Katherine."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요. 저희 그룹에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 저는 캐서린입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Oh well, yet another survivor.  Welcome to our group, I'm Katherine."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요. 저희 그룹에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 저는 캐서린입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Oh well, yet another survivor.  Welcome to our group, I'm Katherine."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요. 저희 그룹에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 저는 캐서린입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Hi, Katherine.  How's it going?"
msgstr "안녕, 캐서린. 잘 지내?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Katherine."
msgstr "만나서 반가워요, 캐서린."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "You sure, I've got plenty of time."
msgstr "물론이죠. 시간은 충분해요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see you later."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 나중에 봐요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Alright, fuck you then."
msgstr "좋아, 그럼 엿먹어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "It's always a pleasure.  How may I help you?"
msgstr "언제나 기쁩니다. 어떻게 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
msgid "I just had some questions."
msgstr "질문이 좀 있는데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "We have many things to pray for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "기도해야 할 것이 너무 많은 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I understand.  I don't have the answers you are looking for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 하지만 안타깝게도 원하시는 답변을 드릴 수 없습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "그럼 저는 출발하겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Our prayers were heard.  We knew the day was coming, so we prepared.  Our "
"community stockpiled months' worth of canned goods, well enough until the "
"chaos ends.  With the food we have left, we could live peacefully, but we "
"foolishly didn't take extra people into consideration.  With so much at "
"risk, I don't think we can afford more people.  Though I'm not the one who "
"makes the decisions here, and it's probably for the better."
msgstr ""
"우리의 기도가 응답되었습니다. 그날이 다가오고 있다는 것을 알고 있었기에, 우리는 준비했습니다. 우리 공동체는 몇 달 치의 통조림 식품을"
" 비축해 두었고, 혼란이 끝날 때까지는 충분히 버틸 수 있었습니다. 남은 식량으로 평화롭게 살 수 있었지만, 어리석게도 추가 인원을 "
"고려하지 않았습니다. 이렇게 많은 사람들이 위험에 처해 있으니 더 많은 사람을 수용할 여력이 없을 것 같습니다. 물론 여기서 결정을 "
"내리는 사람은 제가 아니고, 아마도 더 나은 방향으로 가고 있을 것입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you can take in joinees once there's a vacancy?"
msgstr "공석이 생기면 직원을 받을 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I worked for the Church, organized charities and filed paperwork.  That's "
"how I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"
msgstr ""
"저는 교회에서 일하고, 자선 단체를 조직하고, 서류 정리도 했습니다. 그렇게 창립자를 만났죠. 모두를 위해 정말 많은 일을 했는데도, "
"아무도 알아주지 않았어요…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"You're right, I don't.  They should've come when they had the chance.  Now "
"that our Ark has sailed, they want to jump aboard.  Such is the way of "
"sinners, I suppose."
msgstr ""
"네 말이 맞아, 난 안 그래. 걔네들은 기회가 있었을 때 왔어야지. 이제 우리 방주가 떠났으니, 걔네들은 배에 올라타고 싶어 하잖아. "
"죄인들의 습성이 그런 거겠지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"If there's a vacancy.  Even then, there's the decision of which joinee to "
"include.  Those people don't share or respect the same values as we do.  "
"None of them are promising candidates."
msgstr ""
"공석이 생기면, 심지어 공석이 생기더라도 누구를 합류시킬지 결정해야 합니다. 그 사람들은 우리와 같은 가치관을 공유하거나 존중하지 "
"않습니다. 그들 중 누구도 유망한 후보자가 아닙니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Jesus warned us about false prophets."
msgstr "예수께서는 거짓 선지자들에 대해 경고하셨습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"She knows this and that about electronics.  The generator we have here was "
"made by her.  Nice to have one here, even though there's not much use for it"
" yet."
msgstr ""
"그녀는 전자기기에 대해 이것저것 잘 알고 있어요. 여기 있는 발전기도 그녀가 만든 거예요. 아직 쓸 일이 별로 없지만, 여기 하나 있으면"
" 좋을 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I hear she knows this and that about electronics.    She keeps herself "
"occupied by doing menial tasks around the camp, looking for payment."
msgstr "전자기기에 대해 이것저것 잘 안다고 하더라. 캠프 주변에서 잡일을 하면서 돈을 벌고 있다고."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"There's not an illness God can't cure.  Yet, by fate, we were given a "
"doctor.  She's now taking care of Arturo, that poor thing.  Oh well, who am "
"I to question God's ways?"
msgstr ""
"신이 고칠 수 없는 병은 없어. 그런데 운명적으로 우리에게 의사가 생겼지. 그 의사가 지금 불쌍한 아르투로를 돌보고 있어. 아, 내가 "
"뭐라고 신의 뜻을 의심하겠어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"She occasionally plays her guitar in the hall, and she's quite good at it.  "
"Unsurprisingly, she doesn't know any hymns.  Wouldn't let her near my son."
msgstr ""
"가끔 홀에서 기타를 치시는데, 꽤 잘 치세요. 그런데 놀랍게도 찬송가를 하나도 모르시더라고요. 아들 근처에도 못 오게 하려고요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"My dear, sweet husband.  He worked as a cook for one of the homeless "
"shelters, that's how we met.  He's always liked to try new things.  He "
"should be in the dining hall, if you want to see him."
msgstr ""
"사랑하는 내 남편. 노숙자 쉼터에서 요리사로 일했는데, 그렇게 만났어요. 항상 새로운 걸 시도하는 걸 좋아하셨죠. 보고 싶으면 식당에 "
"오세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He's my son, such a wonderful boy.  He's always been the light in my life, "
"and I've tried to teach him well.  We've been a bit distant as of late, but "
"I'm sure he'll come around."
msgstr ""
"그는 제 아들이에요. 정말 멋진 아이예요. 항상 제 삶의 빛이 되어 주었고, 저는 그에게 잘 가르치려고 노력했어요. 요즘은 좀 "
"멀어졌지만, 분명 돌아올 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He can keep his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he's a bit "
"more useful than some of the others.  He helped Corrie make that generator."
msgstr ""
"그는 자기만의 허무함으로 거리를 둘 수 있어. 적어도 다른 이들보다는 좀 더 쓸모가 있지. 코리가 발전기를 만드는 걸 도왔지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'm not planning to communicate with him, that's for certain.  He can keep "
"his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he knows how to cut "
"lumber."
msgstr ""
"난 그와 소통할 생각이 없어, 그건 확실해. 그는 그 얄밉고 허무한 모습 때문에 거리를 둘 수 있을 거야. 적어도 나무를 자르는 법은 "
"알잖아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"If you're here for an exciting story, you're talking with the wrong person."
"  Ever since I was born I've lived very modestly.  Did I regret it?  No, it "
"will all be worth it in the end…"
msgstr ""
"흥미진진한 이야기를 들으러 왔다면, 잘못된 사람과 이야기하고 있는 겁니다. 저는 태어나서부터 아주 검소하게 살아왔습니다. 후회했을까요? "
"아니, 결국엔 다 가치 있는 일이 될 거예요…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Tell me about the community."
msgstr "커뮤니티에 대해 말해주세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
msgid "Tell me about your family."
msgstr "네 가족들에 대해 이야기해줘."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I've been a member of the New England Church Community for a quarter of a "
"century, took part in each and every sermon and gathering they held even "
"while I was carrying my boy Jeremiah.  Not to mention the countless times we"
" visited those filthy homeless shelters and prisons filled with sinners.  I "
"even met the Founder himself.  I can confidently say I'm more worthy to be "
"here than those impostors who leech on us at this camp."
msgstr ""
"저는 25년 동안 뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체의 일원으로 지냈고, 아들 예레미야를 품에 안고 있을 때조차도 그들이 연 모든 설교와 모임에 "
"참석했습니다. 죄인들로 가득 찬 그 더러운 노숙자 보호소와 감옥을 수없이 방문했던 것은 말할 것도 없습니다. 심지어 설립자님도 직접 만나"
" 뵙고 왔습니다. 이 캠프에서 우리를 속이는 사기꾼들보다 제가 여기 있을 자격이 더 있다고 자신 있게 말할 수 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "The Founder?"
msgstr "창립자?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure you've met my husband, Simon.  He was also a volunteer at a "
"homeless shelter, working as a cook.  We were brought together by the hands "
"of fate as some would say.  We have a son together, Jeremiah, the light in "
"my life.  Such a creative and well-behaved boy, I just wish we could find an"
" appropriate woman for him."
msgstr ""
"제 남편 사이먼을 만나셨을 거예요. 그는 노숙자 보호소에서 자원봉사자로 일하며 요리사로 일했습니다. 어떤 사람들은 운명의 장난이라고 "
"말하듯, 우리는 함께하게 되었습니다. 제게는 제레미아라는 아들이 있는데, 그는 제 인생의 빛입니다. 정말 창의적이고 예의 바른 아들인데,"
" 그에게 딱 맞는 여자를 만날 수만 있다면 얼마나 좋을까요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He was quite reserved when I met him, seemed distant in his thoughts.  "
"Theresa has the answers you are looking for."
msgstr "제가 그를 만났을 때 그는 꽤 내성적이었고, 생각에 잠겨 있는 듯했습니다. 테레사가 당신이 찾고 있는 답을 가지고 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll talk to her then."
msgstr "그럼 그녀와 이야기해 볼게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Look, I'm rather upset and just need some time alone, okay?  I'm sure you're"
" very busy."
msgstr "있잖아, 난 좀 화가 나서 혼자 있을 시간이 필요해. 알았지? 너도 많이 바쁘겠지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I don't have the time to wait, now can we get on with business?"
msgstr "더 이상 기다릴 시간이 없습니다. 이제 본론으로 들어가도 될까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"&Katherine scowls with anger at you.  \"This is the exact <freaking> reason "
"I don't want to talk to you, now go away!\""
msgstr ""
"캐서린이 화가 나서 당신을 노려보며 말했다. \"바로 이거야. 너랑 얘기하고 싶지 않은 <freaking> 이유가 바로 이거잖아. 이제 "
"꺼져!\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Fuck's sake <name_b>, I'm leaving!"
msgstr "젠장, <name_b>, 나 간다!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I have the pine needles you asked me for."
msgstr "당신이 요청한 소나무 바늘이 있어요."

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "You learn how to craft pine tea."
msgstr "소나무 차를 만드는 법을 배웁니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
msgid "What do you do around here?"
msgstr "이 주위에서 뭐 하는 중이야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"A sin against God, did you know that's what you are?  Get away from me."
msgstr "신에 대한 죄, 네가 바로 그런 죄인 줄 알았어? 내게서 떨어져."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"&Kostas looks up at you and scorns.  \"I'm rather busy right now with an "
"important project, go away please.\""
msgstr "&코스타스가 당신을 올려다보며 비웃듯 말합니다. \"지금 중요한 프로젝트 때문에 좀 바빠요. 가주세요.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "<u_name>, how can I help you?"
msgstr "<u_name> 님, 어떻게 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"You must be new here, nice to meet you.  They call me Kostas, I'm the local "
"herbalist."
msgstr "여기 처음 오셨나 보네요. 만나서 반갑습니다. 저는 코스타스라고 불리고, 이 동네 약초상입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"You must be new here, nice to meet you.  They call me Kostas, I'm the local "
"herbalist."
msgstr "여기 처음 오셨나 보네요. 만나서 반갑습니다. 저는 코스타스라고 불리고, 이 동네 약초상입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"You must be new here, nice to meet you.  They call me Kostas, I'm the local "
"herbalist."
msgstr "여기 처음 오셨나 보네요. 만나서 반갑습니다. 저는 코스타스라고 불리고, 이 동네 약초상입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Kostas."
msgstr "만나서 반가워요, 코스타스."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I heard Jeremiah wanted to learn a few things from you."
msgstr "예레미야가 당신에게서 몇 가지를 배우고 싶어한다고 들었습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hi, Kostas.  Care to trade?"
msgstr "안녕하세요, 코스타스. 거래하실래요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hey, I think we've got some time to chat, don't you?"
msgstr "야, 우리 좀 이야기할 시간 있을 것 같아, 그렇지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hey Kostas, find something interesting lately?"
msgstr "안녕, 코스타스. 최근에 흥미로운 걸 발견했어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hey, Kostas.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 코스타스."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "What the hell are you talking about?"
msgstr "도대체 무슨 말을 하는 거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"I'm afraid I haven't gone out there for a while, maybe come back after "
"<restock_time_point>.  These are all I have, care to take a look?"
msgstr ""
"죄송하지만 한동안 밖에 나가지 못했어요. <restock_time_point> 이후에 다시 올 수 있을 것 같아요. 제가 가지고 있는 건"
" 이게 전부인데, 한번 보실래요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Sorry these are all I have.  However I'll be back from my next run after "
"<restock_time_point>.  Care to take a look in the meanwhile?"
msgstr ""
"죄송하지만, 제가 가지고 있는 건 이게 전부예요. 하지만 <restock_time_point> 이후에 다음 쇼핑을 하고 돌아올게요. "
"그동안 한번 구경해보실래요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Alright, I'll take a look."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 살펴보겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Alright, thanks for informing me.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "알겠습니다. 알려주셔서 감사합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
msgid "What can I do for you, <name_g>?"
msgstr "<name_g> 님, 무엇을 도와드릴까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Are there any jobs I could do?"
msgstr "제가 할 수 있는 일이 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"My story?  I'm afraid it's not as gripping as the other tales around here.  "
"My father was an herbalist, my grandfather was an herbalist and - as "
"ancestral pressure would have it - I also became an herbalist.  I studied "
"from the best teachers and, through the years, a generation's knowledge "
"passed on to me.  I've spent a good portion of my life warning others of the"
" fakery that is plastic medicine and helping them rediscover the forgotten "
"beauty that lies in our surroundings.  I joined the New England Church "
"Community to express my gratitude towards the benevolence of nature.  This "
"is where it brought me."
msgstr ""
"제 이야기요? 여기 있는 다른 이야기들만큼 흥미롭지는 않네요. 아버지, 할아버지 모두 약초 전문가셨고, 조상의 압력에 이끌려 저도 약초 "
"전문가가 되었습니다. 최고의 스승들에게서 배우고 오랜 세월을 거치며 한 세대의 지식을 물려받았습니다. 제 인생의 상당 부분을 다른 "
"사람들에게 가짜 약초의 허구성을 경고하고, 우리 주변에 숨겨진 잊혀진 아름다움을 되찾도록 돕는 데 바쳤습니다. 자연의 자비로움에 감사를 "
"표하기 위해 뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체에 가입했고, 그것이 저를 이곳으로 이끌었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"It's been quiet and peaceful.  Nature is recovering, and so are we.  There's"
" something bittersweet about <the_cataclysm>, isn't there?  Our species was "
"on the path of destruction, but Mother Nature spared us.  A sign of mercy "
"for a creature that did not deserve it."
msgstr ""
"조용하고 평화로웠습니다. 자연은 회복되고 있고, 우리도 마찬가지입니다. <the_cataclysm>에는 달콤쌉싸름한 무언가가 있지 "
"않나요? 우리 종은 멸망의 길로 치닫고 있었지만, 대자연은 우리를 살려주었습니다. 받을 자격이 없는 존재에게 베푸는 자비의 표시였죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You must be new to herbalism, no?  In short, I scavenge the land for herbs "
"to supply our humble community with medicine.  And that's just one part of "
"my job.  Say, are you interested in buying campsite gear?  I came across an "
"abandoned camp while foraging.  One can only wonder what happened to its "
"poor inhabitants…"
msgstr ""
"약초 채집은 처음이시죠? 간단히 말해서, 저는 우리 가난한 공동체에 약초를 공급하기 위해 땅을 뒤져 약초를 찾는 일을 합니다. 그리고 "
"그건 제 일의 일부일 뿐입니다. 혹시 캠핑 장비 구매에 관심 있으신가요? 채집을 하다가 버려진 캠핑장을 발견했습니다. 그곳의 불쌍한 "
"주민들은 어떻게 됐는지 궁금할 뿐입니다…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Care to share your knowledge about herbalism?"
msgstr "약초학에 대한 지식을 공유하고 싶으신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Foraging is about recognizing the abundance that is around us all the time, "
"not seeking out rare species."
msgstr "채집은 희귀한 종을 찾는 것이 아니라, 항상 우리 주변에 있는 풍요로움을 인식하는 것입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You'll need a good book to confidently identify edible and poisonous wild "
"foods.  I'd recommend the book 'Autobiography of a Mountain Man' for "
"detailed descriptions."
msgstr ""
"먹을 수 있는 야생 식품과 독이 있는 야생 식품을 확실하게 구분하려면 좋은 책이 필요할 겁니다. 자세한 설명은 '산악인의 자서전'을 "
"추천합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Never eat any wild food without first being sure of its identity.  It only "
"takes one mistake."
msgstr "어떤 야생 식품이든 그 식품의 정체를 확실히 알지 못한 채 절대 먹지 마세요. 단 한 번의 실수면 충분합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"The huge diversity of wild plants and fungi can be very daunting to the "
"novice forager.  Don't be too ambitious.  Try to enjoy the learning process "
"without getting frustrated or taking risks around uncertain identifications."
msgstr ""
"야생 식물과 균류의 엄청난 다양성은 초보 채집가에게는 매우 어려울 수 있습니다. 너무 큰 욕심을 부리지 마세요. 불확실한 식별 때문에 "
"좌절하거나 위험을 감수하지 않고 배우는 과정을 즐기도록 노력하세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"I can tell you this: pine needles make the best tea.  Perhaps I'll make you "
"one someday."
msgstr "이거는 장담할 수 있어. 솔잎으로 만든 차가 제일 맛있거든. 언젠가는 나도 한 잔 만들어 줄게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Can I try your pine needle tea?"
msgstr "소나무 바늘 차를 마셔볼 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Sure.  Bring me a dozen pine boughs and I'll boil you some."
msgstr "물론이죠. 소나무 가지 12개를 가져오시면 끓여 드릴게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
msgid "I'll be back soon."
msgstr "금방 돌아오지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"This recipe is a gemstone of my family heritage.  Lucky for us that the most"
" common evergreen tree in the U.S. is non-toxic.  Start by rinsing the "
"needles, and separating any woody parts from them.  Then, cut the pine "
"needles in half.  Add one bough's worth of chopped needles to a cup or mug "
"and fill it with boiling water.  Let the needles steep for ten minutes, "
"until they turn brownish and sink down to the bottom.  As a final step, you "
"can strain the needles, but then you'd be wasting precious calories.  A "
"drink like this is perfect for mid-winter colds."
msgstr ""
"이 레시피는 저희 가문의 유산을 담은 보석과도 같습니다. 다행히 미국에서 가장 흔한 상록수는 무독성입니다. 먼저 솔잎을 씻어서 나무껍질 "
"부분을 분리해 냅니다. 그런 다음 솔잎을 반으로 자릅니다. 잘게 썬 솔잎 한 가지 분량을 컵이나 머그컵에 넣고 끓는 물을 채웁니다. "
"솔잎이 갈색으로 변하고 바닥까지 가라앉을 때까지 10분간 우려냅니다. 마지막으로 솔잎을 걸러낼 수도 있지만, 그렇게 하면 귀중한 칼로리를"
" 낭비하게 됩니다. 이런 음료는 한겨울 감기에 딱 좋습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 또 봐요, 코스타스."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah…  I don't think he'd be a good fit for an herbalist.  He has a "
"bad habit of wandering off someplace, could get him killed one of these "
"days."
msgstr "응, 응… 약초상에게는 적합하지 않을 것 같아. 어딘가를 떠도는 버릇이 있어서, 언젠가는 죽을지도 몰라."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Jeremiah's a bright kid.  I'll just tell him to not wander as a stipulation."
msgstr "제레미아는 똑똑한 아이야. 그냥 돌아다니지 말라고만 해 줄게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I know him pretty well, I'm sure he'll learn as he goes along."
msgstr "저는 그를 아주 잘 알고 있습니다. 그는 앞으로 나아가면서 배울 거라고 확신합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"If you don't take him under your wings, I'll rip them off for you.  Capiche?"
msgstr "네가 그를 네 보호 아래 두지 않으면, 내가 너를 위해 그놈들을 뜯어낼 거야. 뭐라고 했지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Alright, you've convinced me.  I'll take Jeremiah on and show him the ropes."
msgstr "좋아, 설득했군. 내가 예레미야를 데리고 가서 요령을 알려주겠어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Alright, you've convinced me.  I'll take Jeremiah on and show him the ropes."
msgstr "좋아, 설득했군. 내가 예레미야를 데리고 가서 요령을 알려주겠어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Alright, you've convinced me.  I'll take Jeremiah on and show him the ropes."
msgstr "좋아, 설득했군. 내가 예레미야를 데리고 가서 요령을 알려주겠어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "No, I'm still certain about this.  Jeremiah just isn't a good fit."
msgstr "아뇨, 저는 아직도 확신해요. 예레미야는 적합하지 않아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Alright.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "좋아. 다음에 또 보자, 코스타스."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You think you're so tough <name_b>?  I'm not taking Jeremiah on, certainly "
"not when his representitive is so barbaric.  I don't know how he got such a "
"violent individual like yourself to do this, but I hope he can find someone "
"else in the future."
msgstr ""
"<name_b>, 네가 그렇게 강하다고 생각해? 난 예레미야를 상대하지 않을 거야. 그의 대표가 그렇게 야만적일 땐 더더욱. 어떻게 "
"당신처럼 폭력적인 사람을 이렇게 만들었는지는 모르겠지만, 앞으로 다른 사람을 만날 수 있기를 바라."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Fuck you then, you judgmental <name_b>."
msgstr "그럼 엿먹어라, 판단력 없는 <name_b>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"I'm talking about you and your filthy, unnatural appearance.  I don't like "
"your kind, and neither does anyone else.  Go repent before the Lord for your"
" many sins, if he'll even listen to you."
msgstr ""
"내가 말하는 건 너와 네 더럽고 부자연스러운 외모에 대한 거야. 난 네 그런 부류가 싫고, 다른 사람들도 마찬가지야. 네가 지은 수많은 "
"죄를 주님 앞에 회개해 봐. 그분이 네 말을 들어주실지 몰라도 말이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Fuck you, I'm blowing this joint."
msgstr "엿먹어, 이 조인트를 터뜨릴 거야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"&Kostas becomes visibly angry now, glaring at you.  \"Feeling pushy today, "
"are we?  If you want to hear it plain, we're not on good terms at the moment"
" and I would appreciate it if you didn't bother me for a while.  "
"Understand?\""
msgstr ""
"&코스타스는 이제 눈에 띄게 화가 나서 당신을 노려보며 말했다. \"오늘 좀 성급한 것 같죠? 솔직히 말해서, 우리 사이가 안 좋아서 "
"당분간은 방해하지 말아 주면 좋겠어요. 알겠어요?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Okay, see you later."
msgstr "알았어, 나중에 보자."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Is everyone treating you fairly?"
msgstr "모두가 당신을 공평하게 대하고 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Ahh!  What the hell are you?  Get the freaking away from me!"
msgstr "아! 너 뭐야? 나한테서 꺼져!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Buzz off <name_b>, I'm not interested in <freaking> chatting with you."
msgstr "꺼져요 <name_b>, 난 당신과 채팅하고 싶지 않아요 <freaking>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey <name_g>!  Nice to see you again!"
msgstr "안녕하세요, <name_g>님! 다시 뵙게 되어 반갑습니다!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey <u_name>!  Nice to see you again!"
msgstr "안녕하세요, <u_name>님! 다시 뵙게 되어 반갑습니다!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I don't think I've met you before, have I?  I'm Maria Serrano, it's nice to "
"see an new face."
msgstr "전에 만난 적이 없는 것 같죠? 저는 마리아 세라노예요. 새로운 얼굴을 보니 반갑네요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you, Maria."
msgstr "마리아, 만나서 반가워요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey Maria.  What's up?"
msgstr "안녕, 마리아. 무슨 일이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Maria, why the sudden hostility?"
msgstr "마리아, 왜 갑자기 적대감이 생겼어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey Maria.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 마리아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Alright, alright, chill out, I'm leaving!"
msgstr "좋아, 좋아, 진정해, 나 간다!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Could you sew something for me?"
msgstr "저를 위해 뭔가 재봉해 주실 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "How's my order going?"
msgstr "제 주문은 어떻게 진행되고 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I arrived a bit later than everyone else, I was at my studio when "
"<the_cataclysm> came.  Had to dodge a big horde of <zombies> on my way out "
"of town, totaled my car, and hiked the rest of the way."
msgstr ""
"다른 사람들보다 조금 늦게 도착했어요. <the_cataclysm>이 왔을 때 저는 스튜디오에 있었어요. 마을을 나서는 길에 엄청난 "
"<zombies> 떼를 피해야 했고, 차가 완전히 망가져서 남은 길은 걸어서 갔어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I always wanted to be a fashion designer when I was young.  I used to have a"
" set of dolls, and I'd make dresses for them out of spare cloth I could "
"find.  I took up sewing in high school, and I was trying to get a job with "
"Fashion Nova before <the_cataclysm> screwed that up."
msgstr ""
"어렸을 때 저는 항상 패션 디자이너가 되고 싶었어요. 인형 세트가 있었는데, 남는 천을 구해서 인형들 드레스를 만들어 주곤 했죠. "
"고등학교 때 재봉을 시작했는데, <the_cataclysm> 때문에 망하기 전까지 패션 노바에서 일자리를 구하려고 애썼어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Things are alright, could be better.  I've been mending clothes and sheets "
"ever since I arrived, fixing this and that.  Theresa's been a big help in "
"those regards, we've traded quilt patterns and designs quite a bit."
msgstr ""
"괜찮아요. 더 나아질 수 있었을 것 같아요. 도착한 이후로 옷이랑 침대시트를 수선하고 이것저것 고치고 있어요. 테레사가 그런 면에서 큰 "
"도움이 됐어요. 퀼트 도안이랑 디자인을 꽤 많이 교환했거든요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Theresa?"
msgstr "테레사에 대해 말씀해 주시겠어요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"She's a kind old lady, does a lot of knitting.  She could probably make you "
"something if you asked nicely."
msgstr "할머니는 친절하고 뜨개질도 많이 하세요. 정중하게 부탁하면 뭔가 만들어 주실 수도 있을 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Yeah, they are.  I just wish my work was more appreciated."
msgstr "네, 맞아요. 다만 제 작업이 좀 더 인정받았으면 좋겠어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What'll ya have?"
msgstr "뭐 드실래요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a t-shirt."
msgstr "저는 티셔츠를 하나 가져갈게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a pair of pants."
msgstr "나는 바지 한 벌을 가질 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a leather jacket."
msgstr "가죽 재킷을 입을게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a dress."
msgstr "나는 드레스를 입을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a duster."
msgstr "나는 털이 달린 걸 가져갈게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a trench coat."
msgstr "저는 트렌치코트를 입을게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a backpack."
msgstr "저는 배낭을 가져갈게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a gambeson."
msgstr "저는 갬베슨을 주문할게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What can you sew?"
msgstr "무엇을 꿰맬 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What's the price?"
msgstr "가격은 얼마인가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Do you make more things with leather?"
msgstr "가죽으로 만든 물건이 더 많아지나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a set of pouches."
msgstr "저는 파우치 한 세트를 가질게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "가죽바지 한 벌을 사겠어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a leather cloak."
msgstr "저는 가죽 망토를 입을게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a thicker leather jacket."
msgstr "더 두꺼운 가죽 재킷을 입을게요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a set of body armor."
msgstr "저는 방탄복 세트를 가질 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I've been busy lately, what did you ask for again?"
msgstr "요즘 바빴는데, 또 무슨 부탁을 하셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a t-shirt."
msgstr "나는 티셔츠를 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a pair of pants."
msgstr "나는 바지 한 벌을 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a leather jacket."
msgstr "가죽 재킷을 주문했어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a dress."
msgstr "나는 드레스를 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a duster."
msgstr "나는 먼지떨이를 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a trench coat."
msgstr "나는 트렌치코트를 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a backpack."
msgstr "나는 배낭을 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a gambeson."
msgstr "저는 갬베슨을 주문했습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a set of pouches."
msgstr "파우치 한 세트를 주문했어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "나는 가죽바지 한 벌을 주문했다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a leather cloak."
msgstr "가죽 망토를 주문했어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a thick leather jacket."
msgstr "두꺼운 가죽 재킷을 주문했어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a set of body armor."
msgstr "저는 방탄복 세트를 주문했습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I sure can!  For now, I can make t-shirts, pants, dresses, dusters, trench "
"coats, backpacks, jackets, and a gambeson; if that's your thing."
msgstr ""
"물론이죠! 지금은 티셔츠, 바지, 드레스, 더스터, 트렌치코트, 백팩, 재킷, 그리고 갬비슨까지 만들 수 있어요. 혹시 좋아하시는 "
"거라면요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Let's get to it."
msgstr "시작해 볼까요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Can you make me something else with leather?"
msgstr "가죽으로 뭔가 다른 걸 만들어 줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses are four icons.  Dusters, trench "
"coats, and backpacks are eight icons.  A gambeson is sixteen."
msgstr ""
"티셔츠, 바지, 재킷, 드레스는 네 가지 아이콘입니다. 더스터, 트렌치코트, 백팩은 여덟 가지 아이콘입니다. 갬비슨은 열여섯 가지입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses take me just a day.  Dusters, trench "
"coats, and backpacks take four days, while a gambeson takes six days."
msgstr "티셔츠, 바지, 재킷, 원피스는 하루면 완성할 수 있어요. 더스터, 트렌치코트, 백팩은 나흘, 갬비슨은 엿새가 걸려요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"But of course!  Right now, I can make a set of pouches, pants, cloaks, "
"thicker jackets, or even a full set of body armor; it should be useful in "
"your travels."
msgstr "물론이죠! 지금 당장도 주머니, 바지, 망토, 두꺼운 재킷, 심지어 방탄복 세트까지 만들 수 있어요. 여행에 유용할 거예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I think I rather want something softer…"
msgstr "저는 좀 더 부드러운 것을 원할 것 같아요..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Pouches and pants are eight icons.  Cloaks and thick jackets are twelve "
"icons.  A set of body armor is twenty-four."
msgstr "주머니와 바지는 8개의 성상입니다. 망토와 두꺼운 재킷은 12개의 성상입니다. 방탄복 세트는 24개입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Pouches and pants take me two days.  Cloaks and thick jackets take four "
"days, while the set of body armor takes six days."
msgstr "주머니와 바지는 이틀 걸리고, 망토와 두꺼운 재킷은 나흘, 방탄복은 엿새 걸립니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Alright, I'll get to it."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 시작해 볼게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Here it is, I hope you enjoy it.  If you want something else, just come to "
"me."
msgstr "자, 여기 있습니다. 마음에 드셨으면 좋겠어요. 다른 걸 원하시면 언제든 저에게 오세요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"'Cause your a <freaking> <name_b> is why!  You think you can just do what "
"fucking ever you want with no consequence!  I'm sick of this, I'm not "
"talking to you anymore."
msgstr ""
"네가 <freaking> <name_b>라서 그래! 씨발, 아무 문제 없이 하고 싶은 대로 할 수 있다고 생각하는 거야! 이제 "
"지긋지긋해, 너랑 더 이상 얘기 안 할 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Okay, <name_b>, piss on it."
msgstr "알았어, <name_b>, 그만해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "How is your love life going in here?"
msgstr "여기서의 연애생활은 어때요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I heard you were handy with computers."
msgstr "당신이 컴퓨터를 잘 다룬다고 들었어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"What in the world are you still doing around here, come back to screw me "
"over?"
msgstr "도대체 왜 여기서 나를 괴롭히려고 돌아온 거야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "You don't look too shabby, <u_name>."
msgstr "<u_name>, 당신은 별로 초라해 보이지 않네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I definitely haven't met you yet.  Nice to meet you, I'm Olwen."
msgstr "아직 만나보지 못했어요. 만나서 반갑습니다. 저는 올웬이에요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a traveler."
msgstr "저는 단지 여행자일 뿐입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Hi, Olwen.  What's up?"
msgstr "안녕, 올웬. 무슨 일이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, Olwen.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 올웬."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "No, I'll be on my way."
msgstr "아니요, 저는 곧 갈게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "You look somewhat interesting.  So, what's your story?"
msgstr "뭔가 흥미로운 분이신 것 같네요. 무슨 이야기를 하시는 건가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler."
msgstr "저는 단지 호기심 많은 여행자일 뿐입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here."
msgstr "저는 이곳에 망명을 요청하고 있습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'd rather not say.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "말하고 싶지 않아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to "
"wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>."
msgstr "요즘은 이곳을 찾는 여행객이 많지 않아요. <zombies> 떼 말고는 돌아다닐 만한 것도 별로 없어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Any old port in a storm, I guess."
msgstr "폭풍 속의 항구라면 그럴 수도 있겠지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to "
"wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>.  The people here won't be too "
"friendly with you either, so that sucks."
msgstr ""
"요즘 여기 오는 여행객이 별로 없네. <zombies> 떼 말고는 돌아다닐 곳도 별로 없네. 여기 사람들도 너한테 별로 친절하지 않을 "
"테니, 그건 좀 짜증 나."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Sure does."
msgstr "물론이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I suppose a lot of us are these days, with all the nasty things wandering "
"around.  I hope you like it here, might not be the most comfortable, but "
"it'll do for me."
msgstr ""
"요즘은 온갖 불쾌한 것들이 돌아다니는 시대라 우리 중 많은 사람들이 그런 것 같아요. 여기가 마음에 드셨으면 좋겠어요. 가장 편하지는 "
"않을지 몰라도, 저한테는 충분할 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "What's up?"
msgstr "무슨일이야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"They're alright, I suppose.  Helena's an asshole as usual, we're low on "
"supplies, and all scared to go twenty feet outside the gate."
msgstr "괜찮은 것 같아. 헬레나는 평소처럼 엉뚱한 놈이고, 물자도 부족하고, 다들 문 밖 6미터도 못 나가는 게 무서워."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Not much too it, really.  I came here on that bus with everyone else when "
"<the_cataclysm> happened to stroll by.  I've been servicing everyone's "
"electronics since then."
msgstr ""
"사실 그렇게 대단한 건 아니었어요. 다른 사람들과 함께 버스를 타고 여기 왔는데, 마침 <the_cataclysm> 님이 "
"지나가시더라고요. 그 이후로 모두의 전자제품을 수리해 왔어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about your past?"
msgstr "당신의 과거에 대해 말해줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Why not?  Oversharing is kind of my thing anyway.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr "왜 안 되겠어요? 원래 제가 너무 많이 공유하는 편이거든요. 면접 질문 더 있으신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"My dad's having a hard time letting go of the past.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr "아빠는 과거를 잊는 데 어려움을 겪고 계세요. 면접 질문 더 있으신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Well…  Things were going pretty well between Julian and I before "
"<the_cataclysm>, but after everything that happened…  Ugh, I'm getting "
"depressed just thinking about it.  Let's just talk about something else."
msgstr ""
"음... <the_cataclysm> 전까지만 해도 줄리안과 저는 꽤 잘 지냈는데, 그 모든 일이 벌어지고 나서... 으, 생각만 해도 "
"우울해지네요. 다른 얘기로 넘어가죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Pretty well actually!  Julian just asked me to marry him!  With wedding "
"rings and everything!  I must be the happiest woman still alive!"
msgstr "사실 꽤 괜찮아! 줄리안이 방금 나한테 청혼했어! 결혼반지도 다 주고! 아마 세상에서 가장 행복한 여자일 거야!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I'm on cloud nine!  I just came back from trying on my wedding dress!  "
"Julian is so charming thinking of everything, I don't know how to repay him,"
" I'm really over the moon with the wedding."
msgstr ""
"지금 너무 기뻐요! 방금 웨딩드레스 입어보고 왔어요! 줄리안은 정말 모든 걸 생각해내는 매력이 있어요. 어떻게 보답해야 할지 모르겠어요."
" 결혼식이 너무 기대돼요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I got a master's in computer science from the University of Rhode "
"Island.  Everyone around here comes to me when they want to keep their "
"computers running.  Corrie works more with the hardware portion of these "
"things; I'd recommend visiting her."
msgstr ""
"네, 로드아일랜드 대학교에서 컴퓨터공학 석사 학위를 받았어요. 여기 사람들은 컴퓨터 관련해서 다들 저한테 문의하거든요. 코리는 하드웨어 "
"쪽 일을 더 많이 하거든요. 코리에게 문의해 보는 걸 추천해요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Could you teach me anything?"
msgstr "무엇이든 가르쳐 주실 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Well, this is a really xenophobic bunch, and regard some of your, changes, "
"as a curse brought on by God.  I'm cool with you though, not like some of "
"these other <name_b>.  There are a few who wouldn't mind you, though."
msgstr ""
"음, 이 사람들은 정말 외국인 혐오증이 강해서 당신들의 변화 중 일부를 신이 내린 저주로 여기고 있군요. 하지만 저는 당신들과는 "
"괜찮습니다. 다른 <name_b>들처럼요. 하지만 당신들을 싫어하지 않는 사람들도 몇 명 있잖아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "In that case, I'd better get going."
msgstr "그렇다면, 나는 떠나는 게 좋겠다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"You've been quite the <name_b> as of late, and I'm sick of it.  Now go away."
msgstr "요즘 너 정말 <name_b>답지 않게 행동해서 이제 지긋지긋해. 이제 가버려."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Alright, I'll leave."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 가겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Let's talk about getting you those trophies."
msgstr "당신에게 트로피를 가져다주는 것에 대해 이야기해 봅시다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Why don't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "왜 이 트로피를 직접 사냥하지 않으세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Why didn't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "왜 이 트로피를 직접 찾지 않으셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "정말 이 트로피가 필요한가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Get away from me, demon.  I shoot crazy sinners like you on a regular basis,"
" and my rifle's right here."
msgstr "악마야, 내게서 떨어져. 난 너 같은 미친 죄인들을 정기적으로 쏘고 있어. 내 소총은 바로 여기 있어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Get away from me <name_b>.  I'm not interested in whatever <freaking> thing "
"you have to say right now."
msgstr "<name_b>, 나한테서 떨어져. 지금 네가 하는 <freaking> 소리에는 전혀 관심 없어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Praise the Lord, <name_g>."
msgstr "주님을 찬양합니다, <name_g>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Praise the Lord, <u_name>."
msgstr "주님을 찬양합니다, <u_name>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Greetings, <name_g><punc>  You okay?"
msgstr "안녕하세요, <name_g><punc> 괜찮으세요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Huh, so it was you over there.  It's always great to see a new face.  Name's"
" Russell, Russell Connelly."
msgstr "허, 거기 계신 분이 당신이었군요. 새로운 얼굴을 보는 건 언제나 반갑네요. 제 이름은 러셀, 러셀 코넬리입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Russell, hey?  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "러셀, 안녕? 만나서 반가워요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Hi, Russell.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "안녕, 러셀. 시간 좀 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Hey, Russell.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 러셀."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Chill out man, I'll leave you alone."
msgstr "진정하세요, 난 당신을 내버려 둘게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"It's not often that we see new folks around the remnants of the New England "
"Community Church.  So, got any tales to share from the outside world?"
msgstr ""
"뉴잉글랜드 커뮤니티 교회의 잔해 주변에서 새로운 사람들을 만나는 건 흔한 일이 아니죠. 혹시 바깥세상에서 전해 주실 이야기가 있으신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "저는 그냥 호기심 많은 여행자일 뿐입니다. 당신은 무슨 일이세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "저는 여기로 망명을 요청하고 있습니다. 무슨 일이세요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Who cares what's up with me?  You're the new one here.  Let me put it "
"another way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking about the monsters "
"that lurk deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them with your very own "
"eyes?"
msgstr ""
"내가 뭐 하든지 누가 신경이나 써? 넌 여기 새로 온 사람이잖아. 다시 말해, 밖에서 뭘 봤어? 숲 깊숙한 곳에 숨어 있는 괴물들 "
"말이야. 네 눈으로 직접 봤어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I wouldn't be here if I saw one.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "내가 봤다면 여기 없었을 거야. 왜 묻는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I've seen too many things out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "세상에는 너무 많은 걸 봐왔잖아요. 왜 물어보시는 거예요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I won't let you leave just yet.  You're the new one here, I have so much to "
"ask.  Let me put it another way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking "
"about the monsters that lurk deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them "
"with your very own eyes?"
msgstr ""
"아직은 못 가게 할 거야. 넌 여기 새로 온 사람이고, 물어볼 게 너무 많아. 다시 말해, 밖에서 뭘 봤어? 숲 깊숙한 곳에 숨어 있는 "
"괴물들에 대해 말하는 거야. 네 눈으로 직접 봤어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I've seen too much out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "세상에 이런 일이 너무 많은 걸 봤어요. 왜 물어보시는 거예요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Well, let's just say I'm interested in rare game.  I've heard stories, "
"rumors and some tall tales about otherworldly beings out there in the "
"wasteland.  That's where you come in.  I want to see the evidence, something"
" physical I can collect as a trophy collection.  You seem to have "
"experience, I was hoping you could help me."
msgstr ""
"음, 제가 희귀 사냥감에 관심이 있다고만 해두죠. 황무지에 있는 다른 세계의 존재들에 대한 이야기, 소문, 그리고 허황된 이야기들을 많이"
" 들었어요. 바로 그 부분에서 당신이 필요하죠. 증거를 보고 싶어요. 트로피 컬렉션으로 수집할 수 있는 물리적인 무언가가 필요해요. "
"당신은 경험이 있으신 것 같은데, 혹시 도와주실 수 있을까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Go and hunt them yourself.  You have a gun after all."
msgstr "가서 직접 사냥해. 총이 있으니까."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I've got other things to deal with.  Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "다른 일도 해야 하고. 이 트로피들이 정말 필요해?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I can help.  Anyway, how are things?"
msgstr "제가 도와드릴 수 있어요. 아무튼, 잘 지내시죠?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
msgid "Find somebody else, dude."
msgstr "다른 사람 알아보슈, 형씨."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I've been better.  Having a hellish time keeping up with strange wildlife "
"that suddenly want us dead… hey, let's forget the world while we're talking."
"  How's life treatin' ya?"
msgstr ""
"난 좀 나아졌어. 갑자기 우리를 죽이려는 이상한 야생 동물들을 따라잡느라 지옥 같은 시간을 보내고 있었지… 야, 얘기하는 동안 세상 일은"
" 잊어버리자. 인생은 어때?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion"
" happens to be collecting trophies.  I appreciate your help, by the way."
msgstr ""
"있잖아, 나도 너처럼 평범한 신을 두려워하는 사람일 뿐이야. 뭔가 생각을 멈출 수 있는 뭔가가 있어야 해. 안 그러면 화를 낼 테니까. "
"난 트로피 모으는 데 열정이 있어. 참고로, 네 도움 정말 고마워."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion"
" happens to be collecting trophies."
msgstr ""
"있잖아, 나도 너처럼 평범한 신을 두려워하는 사람일 뿐이야. 뭔가 생각을 멈출 수 있는 뭔가가 있어야 해. 안 그러면 화를 낼 테니까. "
"내 취미는 트로피 모으는 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Your life, your escape mechanism…"
msgstr "당신의 삶, 당신의 탈출구…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Oh it's nothing new to me.  Livin' off the land, far from everyone - it's "
"just what I'm adjusted to.  I've kept in touch with the church folks, and "
"that was enough.  I had a loyal companion back home, Betsey, my rottweiler."
"  Things have been very different since she passed away, though."
msgstr ""
"아, 저한테는 전혀 새로운 게 아니에요. 땅에서 자급자족하며, 모든 사람과 떨어져 사는 게 제게는 그저 적응된 것일 뿐이에요. 교회 "
"사람들과는 연락을 주고받았고, 그것으로 충분했어요. 고향에는 충실한 동반자, 제 로트와일러 베시가 있었죠. 하지만 베시가 세상을 떠난 "
"후로 상황은 많이 달라졌어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "What do you do now?"
msgstr "이제 무엇을 하시나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Betsey?"
msgstr "베시에 대해 더 자세히 말씀해 주시겠어요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I hunt with most of my time these days.  Whatever game I spot, I bag and "
"donate.  Thing is, it's getting harder and harder.  Have you also noticed "
"how corruption is slowly overtaking the natural wildlife in this God-given "
"planet?  They think the flesh is just rotten.  No, it's mutated, become "
"something else."
msgstr ""
"요즘은 사냥하는 데 시간을 많이 써요. 뭘 발견하든 가방에 넣어 기부하죠. 문제는 점점 더 어려워지고 있다는 거예요. 이 신이 주신 "
"행성에서 자연 야생 동물들이 부패에 점점 더 시달리고 있다는 걸 눈치채셨나요? 그들은 살이 그냥 썩었다고 생각하죠. 아니, 돌연변이가 "
"일어나서 다른 무언가로 변한 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"&Russel's expression becomes somber, and he briefly stares at the wall.  "
"\"She was my dog, had her for seventeen years.  We used to go duck-hunting, "
"she'd swim out and get anything I shot.  She helped me track many a deer "
"through the woods…   When <the_cataclysm> hit, she saved me from some "
"<zombies> when we were skippin' town, but she died…  Then she came back, "
"wasn't herself…  I had to put her down.\""
msgstr ""
"러셀의 표정이 침울해지더니 잠시 벽을 응시했다. \"그녀는 내 개였어. 17년 동안 키웠지. 오리 사냥을 나가면 헤엄쳐 나가서 내가 쏘는"
" 건 뭐든 잡아냈지. 숲 속에서 사슴을 많이 추적하는 데 도움을 줬지… <the_cataclysm>이 덮쳤을 때, 마을을 깡충깡충 "
"뛰놀다가 <zombies>에게서 나를 구해줬지만, 결국 죽었어… 그러고는 다시 돌아왔고, 예전 같지 않았어… 결국 죽여야 했어.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Let's change the subject."
msgstr "애도를 표합니다. 화제를 바꿔보죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I may be more skilled or better equipped but you, my friend, have something "
"I don't: experience.  A good hunter never leaves his hunting ground.  I sure"
" ain't gonna leave it!  Now you <name_g>, you know what it's REALLY like out"
" there!"
msgstr ""
"내가 더 숙련되거나 장비가 더 좋을지 몰라도, 친구야, 넌 내가 갖지 못한 게 있어. 바로 경험 말이야. 훌륭한 사냥꾼은 사냥터를 떠나지"
" 않아. 나도 절대 떠나지 않을 거야! 이제 <name_g>, 사냥터가 어떤 곳인지 제대로 알겠지!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I hate to break it to you, but I came here because I don't want to see the "
"world."
msgstr "솔직히 말씀드리자면, 저는 세상을 보고 싶지 않아서 여기에 왔습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm humbled by your words.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "당신의 말씀에 감동했습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "And I hate to break it to you, but my point still stands."
msgstr "그리고 여러분께 이런 말씀을 드리고 싶지는 않지만, 제가 말하고자 하는 요점은 여전히 유효합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"We're all desperately holding on to our stockpiles, but I can find something"
" for you.  I have some spare hides and pelts, if you're interested in "
"buying."
msgstr ""
"우리 모두 비축해 둔 것을 간절히 간직하고 있지만, 제가 당신께 드릴 수 있는 건 찾아드릴게요. 여분의 가죽과 모피도 있으니, 구매에 "
"관심이 있으시다면 말씀해 주세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Since I helped you out with your trophies, can I get a discount?"
msgstr "제가 트로피를 모으는 데 도움을 드렸으니 할인을 받으실 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Let's make a deal."
msgstr "거래를 성사시키자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I can't give a discount, but here's some meat instead.  Made by yours truly."
msgstr "할인은 못 드리지만, 대신 고기 좀 주세요. 제가 직접 만든 거예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Thank you.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "감사합니다. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see you around, Russell."
msgstr "고맙습니다. 다음에 또 봐요, 러셀."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Now that your guitar is fixed, could you play something for me?"
msgstr "이제 기타를 고쳤으니, 저를 위해 뭔가 연주해 주시겠어요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "That's a nice guitar you have."
msgstr "좋은 기타를 가지고 계시네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"&Sonia glances at you harshly, then turns away.  \"Come back later, I'm busy"
" right now.\""
msgstr "&소니아는 당신을 흘끗 쳐다보더니 돌아선다. \"나중에 다시 와요. 지금 바빠요.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Well now, good to see you again, friend."
msgstr "음, 다시 만나서 반갑네요, 친구."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Well now, good to see you again, friend."
msgstr "음, 다시 만나서 반갑네요, 친구."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Well now, good to see you again, friend."
msgstr "음, 다시 만나서 반갑네요, 친구."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Nice of you to come around <u_name>."
msgstr "<u_name>님, 와주셔서 반갑습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Good to see people like you in the world.  I'm Sonia, Sonia Greene.  I "
"entertain the people."
msgstr "세상에 당신 같은 사람들이 있어서 반갑네요. 저는 소니아, 소니아 그린이에요. 저는 사람들을 즐겁게 해 드려요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Sonia?  Nice to meet you, I'm <u_name>.  How are things here?"
msgstr "소니아? 만나서 반가워요, 저는 <u_name>이에요. 요즘 어떻게 지내세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Hey Sonia.  What's up?"
msgstr "안녕, 소니아. 무슨 일이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Hey Sonia.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 소니아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Alright, see you later."
msgstr "좋아, 나중에 보자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Just playing some good ol' tunes.  There's so much negativity around here, "
"someone's gotta cheer people up, ya know?"
msgstr "그냥 옛날 좋은 노래 몇 곡 틀어주는 거야. 요즘 너무 부정적인 분위기라서 누군가는 사람들 기분 풀어줘야 하는 거 알지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Nothin' much, just sitting around and biding my time, getting any work I "
"can.  I might play something to cheer everyone up, if my guitar wasn't "
"busted."
msgstr ""
"별거 아니야, 그냥 앉아서 시간 보내면서 일할 수 있는 건 뭐든 하는 거야. 기타가 망가지지 않았다면, 다들 기분 좋아지도록 뭔가 연주해"
" 줄 수도 있겠지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"You're damn right.  I like its scars, makes it look like it has a history, "
"you know?  We've been through a lot.  Those pesky <zombies> forced me to "
"harm my sweet, sweet guitar, but I retaliated and bashed their heads in!  I "
"lost a part of me that day, but the guitar's alright.  Just a bit rusted "
"from all that blood and gore, that's all."
msgstr ""
"맞아. 흉터가 마음에 들어. 뭔가 역사가 있는 것처럼 보여. 알잖아? 우리는 많은 일을 겪었잖아. 그 성가신 <zombies> 때문에 내"
" 멋진 기타를 망가뜨리게 됐지만, 난 반격해서 놈들의 머리를 박살 냈어! 그날 내 몸의 일부를 잃었지만, 기타는 괜찮아. 피와 살덩이 "
"때문에 좀 녹슬었을 뿐이야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Now that's a wild story.  I owe my life to this kid Chloe, really.  I'll let"
" her tell the tale."
msgstr "정말 뜬금없는 이야기네요. 저는 클로이라는 아이 덕분에 살아왔어요. 클로이에게 직접 이야기해 달라고 부탁할게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"I was in an underground band - Taurists was our name - before all this.  "
"Performing gigs at local venues and jamming with my friends; that's all my "
"life was about.  Now, I'm a badass soloist with a war-torn guitar, a singer "
"of the old-world preserving the wonders of music and the Taurist legacy for "
"generations to come.  That's also a synonym for not having all that much "
"going on in my life."
msgstr ""
"이 모든 일이 있기 전에는 언더그라운드 밴드, '타우리스트(Taurists)'에 속해 있었습니다. 동네 공연장에서 공연하고 친구들과 즉흥"
" 연주를 하는 게 제 삶의 전부였죠. 지금은 전쟁으로 부서진 기타를 든 멋진 솔로이스트이자, 구시대의 가수로서 음악의 경이로움과 "
"타우리스트의 유산을 미래 세대에게 물려줄 것입니다. 하지만 그건 제 삶에 그다지 많은 일이 없다는 뜻이기도 합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Oh, just fine.  A bit malnourished and all, but I can't really complain if "
"that's the worst of it, right?  My guitar makes our twisted little world a "
"bit more tolerable, though.  Takes my mind off stuff and muffles the screams"
" of the boogeyman, you know?"
msgstr ""
"아, 괜찮아. 좀 영양실조긴 하지만, 그게 최악이라면 불평할 수 없지, 안 그래? 그래도 내 기타 덕분에 우리 뒤틀린 작은 세상이 좀 더"
" 견딜 만해지긴 해. 다른 생각을 떨쳐버리고 부기맨의 비명 소리도 들을 수 있게 해 주니까, 알겠지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Fairly?  There's no such thing as fairness in the world.  The NECC wouldn't "
"give a damn if I starved to death on this very bench.  At least I have "
"friends here, ones that appreciate what I do.  I make music and that's all I"
" have left, it means everything to me."
msgstr ""
"공평하다고요? 세상에 공평함이란 건 없어요. 내가 바로 이 자리에서 굶어 죽는다 해도 NECC는 눈곱만큼도 신경 안 쓸 거예요. 적어도 "
"여기엔 친구들이 있으니까요. 내가 하는 일을 알아봐 주는 친구들 말이죠. 저는 음악을 만들고, 그게 제게 남은 전부예요. 음악은 제게 "
"모든 것을 의미해요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I can play you a tune or two that I know.  It will cost you a little "
"something, just one icon.  The artist doesn't want to starve, if you know "
"what I mean."
msgstr ""
"물론이지, 내가 아는 곡 한두 곡 들려줄 수 있어. 약간의 대가를 치르게 될 거야. 아이콘 하나만 있으면 되니까. 무슨 말인지 알겠지? "
"예술가가 굶어 죽고 싶어 하는 건 아니니까."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Alright, let's hear it."
msgstr "좋습니다. 들어보시죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "&Sonia doesn't say anything back, ignoring you."
msgstr "&소니아는 당신을 무시하고 아무 말도 하지 않습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "[Walk away.]"
msgstr "[가세요.]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Let's talk about your goals."
msgstr "당신의 목표에 대해 이야기해 봅시다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
msgid "Tell me about yourself."
msgstr "네 자신에 대해 이야기해줘."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "What the hell are you?  Get away from me!"
msgstr "도대체 뭐야? 나한테서 떨어져!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"It's you again <u_name>, you have some nerve coming around after what you've"
" done."
msgstr "<u_name>, 또 당신이에요. 당신이 한 짓을 생각하면 좀 담력이 생긴 것 같군요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, it's you again <u_name>!  Any news from the outside world?"
msgstr "안녕하세요, 또 오셨네요 <u_name>! 바깥세상 소식 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Ah, another survivor!  I hope you come in peace.  I'm Tom, nice to meet you."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요! 편히 오시길 바랍니다. 저는 톰입니다. 만나서 반갑습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Ah, another survivor!  I hope you come in peace.  I'm Tom, nice to meet you."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요! 편히 오시길 바랍니다. 저는 톰입니다. 만나서 반갑습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Ah, another survivor!  I hope you come in peace.  I'm Tom, nice to meet you."
msgstr "아, 또 다른 생존자가 나왔네요! 편히 오시길 바랍니다. 저는 톰입니다. 만나서 반갑습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Tom."
msgstr "만나서 반가워요, 톰."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Tom, got a minute?"
msgstr "안녕 톰, 시간 좀 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕, 톰."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Alright, alright, I'll leave you be."
msgstr "알았어, 알았어, 난 그냥 내버려 둘게."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Was it difficult to find us?  We haven't seen a single soul out there for so"
" long, I'm starting to lose my hope.  So, tell me about yourself."
msgstr ""
"우리를 찾는 게 어려웠나요? 너무 오랫동안 아무도 못 봤거든요. 희망을 잃기 시작했어요. 그럼, 당신에 대해 좀 이야기해 주세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "저는 그냥 호기심 많은 여행자일 뿐입니다. 여러분은 어떠세요? 잘 지내시나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "저는 여기로 망명을 요청하고 있습니다. 당신은 어떻게 지내시나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Hey, that's nice of you to ask.  The people here are barely holding on.  "
"Malnutrition, sleepless nights, odd sounds from the woods, everyone turns a "
"little mad in these circumstances.  It's not their fault, I know, but they "
"did get what they wanted."
msgstr ""
"야, 물어봐서 고마워. 여기 사람들은 간신히 버티고 있어. 영양실조에 잠 못 이루는 밤들, 숲에서 들려오는 이상한 소리들, 이런 상황에서"
" 다들 좀 미쳐버리잖아. 걔네 잘못은 아니라는 건 알지만, 결국 원하는 걸 얻었잖아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Please continue."
msgstr "계속 진행해 주세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "No rest for the weary.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "지친 자에게는 쉴 틈이 없지. 또 보자, 톰."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"The sky has broken!  They received a rather passive-aggressive sign from "
"God!  The wait is finally over.  Well, not for me.  So much is left "
"unanswered, and I know for a fact the answer's out there."
msgstr ""
"하늘이 무너졌어! 신에게서 다소 수동적이고 공격적인 신호를 받았어! 기다림이 드디어 끝났어. 하지만 난 아니야. 아직 답이 없는 게 너무"
" 많은데, 답은 분명히 저 밖에 있다고 확신해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Perhaps it's not worth finding out."
msgstr "아마도 알아볼 가치가 없을지도 몰라요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Try not to get stuck in the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "과거에 얽매이지 마세요. 나중에 또 봐요, 톰."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Perhaps.  You don't wanna think about the stuff I'm thinking about, it would"
" spiral a newbie independent thinker into madness.  I don't blame you for "
"saying that."
msgstr ""
"그럴지도 몰라. 내가 생각하는 것들은 네가 생각하고 싶지 않을 거야. 그러면 초보 독립 사상가는 미칠 것 같아. 네가 그렇게 말하는 걸 "
"비난할 순 없어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I'm currently in the middle of solving a pointless mystery for my own "
"entertainment.  Of course I have time!"
msgstr "지금 제 재미를 위해 의미 없는 미스터리를 풀고 있는 중이에요. 물론 시간은 있죠!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Maybe I could help you with that mystery?"
msgstr "제가 그 미스터리를 푸는 데 도움을 드릴 수 있을까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Sorry Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "미안해요, 톰."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I haven't got a story.  I'm an independent thinker.  Living out here, away "
"from the Man."
msgstr "난 사연이 없어. 난 독립적인 사상가야. 남자에게서 떨어져서 여기서 살아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I was nobody but an ordinary office drone.  Lived the average suburban life,"
" prepping for the inevitable.  Had the bright idea of purchasing a Last Man "
"On Earth shelter, but I decided to settle for less when I found out it cost "
"five times my annual salary.  That's how I ended up in a religious "
"campground with my family and a survival kit."
msgstr ""
"저는 그저 평범한 사무직 노동자일 뿐이었습니다. 평범한 교외 생활을 하며 필연적인 상황에 대비했습니다. 지구 최후의 생존자를 위한 "
"대피소를 마련한다는 기발한 아이디어가 있었지만, 연봉의 다섯 배에 달하는 비용이 든다는 사실을 알고는 그보다 못한 대피소에 만족하기로 "
"했습니다. 그렇게 저는 가족과 함께 생존 키트를 챙겨 종교 시설 캠핑장에 머물게 되었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"All of us are here; me, Felicity, and Olwen.  We're so lucky, I feel like "
"crying tears of joy every time I see them."
msgstr "저, 펠리시티, 올웬, 우리 모두 여기 있어요. 정말 행운이에요. 걔네들을 볼 때마다 기쁨의 눈물이 나고 싶어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Felicity?"
msgstr "펠리시티에 대해 말씀해 주시겠어요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Olwen?"
msgstr "올웬에 대해 말씀해 주시겠어요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"She's my wife, we've been married for a while now.  We used to live in Rhode"
" Island, worked at a publishing firm, Stillwater.  She's always wanted to be"
" a writer, that's why we moved away.  We've been a bit distant as of late, I"
" don't think she's taking the \"whole end-of-the-world\" thing too well."
msgstr ""
"그녀는 제 아내이고, 저희는 꽤 오랫동안 결혼 생활을 해왔어요. 예전에는 로드아일랜드에 살았고, 스틸워터라는 출판사에서 일했어요. 아내는"
" 항상 작가가 되고 싶어 했고, 그래서 이사를 왔어요. 요즘은 좀 멀어졌는데, 아내가 \"세상의 끝\"이라는 상황을 잘 받아들이지 못하는"
" 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Olwen's a bright girl; she's fiddled with electronics and computers since "
"she was in high school.  She got a master's in it from the University of "
"Rhode Island.  Felicity's been a good mother for her, always been there for "
"us.  Olwen might be able to teach you a few things, she should be around "
"here somewhere."
msgstr ""
"올웬은 똑똑한 아이예요. 고등학교 때부터 전자기기와 컴퓨터를 만져 왔고, 로드아일랜드 대학교에서 컴퓨터 관련 석사 학위를 받았어요. "
"펠리시티는 올웬에게 좋은 엄마였고, 항상 우리 곁에 있어 줬어요. 올웬이 몇 가지 가르쳐 줄 수 있을 거예요. 아마 여기 어딘가에 있을 "
"거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I see that she is feeling down since <the_cataclysm> ruined their plans of "
"living together, but Julian was asking me the other day about my wedding "
"with Felicity so…  I can expect that to not last long."
msgstr ""
"<the_cataclysm> 때문에 함께 살 계획이 망가져서 그녀가 기분이 나쁠 것 같지만, 줄리안이 며칠 전에 펠리시티와의 결혼에 대해"
" 물었더니… 오래가지는 않을 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I saw her big smile when receiving her ring from Julian, some days the "
"smiles of my family are what keeps me going after everything that happened…"
msgstr ""
"줄리안에게서 반지를 받을 때 그녀가 활짝 웃는 모습을 봤어요. 어떤 날은 가족들의 미소가 모든 일에도 불구하고 저를 계속 살아가게 하는 "
"힘이 되기도 해요..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"She is constantly jumping from happiness after trying her wedding dress with"
" her mother…  I keep getting distracted from my investigation into "
"<the_cataclysm>, but seeing those two makes me smile so I can't stop seeing "
"their antics."
msgstr ""
"엄마와 함께 웨딩드레스를 입어본 후 계속 행복에 뛰어오르는 그녀… <the_cataclysm>에 대한 조사에 정신이 팔려 있었는데, 그 "
"둘을 보면 웃음이 나와서 그들의 익살스러운 행동을 멈출 수가 없었다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"New England Church Community is what they're called.  My wife was the first "
"in the family to come in contact with 'em.  She joined because of their "
"charity work and as for myself, well… you know why I was there.  Let me tell"
" you, being surrounded by like-minded folks was like a breath of fresh air."
"  Even if the only belief we shared was paranoia, but you get what I'm "
"saying.  I tried everything to prep my family for the inevitable, I really "
"did, but in the end it wasn't me who saved us all."
msgstr ""
"뉴잉글랜드 교회 공동체라고 부르죠. 제 아내가 가족 중에 처음으로 그들과 접촉한 사람이었습니다. 아내는 그들의 자선 활동 때문에 "
"가입했고, 저는… 음… 왜 그곳에 갔는지 아시겠죠. 비슷한 생각을 가진 사람들과 함께 있는 건 마치 신선한 공기를 마시는 것 같았습니다."
" 비록 우리가 공유하는 유일한 믿음이 편집증이었다 하더라도, 제 말이 무슨 뜻인지 아시겠죠? 저는 가족을 불가피한 상황에 대비시키기 위해"
" 모든 것을 다 해봤지만, 결국 우리 모두를 구한 건 제가 아니었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I want to find out the truth and preserve the past for the following "
"generation, so that they'll know some of what happened."
msgstr "저는 진실을 알아내고 과거를 다음 세대에 전하고 싶습니다. 그러면 그들도 무슨 일이 일어났는지 알게 될 테니까요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Any progress?"
msgstr "진전이 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Sounds like an ambitious project.  Is there anything I can do to help you "
"out?"
msgstr "야심찬 프로젝트 같네요. 제가 도와드릴 수 있는 일이 있을까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Good luck with that.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "행운을 빌어요. 또 봐요, 톰."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"So far?  Not so great.  Now that the Internet is down, I don't know.  Such "
"abundant hidden information - all gone!"
msgstr "지금까지요? 별로 좋지 않아요. 인터넷이 끊겼으니 잘 모르겠네요. 숨겨진 정보가 너무 많았는데, 다 사라졌네요!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Try not to glorify the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "과거를 미화하지 마세요. 나중에 봐요, 톰."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Of course!  Just put all your literary findings on that chair over there.  "
"Remember, you're not only doing a favor for me, but for all of humanity as "
"well.  World heritage is what we're talking about!  I managed to get my "
"hands on a book called 'Zombie Survival Guide' while, uh… dumpster diving.  "
"Imagine how much this book alone reveals about our pre-Cataclysm culture!  "
"Oh boy, how wrong we were about everything."
msgstr ""
"물론이죠! 문학 관련 자료는 다 저쪽 의자에 올려두세요. 저뿐만 아니라 온 인류를 위해서도 좋은 일을 하고 있다는 걸 기억하세요. 바로 "
"세계 유산 이야기입니다! 쓰레기통을 뒤지다가 '좀비 생존 가이드'라는 책을 손에 넣었어요. 이 책 하나만으로도 대격변 이전 우리 문화에 "
"대해 얼마나 많은 걸 알 수 있을지 상상해 보세요! 세상에, 우리가 얼마나 모든 걸 잘못 알고 있었는지."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I mean, can I help with the research?"
msgstr "제가 연구를 도울 수 있을까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"No no no no no!  Thinking is one of the only thing I have left and you can't"
" take that away from me.  But, If you *really* want to make yourself useful,"
" relevant newspapers would help me piece out the puzzle."
msgstr ""
"아니, 아니, 아니, 아니! 생각은 내게 남은 유일한 것 중 하나고, 넌 그걸 내게서 빼앗아 갈 수 없어. 하지만, 네가 *정말* 쓸모 "
"있는 사람이 되고 싶다면, 관련 신문들이 내가 퍼즐을 맞추는 데 도움이 될 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
msgid "Delivering <topic_item>."
msgstr "<topic_item>을(를) 전달합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "No, I'm all out of them.  Now, I've got better things to do, goodbye."
msgstr "아니, 다 떨어졌어. 이제 더 중요한 일이 있으니까, 안녕."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Okay Tom, go ahead and be that way."
msgstr "좋아, 톰, 그렇게 하세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Why don't you blow this joint and come with me?"
msgstr "이 조인트 피우고 나랑 같이 가자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "You're back?  Shove off <name_b>!"
msgstr "돌아왔어? <name_b>, 빨리 나가!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "I got my rights to be here, chum.  Squatter's rights!"
msgstr "난 여기 있을 권리가 있어, 친구야. 불법 거주자의 권리 말이야!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "I got my rights to be here, chum.  Squatter's rights!"
msgstr "난 여기 있을 권리가 있어, 친구야. 불법 거주자의 권리 말이야!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "I got my rights to be here, chum.  Squatter's rights!"
msgstr "난 여기 있을 권리가 있어, 친구야. 불법 거주자의 권리 말이야!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I got here first, therefore this place belongs to me.  Them's the rules in "
"the <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "내가 먼저 왔으니, 여기는 내 것이다. <the_cataclysm>의 규칙은 이렇다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Now that's an archaic belief.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "그건 좀 오래된 믿음이군요. 다음에 또 봐요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I ain't leaving, <name_g>.  Not until you or someone else has checked out "
"that nightmare for me."
msgstr "난 떠나지 않을 거야, <name_g>. 네가 아니면 다른 누군가가 내 악몽을 확인해 줄 때까지는."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Thanks, <name_g>.  I sure owe you one."
msgstr "고맙습니다, <name_g>. 정말 빚진 게 하나 있네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I ain't leaving, <name_g>.  Not until that eldritch screeching nightmare is "
"dead 'n buried."
msgstr "난 떠나지 않을 거야, <name_g>. 그 섬뜩한 비명 소리의 악몽이 완전히 사라지기 전까지는."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "What nightmare?"
msgstr "무슨 악몽이야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "I'll see you around then."
msgstr "그때 뵙겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"That ain't the point here, chum.  Don'tcha get it?  This was MY territory, "
"but they took it away from me.  Now they think of us as nothin' but a "
"<freaking> nuisance."
msgstr ""
"그게 중요한 게 아니야, 친구야. 이해 안 돼? 여긴 내 영역이었는데, 걔네가 뺏어갔잖아. 이제 걔네는 우리를 그냥 <freaking> "
"귀찮은 존재로만 여기잖아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"That ain't the point here, chum.  Don'tcha get it?  This was MY territory, "
"but they took it away from me.  Now they think of us as nothin' but a "
"<freaking> nuisance."
msgstr ""
"그게 중요한 게 아니야, 친구야. 이해 안 돼? 여긴 내 영역이었는데, 걔네가 뺏어갔잖아. 이제 걔네는 우리를 그냥 <freaking> "
"귀찮은 존재로만 여기잖아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"That ain't the point here, chum.  Don'tcha get it?  This was MY territory, "
"but they took it away from me.  Now they think of us as nothin' but a "
"<freaking> nuisance."
msgstr ""
"그게 중요한 게 아니야, 친구야. 이해 안 돼? 여긴 내 영역이었는데, 걔네가 뺏어갔잖아. 이제 걔네는 우리를 그냥 <freaking> "
"귀찮은 존재로만 여기잖아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Who I was is gone, dead… died when I put down the monsters wearing the face "
"of my friends.  Ever since then, I've felt nothing but disgust for myself.  "
"Let's not fuckin' reminisce."
msgstr ""
"내가 누구였는지, 죽었어... 친구들 얼굴을 한 괴물들을 쓰러뜨렸을 때 죽었어. 그 이후로 난 나 자신에 대한 혐오감만 느꼈어. 씨발, "
"추억에 잠기지 말자."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"They are nice people, lettin' us stay here 'n all.  I got friends here, and "
"while we may not be members we belong here.  We'll fight together if they "
"ever try to kick us out."
msgstr ""
"그들은 좋은 사람들이고, 우리가 여기 머물도록 내버려 두었어요. 여기 친구들이 있는데, 비록 멤버는 아니지만 우리는 여기 속해 있어요. "
"만약 그들이 우리를 쫓아내려고 한다면, 우리는 함께 싸울 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"It ain't so bad.  I got shelter, heat, and people to defend me if any "
"<zombie> shuffles its way in here.  If I want to eat then I'll be doin' "
"construction work all day."
msgstr ""
"그렇게 나쁘지 않아. 피난처도 있고, 난방도 있고, 혹시라도 <zombie>가 여기로 들어오면 날 지켜줄 사람들도 있어. 먹고 싶으면 "
"하루 종일 공사장에서 일하면 돼."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Food is just the thing a starving man needs.  Thanks for the help, <name_g>."
msgstr "배고픈 사람에게는 음식이 꼭 필요하죠. 도와주셔서 감사합니다, <name_g>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
