#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "No, my name has been a name here for a very long time too."
msgstr "아니요, 제 이름도 여기서 오랫동안 불려온 이름이에요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "No, I just made it up."
msgstr "아니요, 제가 그냥 지어낸 거예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Yes, I just got here.  What's happening?"
msgstr "네, 방금 도착했어요. 무슨 일이에요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I don't know about names, let's talk about something more interesting."
msgstr "이름은 모르겠지만, 좀 더 흥미로운 것에 대해 이야기해 보죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "You know the real people's stories?  Yes, a lot like that."
msgstr "실제 사람들의 이야기를 아시나요? 네, 비슷한 내용이 많아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Cool, cool.  So you like myths and stuff?"
msgstr "멋지네요. 그럼 신화 같은 거 좋아하세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[INT 14] Do you have a twin named Malsumis?"
msgstr "[INT 14] 말수미스라는 쌍둥이가 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I'm a very smart survivor of the apocalypse.  <end_talking_leave>  "
"Later Glooscap."
msgstr "네, 저는 종말에서 살아남은 매우 똑똑한 생존자입니다. <end_talking_leave> 나중에 글로스캡."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"And stuff sure.  How can I help you stranger?  They say I'm the nice one.  "
"See this smile?  Nice smile right?"
msgstr "그리고 물론이죠. 낯선 분, 어떻게 도와드릴까요? 제가 착한 사람이라고들 하더군요. 이 미소 보이시나요? 예쁜 미소 맞죠?"

