#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, I got it.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "네, 알겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I just wanted to ask if you have a job for me."
msgstr "저는 혹시 제게 맡길 일이 있는지 물어보고 싶었습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I'm just hungry, and I thought you might give me some food for some job."
msgstr "저는 배가 고프고, 혹시 어떤 일을 하면 먹을 것을 줄 수 있을지 궁금했어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Can we just talk it over?"
msgstr "그냥 이야기해 볼 수 있을까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Get out, loser."
msgstr "나가, 패배자야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Do I have a <freaking> exclamation sign over my <freaking> head, like I'm a "
"<freaking> quest-giver from some <freaking> video game?"
msgstr ""
"마치 내가 어떤 비디오 게임에서 나오는 퀘스트를 주는 사람인 것처럼, 내 머리 위에 <freaking> 느낌표가 떠 있는 걸까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "No, of course not!  Sorry, I'm leaving."
msgstr "아니, 물론이죠! 죄송해요, 저는 가겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
