msgid "Oh well.  Thanks anyway.  I'll go ask around."
msgstr "뭐, 어쨌든 고마워요. 가서 물어볼게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"You mean you're still looking for wood?  Crazy… but we had a suspicion folks"
" might show up in an emergency.  Talk to the manager if you want to make an "
"order."
msgstr ""
"아직도 나무를 찾고 있다는 거야? 말도 안 돼… 하지만 혹시 비상시에 사람들이 나타날지도 모른다는 예감이 들었어. 주문하고 싶으면 "
"매니저한테 말해."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"Well, the machinery works just fine.  We were always self-sufficient and "
"<the_cataclysm> only really made that more apparent.  So if you want to "
"place an order and help keep the operation running, talk to the manager.  "
"We'll trade you for our wood."
msgstr ""
"음, 기계는 잘 작동합니다. 저희는 항상 자급자족했는데, <the_cataclysm> 덕분에 그 점이 더욱 확연해졌습니다. 그러니 주문을"
" 하셔서 운영에 도움을 주시고 싶으시면 매니저에게 말씀해 주세요. 저희가 목재를 제공해 드리겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
