"알아서 찾아가셔야 할 겁니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if "
"you're the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"여기, 지도에 표시해 두겠습니다. 편하게 들러서 거래하셔도 좋고, 혹시 용병으로 일하실 생각이 있다면 도움이 될지도 모르겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "안녕하세요, 고맙습니다. 그럼, 거래합시다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "항상 작은 거래를 하는 게 좋습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the "
"trader."
msgstr "안녕? 생존자를 만나서 반갑네요. 사업차 오셨다면 그 상인과 이야기를 나눠보세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "조언 고맙군."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "안녕하세요. 뭐 필요하신 거 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "일자리를 찾고 계신가요? 채용할 수도 있어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "아니요, 그냥 안부 인사를 하는 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try "
"to find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr ""
"저는 자유 상인단에서 일하는 캐러밴 경비대원입니다. 하지만 저는 독립 계약자입니다. 인원을 모아 안전을 확보하고 정착할 안전한 곳을 찾는"
" 좋은 방법인 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "그럼 당신은 이 사람들을 위해 일하고 있지만, 그들 중 한 명이 아닌가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything "
"like that?"
msgstr "자유 상인들? 무역 전초기지 같은 게 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "It's a living, eh?  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "이게 생활이잖아요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the "
"early part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone "
"else join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those "
"traders need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr ""
"네, 얘네들은 <the_cataclysm> 초반에 FEMA 대피 벙커 같은 걸 싹 낚아채서 그 공간을 독점하고 있어요. 다른 사람들은 못"
" 들어오게 막고, 물자가 필요해서 상인들을 보내고, 그 상인들도 보호가 필요해서 저 같은 사람들을 보내는 거죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "어떻게 거기 갈 수 있나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr "지금은 괜찮지만, 보통 자유 상인 기지에서 일 사이에 기다리는 용병 한두 명을 찾을 수 있을 거예요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "팁 주셔서 감사합니다! <end_talking_leave>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "물론입니다. 원하시면 지도에 표시해 드릴게요. 여기요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "팁 주셔서 감사합니다! <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  "
"Hey, I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch.\""
msgstr "*눈에서 모자를 살짝 내리고 멍하니 당신을 쳐다본다. \"어? 야, 여기서 자려고 하는데. 야간 근무 중이었거든.\""

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "존 베일리"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*looks up at you, taking a moment to place your face, then grins broadly.  "
"He looks about the same as when you last saw him, perhaps a little more fit."
"  \"So, you're still playing on the 'living' team, huh?  Glad to see you're "
"still kicking around.  Always good to run into a familiar face nowadays.\""
msgstr ""
"*당신을 올려다보며 잠시 당신의 얼굴을 살펴보더니 활짝 웃었다. 마지막으로 봤을 때와 거의 비슷해 보였고, 어쩌면 조금 더 건강해 "
"보였다. \"그래서, 아직도 '살아있는' 팀에서 뛰고 있군요? 아직 잘 뛰고 있다니 다행이네요. 요즘은 아는 사람을 만나는 게 항상 "
"즐겁죠.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He "
"is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair graying and his face "
"flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly "
"scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until "
"recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He "
"presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's "
"Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr ""
"*당신을 힐끗 쳐다보더니 말을 걸려고 가까이 다가가자 눈을 마주친다. 그는 40대 중반의 건장한 체격의 남자다. 머리카락은 희끗희끗하고 "
"얼굴에는 수염과 여행 먼지가 묻어 있다. 입고 있는 옷은 헌 옷인 게 분명하지만, 잘 맞는다. 최근까지만 해도 살이 좀 찐 사람처럼 "
"보인다. \"안녕하세요.\" 그는 악수를 청하며 손을 내밀었다. \"여기 어울리지 않는 것 같군요. 제 이름은 베일리, 존 "
"베일리입니다.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "안녕, 존. 여기서 뭐 하고 계세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
msgid "Hi John.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "안녕하세요, 존."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can"
" do for you, friend?\""
msgstr "*당신이 다가오자 고개를 끄덕이고, 미소를 지으며 자연스럽게 기지개를 켠다. \"뭐 도와드릴까요, 친구?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "이곳에 대해 무엇을 알고 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "어떤 종류의 일자리를 찾고 계신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'm looking for a very specific building in the wilderness.  Have you seen "
"it?"
msgstr "저는 자연 속에서 아주 특별한 건물을 찾고 있어요. 혹시 보셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "지금은 아닙니다. 고맙습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Like I said,\" John shrugs.  \"I'm just checking "
msgstr "내가 말했듯이,\" 존은 어깨를 으쓱한다. \"나는 그냥 확인하고 있을 뿐이야."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr "\"당신과 똑같을 것 같아요.\" 존은 어깨를 으쓱한다. \"확인 중이에요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  "
"Might see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is "
"right."
msgstr "잠깐 쇼핑하고 다시 갈게요. 가격이 괜찮다면 먼저 수리할 부분이 있는지 알아볼 수도 있을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "무엇을 쇼핑하시나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "\"어디로 가는 길에?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "어떤 종류의 일을 찾고 계신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "뭔가 가르쳐 줄 시간이 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr "네, 저와 비슷한 것 같네요. 다시 이야기해야겠네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a "
"stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't "
"use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a "
"lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to "
"loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where "
"they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr ""
"잘 모르겠어요. 식량 비축량은 저와 우리 가족에게 그렇게 나쁘지 않아요. 일찍이 통조림을 좀 구했는데, 한동안은 쓸 수 있을 거예요. "
"총은 가능하면 안 써요. 너무 시끄러워서요. 그런데 놈들이 건축 자재를 많이 가지고 다니는 것 같아요. 시내에서 차를 몰고 철물점이나 "
"목재소를 털려고 하는 건 자살 행위나 다름없어요. 그래서 제 돈을 거기서 빼돌릴 것 같아요. 배달은 되는지 궁금하네요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "다음에는 어디로 갈까요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "\"당신과 당신의 사람들\"은 누구인가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "일자리를 찾고 계신가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  John listens "
"intently"
msgstr "&당신은 최선을 다해 창고를 설명해 주었습니다. 존은 주의 깊게 듣고 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
", then shakes his head.  \"I don't believe I've heard about anything like "
"that, no.  Sorry.\""
msgstr "그러고는 고개를 저었다. \"그런 얘기는 들어본 적이 없는 것 같아요. 죄송해요.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"I can't guarantee it, but I'm pretty sure I've seen"
" something like that.  It was far away, and the weather was bad.  Could've "
"been a church or something, but it didn't look right for that.\""
msgstr ""
"생각에 잠긴 듯 말했다. \"장담은 못 하지만, 그런 걸 본 적이 있는 것 같아요. 멀리 떨어져 있었고 날씨도 안 좋았죠. 교회 같은 "
"곳일 수도 있었지만, 그런 건 아닌 것 같았어요.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Oh well, thanks John.  I'll go ask around."
msgstr "아, 고맙네요, 존. 가서 물어볼게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of "
"them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make "
"it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of"
" them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been"
" through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people "
"though, so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be "
"done, then move on."
msgstr ""
"여기 사람들과 직접 얘기해 보는 게 좋을 거야. <the_cataclysm> 초기에 여기 모인 사람들 중 상당수가 살아남은 것 같아. "
"내가 지금까지 찾은 생존자 중 가장 많은 수지만, 대부분은 지하실에 숨어 있어. 나도 그 충동을 이해할 수 있어. 우리 모두 너무 많은 "
"걸 겪었잖아. 그런데 더 많은 사람을 수용할 공간이 없다고 하니까, 쇼핑 좀 하고, 할 일이 있는지 알아본 후 다음 단계로 넘어가려고 "
"왔어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "\"Move on\" where?"
msgstr "\"계속 나아가라\"는 말은 어디서?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how "
"this trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my "
"hideout and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr ""
"누가 진짜로 말할 수 있을까? 딱히 확실한 계획은 없어. 이번 여행이 어떻게 되느냐에 달렸지. 차에 짐을 가득 채우면 은신처로 돌아가서 "
"거기 있는 사람들 다 확인해야 할 것 같아. 너무 오래 떠나 있는 건 싫어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "\"모두\"란 누구인가요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the "
"really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she"
" told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an "
"unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  "
"Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things "
"were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left "
"on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a"
" lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one "
"thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out "
"for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and "
"scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr ""
"허, 뭐, 간단히 말해서, 저는 정말, 정말 초기에 아내와 아이들을 도시 밖으로 데려갔어요. 아내는 직감이 뛰어나서 도시를 떠날 준비를 "
"하라고 했을 때, 최악의 경우 아빠의 옛 오두막에서 불필요한 초봄 휴가를 보내는 거라고 생각했죠. 아시겠죠? 당연히 아내의 직감을 믿는 "
"게 우리 모두를 구했고, 그 이상도 그 이상도 구했죠. 여전히 힘들었지만, 제가 들은 바에 따르면 동부 해안에서 핵가족을 모두 거느린 "
"사람은 제가 유일할지도 몰라요. 아직도 그 일 때문에 죄책감에 시달리고 있고… 다른 사람들은 다 잃었어요. 어쨌든, 이런저런 일들이 "
"이어졌고, 우리는 우리가 조심하는 몇몇 사람들을 모았어요. 제 친구 다리우스는 일찍 합류했고, 그와 저는 정찰과 청소를 하며 서로의 뒤를"
" 봐주고 있어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "여러분 어디에 계시나요? 저도 가입할 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "다리우스에 대해 말해주세요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "일이 잘못될 줄 어떻게 알았어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "그건 꽤나 믿기 힘든 이야기인 듯합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "조언을 해줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "예전에는 무슨 일을 하셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "화제를 바꿔 볼까요. 여기서 뭐 한다고 하셨죠?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my "
"people, okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some "
"scary fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite "
"your face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's "
"end is a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't "
"really welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you"
" and I get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr ""
"솔직히 말해서, 우리 사람들에 대해 너무 많이 말하고 싶지 않아. 알았지? 괜찮아 보이는 건 알겠지만, 오해는 마. 하지만 세상에는 정말"
" 무서운 사람들이 많아. 겉으로는 멀쩡해 보이다가 혼자 있으면 얼굴을 물어뜯으려고 하잖아. 세상 종말에 대한 반응은 사람마다 조금씩 "
"달라. 우리 사람들은 이제 안정을 찾았지만, 새로운 얼굴은 더 이상 환영하지 않아. 그랬으면 좋겠어. 언젠가 우리가 서로 더 잘 알게 "
"되면 생각이 바뀔지도 몰라."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "당신의 이야기 전체가 좀 믿기지 않네요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he "
"won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, "
"hey?  Anyway.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days "
"without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so "
"he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr ""
"다리우스에 대해 알고 싶으면 다리우스한테 물어보세요. 좋은 사람이고, 절대 물지 않아요. 아, 죄송해요. 좀 뜬금없는 말인데, 아마 "
"은퇴해야 할 것 같아요, 그렇죠? 어쨌든. 다리우스가 없었다면 첫 며칠을 버틸 수 있었을지 모르겠네요. 폭동 이후로 군중 속에서 좀 "
"예민해져서, 지금은 우리 경기를 보러 나가 있어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going "
"to go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, "
"as much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it "
"out.  When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up "
"in the Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a "
"getaway anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get "
"out to the cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It "
"wasn't so much knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck "
"that we trusted our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr ""
"가끔은 다른 사람들이 왜 일이 잘못될지 *모르는* 건지 궁금해요. 돌이켜보면 20대 20인 것 같아요. 솔직히 말해서, 아무리 "
"자화자찬하고 싶더라도, 제가 알아낸 건 아니었어요. 아주 초기 폭동이 시작되었을 때, 비록 중서부에서 일어났지만, 아내는 그냥 불길한 "
"예감이 들었어요. 어차피 여행을 생각하고 있었고, 저는 시간이 좀 있었으니까, 오두막으로 나가서 모든 게 가라앉기를 기다리는 핑계로 "
"삼았어요. 이렇게 되었죠. 일이 어떻게 될지 미리 알고 있었던 게 아니라, 그저 순전히 운이 좋았던 거죠. *그녀*의 직감을 적절한 때에"
" 믿고 운이 좋았던 거죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do "
"gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie "
"hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the "
"unlikely thing.\""
msgstr ""
"*낄낄거림. \"그럼 내 말 믿든 말든 내겐 다행인 일이네. 그런데 진짜 좀비 사냥꾼인 우리가 마주 보고 이야기하는데, 내 *생존 "
"이야기*가 믿기지 않는다고 생각하는 게 웃기네.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand,"
" but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of "
"help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find "
"for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a"
" lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough"
" as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos "
"out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little "
"things I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't "
"put me in too much danger."
msgstr ""
"도움이 필요한 사람들이 있으면 잡일도 합니다. 아시다시피 자원봉사는 아니지만, 그렇다고 해서 불공평하게 대하지는 않으려고 노력합니다. "
"요즘 많은 사람들이 도움이 필요합니다. 저 같은 청소부라면 찾아줄 수 있는 작은 물건들만으로도 충분합니다. 여러분과 저 같은 사람들은 "
"많은 사람들이 그곳으로 돌아가는 것을 얼마나 두려워하는지 과소평가하기 쉽습니다. 상황이 이미 충분히 나쁜데, 그런 사람들은 그곳이 정말 "
"혼란스러웠을 때 피난처를 찾았습니다. 그곳에서는 풀어야 할 트라우마가 너무 많습니다. 어쨌든 제가 그들을 위해 할 수 있는 작은 일들이 "
"있다면, 제가 할 수 있는 한 최대한 도와주려고 노력합니다. 제가 너무 큰 위험에 처하지 않는 한 말이죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill "
"count?"
msgstr "싸움에서 잘 해낼 수 있을 것 같군요. 좀비 처치 횟수는 몇 번이나 되세요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "당신 같은 사람이 필요해요. 저와 함께 여행하실래요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "당신은 사람들의 감정에 대해 많이 아는 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "네, 맞아요. 당신과 저 같은 사람들은 더 강한 사람들로 이루어져 있거든요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand "
"everything to them."
msgstr "사람들은 모든 것을 당신에게 맡기는 것이 아니라 스스로 스스로 해결하는 법을 배워야 합니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, "
"doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human "
"though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, "
"especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help "
"it.\""
msgstr ""
"*조금 수줍게 웃는다. \"그런 걸 기록하는 건 좀 기분 나쁘잖아, 안 그래?\" 그는 <mywp>에 여러 칸을 표시한다. \"그래도 난"
" 인간이잖아. 지금까지 <npc_val:zkc_john>까지는 해봤어. 내겐 너무 많은 것 같아. 특히 난 가능하면 적과 직접 교전하는 "
"걸 피하려고 하거든.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a "
"good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially "
"these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to "
"watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr ""
"*당신을 훑어보더니 슬프게 고개를 저었다. \"다리우스와 저는 잘 지내고 있어요. 특히 요즘 같은 시기에 세 번째 사람을 두는 건 쉽지 "
"않을 거예요. 신뢰는 쉽지 않죠. 죄송해요. 당신을 지켜줄 사람이 있기를 바라지만, 제가 대신할 순 없어요.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of "
"stronger stuff."
msgstr "아쉽네요. 우리는 좋은 팀이 될 수 있을 거예요. 당신과 저 같은 사람들은 더 강한 사람들로 이루어져 있잖아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "맞아요. 사람들은 스스로를 지키는 법을 배워야 해요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, "
"especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  "
"Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time "
"judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr ""
"네, 저는, 어… 그런 건 좀 알아요. 공감하지 않을 수가 없어요. 특히 제가 다른 사람들만큼 강하지 않다는 걸 알면서요. 순전히 운 "
"좋게 말이죠. 게다가 이제 우리 가족은 너무 적잖아요. 다른 사람들이 세상의 종말을 얼마나 힘겹게 견뎌냈는지 판단하는 데 시간 낭비하는 "
"게 무슨 의미가 있겠어요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "뭔가 과거가 있는 것 같은데, 그 이야기를 좀 해볼까요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just "
"say I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr ""
"사실 그렇지 않아요. 다 오래된 일이고, 이미 벌어진 일들이 너무 많잖아요. 그냥 제가 상실을 겪는 게 낯설지 않다고만 해두죠. 제 "
"자신이든 다른 사람이든 말이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about"
" thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure,"
" not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe "
"home, too.\""
msgstr ""
"*눈썹을 치켜올린다. \"그건 잘 모르겠어. 너와 같은 선택을 하지 않는 사람들을 열등하다고 생각하는 건 조심해야 해. 물론 모든 사람이"
" 쓰레기 수거에 적합한 건 아니지만, 쓰레기 수거꾼에게도 안전한 집이 있어야 하잖아.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "씨발. 사람들은 스스로 살아가는 법을 배워야 해."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be "
"independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than"
" the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into "
"civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're "
"doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr ""
"*수염을 문지르며 생각에 잠긴 듯 말했다. \"독립하는 게 중요하다는 건 나도 인정해. 하지만 잊지 마, 함께 일하는 게 우리를 "
"언데드보다 낫게 만들어 주는 거란다. 우리가 나무와 들판을 벗어나 문명 사회로 나아갈 수 있었던 이유지. 어쨌든, 철학적인 얘기는 하고 "
"싶지 않아. 혼자서 잘 해내고 있다면, 더 잘해낼 수 있을 거야!\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "그건 약자들을 위한 거야. 너나 나 같은 사람들은 더 강한 사람들로 만들어졌잖아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "글쎄요, 좀비들이 서로 협력하는 것 같아요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best"
" to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and "
"it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr ""
"*낄낄거린다. \"그렇게 부를 수 있다면, 물론이지. 그러니까 좀비들보다 더 잘하려고 최선을 다해야 할지도 몰라. 내 생각엔 꽤 합리적인"
" 것 같은데, 넘기 힘든 기준이 꽤 낮아.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you"
" can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever "
"possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I "
"try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have "
"the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid "
"so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high "
"ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with "
"spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes "
"instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we "
"can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are "
"suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to "
"the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and "
"try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that "
"little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, "
"zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a "
"crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can "
"avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  "
"We get a lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, "
"where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr ""
"물론이죠. 제가 당신이 모르는 게 있는지는 모르겠지만, 당신은 스스로를 잘 다스리는 것 같네요. 저는 가능한 한 교전하지 않고 여기까지 "
"왔습니다. 밖에 있는 좀비들을 다 죽일 생각은 없습니다. 다리우스와 저는 피할 수 있다면 싸우지 않으려고 노력하고, 피할 수 없다면 항상"
" 유리한 위치를 차지하려고 노력합니다. 숫자, 무기, 지형. 좀비들은 서투르고 멍청해서 덤불 같은 곳을 지나가게 해서 넘어지게 합니다. "
"높은 곳에 자리를 잡고 그들이 바보처럼 사다리를 박차고 올라가도록 내버려 두면서 위에서 창으로 찔러줍니다. 하지만 대부분 눈에 띄지 "
"않으려고 노력합니다. 소음도 없고 기름도 필요 없는 자동차 대신 자전거를 이용하고, 숲길을 따라가면 교통 체증을 피할 수 있습니다. 그런"
" 건 자살 행위입니다. 도시는 피하려고 노력하고, 가까이 다가갈 때는 외곽으로 가서 외딴집들을 습격합니다. 그런 상황에서는 몸을 웅크리고"
" 건물 깊숙이 들어가거나 지하실로 빠르게 내려가려고 노력합니다. 그러면 작은 소리가 잘 들리지 않고 밖에서 아무것도 우리를 볼 수 "
"없으니까요. 그리고 좀비들은 멍청하니까 블라인드를 내리는 것도 좋은 방법입니다. 저는 항상 문과 창문을 열기 위해 쇠지렛대를 가지고 "
"다니지만, 가능하면 사용하지 않으려고 노력합니다. 다리우스는 자물쇠를 따는 능력이 있는데, 속도는 느리지만 소리는 나지 않습니다. "
"주유소나 다른 시골 지역을 습격하면 훨씬 더 많은 이득을 얻을 수 있는데, 좀비가 몇 마리 있다면 보통 유인해서 쫓아낼 수 있으니까요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "좀비 외의 다른 것들은 어떨까?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen "
"some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we "
"don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  "
"One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a "
"cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started "
"hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  "
"Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to "
"travel these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we "
"turn around and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't"
" outrun."
msgstr ""
"아, 세상에, 맞아. 세상이 정말 엉망진창이 됐지, 안 그래? 음, 이상한 외계 생명체들을 좀 봤어. 우리 규칙은 '죽는 것보다 "
"무서워하는 게 낫다'야. 뭐가 뭔지, 어떻게 죽여야 할지 모르면, 그냥 휙 지나가. 한번은 멀리서 불타는 눈알을 봤어. 휴대폰 기지국에서"
" 정찰 중이었는데. 눈이 마주치더니 갑자기 환각이 시작됐어. 다리우스가 내가 기지국에서 떨어지지 않게 막아줬지. 이런 일들 때문에 요즘은"
" 어쩔 수 없는 경우가 아니면 여행을 하려면 정신이 좀 나가야 하는 것 같아. 모르는 게 있으면 뒤돌아보고 열심히 페달을 밟아. 지금까지"
" 우리 자전거가 따라잡을 수 없는 건 만나본 적이 없어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  "
"My dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop "
"quite a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of "
"work, but then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and "
"electrical work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering "
"degree, then decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time "
"doing freelance electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a "
"startup that was designing and programming medical equipment.  I was "
"supposed to be a general technician, but through a weird series of events I "
"wound up in sales, then management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big "
"nest egg from my share stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  "
"That was a dumb move, I was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and "
"started doing on-call teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things "
"like that at a college and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent "
"the rest of my time outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr ""
"생각보다 어려운 질문이네요. 저는 꽤 멋진 삶을 살았어요. 아버지가 정비공이셨고, 어렸을 때는 가게에서 꽤 많이 일했죠. 처음에는 그 "
"일을 하려고 생각했지만, 딴 데로 가면서 오랫동안 컴퓨터와 전기 관련 일을 하게 됐어요. 전기 공학 학위를 일부 공부했지만, 제게 맞지 "
"않다고 판단해서 그만두었죠. 프리랜서로 전기 및 프로그래밍 일을 잠시 하다가 의료 장비 설계 및 프로그래밍을 하는 스타트업에 채용됐어요."
" 원래는 일반 기술자였는데, 이상한 일들이 잇따르면서 영업, 그리고 관리직으로 전향했어요. 관리직이 싫었고, 주식으로 큰돈을 벌었으니, "
"주식을 팔고 젊은 나이에 은퇴하려고 했어요. 하지만 그건 어리석은 선택이었어요. 너무 지루했거든요. 그래서 학위를 마치고 대학과 "
"고등학교에서 매장, 컴퓨터, 수학 같은 과목의 당직 교사로 일하기 시작했어요. 그냥 반 시간만 하고 나머지 시간은 야외에서 하이킹을 "
"하거나 그런 식으로 보냈어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr "정말 힘든 인생이군요. 가르쳐 줄 만한 유용한 기술이 좀 있을 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'd be happy to.  I can't spare a lot of free time, but for a little trade, "
"I'll tell you about whatever I can help with."
msgstr "기꺼이 도와드리겠습니다. 시간이 많지는 않지만, 작은 도움이라도 주시면 제가 도울 수 있는 모든 것을 알려드리겠습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting "
"outside."
msgstr "죄송하지만 지금은 그게 다예요. 다리우스가 밖에서 기다리고 있어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr "물론이죠. 무역에 관해 이야기해 보죠."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "명심하겠습니다. 여기서 뭘 한다고 하셨죠?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "고맙습니다. 생각해 보겠습니다. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr "그럴 수도 있겠지만 지금은 가야겠어요."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, can direct you to the free merchants and nearest FEMA camp.
#. ~ Random NPC, can be recruited away.
#. ~ Random NPC, demands heroin and can accept.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "refugee"
msgstr "피난민"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Please don't hurt us, we're just trying to get to safety."
msgstr "우리를 다치게 하지 마세요. 우리는 그저 안전하게 탈출하려고 하는 것뿐입니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "What's your situation here?"
msgstr "당신은 지금 어떤 상황에 처해 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I don't mean any harm.  I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I "
"wonder if you've heard anything about it?"
msgstr "악의는 없어요. 제가 찾고 있는 건 뭔가 이상한 건물이에요. 혹시 그 건물에 대해 들어보신 적 있으신가요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I don't have time for zombie bait like you."
msgstr "난 당신처럼 좀비 미끼에 시간 쓸 여유가 없어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "또 너야. 좋은 소식 있어? 오랜만에 듣는 소식인데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "또 너야. 좋은 소식 있어? 오랜만에 듣는 소식인데."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "또 너야. 좋은 소식 있어? 오랜만에 듣는 소식인데."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No, I don't have any."
msgstr "아니요, 하나도 없어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're just trying to find a safe place right now.  I think there's a FEMA "
"camp nearby that should have room for us."
msgstr "지금은 안전한 곳을 찾고 있는 중이에요. 근처에 FEMA 캠프가 있어서 거기에서 우리를 수용할 수 있을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Good luck with that.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "행운을 빌어요. <end_talking_leave>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The refugee nods "
"along"
msgstr "&당신은 최선을 다해 창고를 묘사합니다. 난민은 고개를 끄덕입니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ", then frowns.  \"Nope, not ringing any bells, sorry.\""
msgstr ", 그리고 눈살을 찌푸린다. \"아니요, 전혀 신경 안 쓰이겠네요. 죄송해요.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"Maybe, yeah.  I saw a weird building sort of like "
"that a while back, but we were on the move and couldn't stop to check it "
"out.\""
msgstr ", 생각에 잠긴 듯 말했다. \"어쩌면 그럴지도 몰라. 얼마 전에 그런 이상한 건물을 봤는데, 이동 중이라 가보지 못했어.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"Maybe, yeah.  I saw a weird building sort of like "
"that a while back, but we were on the move and couldn't stop to check it "
"out.\""
msgstr ", 생각에 잠긴 듯 말했다. \"어쩌면 그럴지도 몰라. 얼마 전에 그런 이상한 건물을 봤는데, 이동 중이라 가보지 못했어.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"Maybe, yeah.  I saw a weird building sort of like "
"that a while back, but we were on the move and couldn't stop to check it "
"out.\""
msgstr ", 생각에 잠긴 듯 말했다. \"어쩌면 그럴지도 몰라. 얼마 전에 그런 이상한 건물을 봤는데, 이동 중이라 가보지 못했어.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just "
"used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found"
" another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been "
"killed, all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all"
" the way to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us "
"there was no room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more "
"room and supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr ""
"우리는 같은 작은 대피소에 있었지만, 온통 엉망이었어요. 사용한 콘돔과 깨진 병, 벽에는 립스틱 자국이 잔뜩 남아 있었죠. 길에서 우리와"
" 같은 난민들을 또 만났는데, 모두 살해당하고 온몸이 갈기갈기 찢어져 있었고, 사방에 피가 낭자해 있었어요. 우리는 그들의 음식을 챙겨 "
"큰 난민 센터까지 갔는데, 총을 든 사람이 자리가 없다고 해서 FEMA 캠프로 가기로 했어요. 그곳에는 더 많은 공간과 물자가 있을 "
"거예요. 장담은 못 하지만, 기회는 있어요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to that FEMA camp?  I want to go there too if "
"it's so great."
msgstr "FEMA 캠프 가는 길 좀 알려줄 수 있어? 정말 좋으면 나도 가고 싶어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr "난민 센터에 가본 적이 없는데, 어디인지 알려주시겠어요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course, we're all in this together.  Let me mark that on your map."
msgstr "물론이죠, 우리 모두 함께 이겨내고 있습니다. 지도에 표시해 두겠습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the information.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "정보를 주셔서 감사합니다. <end_talking_leave>"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Things must be better at the camp…"
msgstr "캠프 상황은 나아질 거야…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "We're all in this together, looking forward to meeting you there."
msgstr "우리는 모두 함께 이겨내고 있으며, 그곳에서 여러분을 만나기를 기대합니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Everything is going to be all right."
msgstr "모든 것이 잘 될 거예요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No worries friend, good luck to you."
msgstr "걱정하지 마세요, 친구여. 행운을 빌어요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "The hard part is getting there."
msgstr "가장 어려운 부분은 그곳에 도달하는 것입니다."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Any progress on getting to the camp?"
msgstr "캠프에 도착하는 데 진전이 있나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Well, success I guess."
msgstr "글쎄, 성공이라고 할까요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Such a disappointment…"
msgstr "정말 실망스럽네요..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  I wouldn't bet they'll treat you any "
"differently than us though.  You might try and bring something to trade, "
"they like that."
msgstr ""
"여기, 지도에 표시해 둘게. 하지만 그들이 우리와 다르게 대할 거라고는 생각하지 않아. 뭔가 교환할 만한 걸 가져가는 건 어떨까? 그들은"
" 그걸 좋아하거든."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to where you're going too?  I love cartography."
msgstr "어디로 가는지 길 안내해 줄 수 있어? 지도 제작하는 거 좋아해."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Looking good there.  I like your whole setup.  What's your story?"
msgstr "좋아 보이네요. 전체적인 구성이 마음에 들어요. 어떤 이야기를 들려주셨나요?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nice.  Good to see you again.  What do you want from me?"
msgstr "좋아요. 다시 만나서 반가워요. 나한테 뭘 바라는 거예요?"

#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should come with me instead."
msgstr "대신 나와 함께 가세요."

#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should definitely come with me instead."
msgstr "당신은 반드시 나와 함께 가야 합니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nothing, just saying hi."
msgstr "아무것도 아니에요. 그냥 안부 인사를 하는 거예요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""
"저는 난민이지만 오해는 마세요. 이번 일을 계기로 정착해서 대가족을 꾸리는 게 제 꿈이에요. 딱 맞는 곳, 딱 맞는 사람을 찾아야 해요."
" 지난 몇 군데는 잘 안 됐거든요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""
"저는 난민이지만 오해는 마세요. 이번 일을 계기로 정착해서 대가족을 꾸리는 게 제 꿈이에요. 딱 맞는 곳, 딱 맞는 사람을 찾아야 해요."
" 지난 몇 군데는 잘 안 됐거든요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""
"저는 난민이지만 오해는 마세요. 이번 일을 계기로 정착해서 대가족을 꾸리는 게 제 꿈이에요. 딱 맞는 곳, 딱 맞는 사람을 찾아야 해요."
" 지난 몇 군데는 잘 안 됐거든요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "So you're not attached right now?"
msgstr "그럼 지금은 애착이 없는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Why, where were you before?"
msgstr "왜요? 전에는 어디에 계셨나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Not interested.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "관심없어요. <end_talking_leave>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"No, I'm not really with them.  We just got stuck together in the same messed"
" up evacuation place.  This one guy was really nice, but they wouldn't let "
"us stay.  They got there first so they told us we needed to find our own "
"place, but if we got anything they wanted they'd trade some of the stuff "
"they have.  I tried to talk them into helping but they were so cold to me."
msgstr ""
"아니, 난 그 사람들하고는 정말 안 어울려. 그냥 똑같은 엉망진창 대피소에 같이 갇힌 것뿐이야. 어떤 남자는 정말 친절했는데, 우리가 "
"머물게 해 주지 않았어. 그 사람들이 먼저 도착해서 우리끼리 숙소를 구하라고 했지만, 원하는 게 있으면 자기네가 가진 물건들을 좀 "
"바꿔주겠다고 했어. 도와주자고 설득해 봤지만, 너무 차갑게 굴었어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yeah, I guess it's hard all over.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "네, 아마 다 힘들겠죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "This is the beginning of a beautiful thing.  I'm with you."
msgstr "이건 아름다운 일의 시작이야. 나도 너와 함께야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr "응!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Actually, I think I'm on the right track here, but you might have some luck "
"finding a little something something back at the Free Merchant base.  They "
"seemed pretty desperate."
msgstr ""
"사실, 제 생각이 맞는 것 같아요. 하지만 자유 상인 기지에서 뭔가를 찾는 건 행운일지도 몰라요. 걔네들은 꽤 절박해 보이더라고요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course.  How do I get there?"
msgstr "물론입니다. 어떻게 가나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yes.  I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "네. 그럼 바로 출발할게요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Hey man.  Do you have any heroin?  I'm in a bit of a bind."
msgstr "야, 혹시 헤로인 있어? 나 좀 곤란해."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Never, that heroin is for me and me alone."
msgstr "절대 안 돼. 그 헤로인은 나만을 위한 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I think you might need it even more than me.  Here you go."
msgstr "저보다 더 필요할 것 같아요. 여기 있어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I love you."
msgstr "사랑해요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, uh, thanks.  I guess."
msgstr "아, 어, 고맙네요. 그럴 수도 있겠네요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No thank you."
msgstr "아니요, 괜찮습니다."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/missiondef_free_merchants.json
#: data/mods/classic_zombies/missiondef.json
msgid "Reach Refugee Center"
msgstr "피난시설에 도달"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Full"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr "피난민 센터의 이 거지는 최근에 무언가 먹을 것을 얻었습니다."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Reena Sandhu"
msgstr "레이나 산두"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Teacher"
msgstr "교사"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ All the beggars have been camping inside the evac shelter because they're
#. too weak and unskilled to make it on their own.
#. ~ This is the only beggar with some skills, sort of the leader.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
msgid "Beggar"
msgstr "거지"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"So, any luck with convincing the others to come on your crazy adventure yet?"
msgstr "아직 그 정신나간 여행에 동행할 사람을 찾지 못한 모양이지?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to say it after all you've done for me, but… I don't suppose "
"you've got anything to eat?"
msgstr "그렇게 날 도와줬는데 이렇게 말하기는 좀 미안하지만… 먹을 게 없는 것 같은데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to say it after all you've done for me, but… I don't suppose "
"you've got anything to eat?"
msgstr "그렇게 날 도와줬는데 이렇게 말하기는 좀 미안하지만… 먹을 게 없는 것 같은데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to say it after all you've done for me, but… I don't suppose "
"you've got anything to eat?"
msgstr "그렇게 날 도와줬는데 이렇게 말하기는 좀 미안하지만… 먹을 게 없는 것 같은데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Thank you again.  I really appreciate the food."
msgstr "먹을 것 정말 고마워."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Please, help me.  I need food.  Aren't you their sheriff?  Can't you help "
"me?"
msgstr "제발, 도와줘. 음식이 필요해. 그, 보안관은 아니지? 도와줄 수 있어?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food."
msgstr "제발 도와줘. 음식 좀 나눠줘."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid ""
"I've talked to the others, and they're all willing to come.  So, you joining"
" us?"
msgstr "다른 사람들에게 말해봤는데, 수락했어. 너도 같이 갈래?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Hey, here, I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "자, 여기. 음식 가져왔어. 확인해봐."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Get away from me."
msgstr "나한테서 떨어져."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"They won't let me in.  They say they're too full.  I'm allowed to camp out "
"here as long as I keep it clean and don't make a fuss"
msgstr "안 들여보내 줘요. 너무 꽉 찼대요. 깨끗하게 관리하고 소란 피우지 않으면 여기서 캠핑해도 돼요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ", but I'm reduced to begging to survive."
msgstr ", 하지만 나는 살아남기 위해 애원할 수밖에 없게 되었습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ", but I'm so hungry."
msgstr ", 하지만 너무 배고파요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Why don't you scavenge your own food?"
msgstr "직접 음식을 찾아보는 게 어때?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "음식 가져왔어. 확인해봐."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I've got some more food, if you want it."
msgstr "음식 더 있는데."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr "미안, 도와줄 수 없어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
msgid "Thank you so much."
msgstr "정말 고마워."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Can I ask you something else first?"
msgstr "다른 거 먼저 물어봐도 될까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I was wrong.  I can't help you."
msgstr "미안, 도와줄 수 없을 것 같아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "Here, you can have this <topic_item>."
msgstr "여기서 <topic_item>을 사용할 수 있습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."
msgstr "정말 최고야. 고마워."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "문제없습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Where else?  I can't fight those things out there.  I'm in terrible physical"
" condition, don't have any useful skills, and I'm terrified of <zombies> and"
" violence.  How am I supposed to find a safe place?"
msgstr ""
"그밖에 어디? 저 밖에서는 싸울 수 없어. 몸도 형편없고, 쓸 만한 기술도 없고, <zombies>의 두려움과 폭력에 시달릴거야. 어떻게"
" 하면 안전한 장소를 찾을 수 있겠어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better "
"than living here."
msgstr "나랑 같이 가자. 모험을 즐기는 성격은 아닌 것 같지만 적어도 여기서 사는 것보다는 더 나을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  You could come there.  There "
"aren't many people left, we could use anyone regardless of skills."
msgstr "이 주변에 내 캠프가 있어. 거기로 오는건 어때? 요즘은 남아있는 사람이 얼마 없으니 능력은 신경쓰지 않고 모으고 있거든."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, "
"people who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances "
"begging for scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make "
"room for me, thanks."
msgstr ""
"바깥으로 가자고?  죽으라는 거야?  바깥으로 나갔던 사람들은 돌아오지 않고 있어.  나와는 달리 혼자서 살아남을 수 있었던 사람들이."
"  차라리 여기서 고철이나 음식을 구걸하다가 저 안쪽 놈들이 들여보내줄지도 모른다는 희망에 걸래.  미안."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe you can't scavenge, but we "
"can use any warm bodies that can lift a tool.  You'd be safer and better fed"
" there."
msgstr ""
"이 주변에 내 캠프가 있어. 네가 쓸만한 물품을 찾으러 다니는 건 못하겠지만 우리는 일단 도구를 들 수 있을 손만 있으면 환영이거든. "
"여기보다는 안전하고 잘 먹을 걸."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I was a high school math teacher.  It was a good job, I loved it.  Funny "
"enough, it's not super applicable after the end of the world.  I mean, at "
"some point people are going to need a teacher again, but right now they just"
" want food, shelter, and clothing."
msgstr ""
"나는 고등학교 수학 선생님이었어. 좋은 일이었지, 난 그게 좋았어. 우습게도, 세상이 끝난 후에는 적용이 불가능해. 내 말은, 어떤 때는"
" 사람들이 다시 선생님이 필요하겠지만, 지금은 그저 음식, 쉼터, 그리고 옷을 원할 뿐이야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe they can't use your skills "
"here, but I could."
msgstr "이 주변에 내 캠프가 있어. 저 사람들은 네 기술을 알아보지 못한 모양이지만 나는 네 기술을 쓸 수 있어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"That's a kind offer of you, but I think I'd rather take my chances here than"
" risking it out there again.  I remember <the_cataclysm>, I'm not in any "
"hurry to face that again."
msgstr ""
"친절한 제안이네. 그렇지만 여기를 나가는 리스크를 고려해서 다시 생각해봐야겠어. <the_cataclysm>이 펼쳐졌던 날을 아직 "
"기억하고 있어. 그리고 그걸 다시 직면할 용기가 아직 없어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"That's quite the offer, but I don't think I'd survive the trip.  I don't "
"think you realize how useless I am in this world."
msgstr "괜찮은 제안이네. 하지만 가는 동안 살아남을 자신이 없어. 내가 얼마나 쓸모없는 사람인지 아직 모르는 것 같네."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I'm too hungry to make a big decision like that."
msgstr "미안, 너무 배가 고파서 그런 결정을 내릴 힘도 없어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I can keep you safe.  I'll take you there myself."
msgstr "내가 지켜줄게. 안전하게 데려다 줄 수 있어."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I really appreciate everything you've done for me, but I don't think you get"
" it.  I can't go out there.  I will die.  I know it's horrible camping out "
"here, but I just can't face that nightmare again."
msgstr ""
"네가 날 도와준 건 정말 기쁘지만 아직 제대로 이해를 못한 것 같네. 난 나갈 수 없어. 난 죽고 말 거야. 그 악몽을 다시 겪을 수는 "
"없다구."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I hope you'll reconsider eventually.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "결국 다시 생각해 보시기를 바랍니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to"
" provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"음… 그래, 보아하니 넌 저 밖에서도 살아남을 수 있고 음식도 가져다줄 수 있는 것 같네. 여기 있는 우리 모두보다 더 잘 살고 있는 것"
" 같고. 하지만, 여기 내 친구들을 버리고는 아무데도 가지 않을 거야. 오랫동안 같이 지냈거든. 루오, 브랜든, 유스케가 가겠다고 하면 "
"나도 갈게."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to"
" provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"음… 그래, 보아하니 넌 저 밖에서도 살아남을 수 있고 음식도 가져다줄 수 있는 것 같네. 여기 있는 우리 모두보다 더 잘 살고 있는 것"
" 같고. 하지만, 여기 내 친구들을 버리고는 아무데도 가지 않을 거야. 오랫동안 같이 지냈거든. 루오, 브랜든, 유스케가 가겠다고 하면 "
"나도 갈게."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to"
" provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"음… 그래, 보아하니 넌 저 밖에서도 살아남을 수 있고 음식도 가져다줄 수 있는 것 같네. 여기 있는 우리 모두보다 더 잘 살고 있는 것"
" 같고. 하지만, 여기 내 친구들을 버리고는 아무데도 가지 않을 거야. 오랫동안 같이 지냈거든. 루오, 브랜든, 유스케가 가겠다고 하면 "
"나도 갈게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "알겠습니다. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK, I'll talk to them too."
msgstr "그래. 걔네들에게도 말해볼게."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "All right!  <lets_go>"
msgstr "좋아! <lets_go>"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Schizophrenic beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Dino Dave"
msgstr "디노 데이브"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We've done it!  We've solved the list!"
msgstr "해냈어! 리스트를 다 채웠다고!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"How's things with you?  My cardboard collection is getting quite impressive."
msgstr "이거 어때? 내 판지 컬렉션 정말 쩔지 않아?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Have I told you about cardboard, friend?  Do you have any?"
msgstr "내가 너에게 판지가 있나고 물었나, 친구? 가지고있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "About that shopping list of yours…"
msgstr "그 쇼핑 리스트 말인데…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr "도와줄 일이 있을까?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What are you going to do with all that cardboard now?"
msgstr "판지 가지고 도대체 뭐하고 있는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"We've done it, Dave!  Smokes says you can build yourself a house up on the "
"roof if you want.  You've got to keep it nice and clean, and help out the "
"people down here by looking out for zombies, but you can still use the "
"washrooms and things downstairs when you need to.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""
"데이브, 우리 해냈어! 스모크스가 네가 원한다면 옥상에 집을 지을 수 있다고 했어. 집을 깨끗하게 유지하고, 좀비를 조심해서 아래층 "
"사람들을 도와야 해. 하지만 필요하면 아래층 화장실 같은 건 계속 쓸 수 있어. 어떻게 생각해?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Cardboard?"
msgstr "판지?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why are you sitting out here?"
msgstr "왜 여기 앉아 있어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Are you seriously wearing a dinosaur costume?"
msgstr "지금 진지하게 공룡 의상을 입고 있는 거야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Do you need something to eat?"
msgstr "먹을 거 필요해?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh nice.  Crunchings and munchings.  That's a cool, a cool thing."
msgstr "좋지. 쩝쩝우물우물. 아주 좋아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr "응. 정말 배가 고파. 저놈들은 음식에 약물을 넣어놓지. 넌 그런 부류는 아닌 것 같아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr "응. 정말 배가 고파. 저놈들은 음식에 약물을 넣어놓지. 넌 그런 부류는 아닌 것 같아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr "응. 정말 배가 고파. 저놈들은 음식에 약물을 넣어놓지. 넌 그런 부류는 아닌 것 같아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I can tell when it has stuff in it, it's got a sandy texture.  But this "
"doesn't.  Thanks again."
msgstr "물건이 들어 있었을 때에는 까슬까슬하던데 이건 그렇지는 않네. 고마워."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "문제없습니다."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I'm building a house out of cardboard.  The sandman doesn't want me to, but "
"I told him to go fuck himself."
msgstr "나는 판지로 집을 짓고 있어. 잠귀신은 집을 짓는 걸 별로 안 좋아하는 눈치던데, 뭐 좆까라지."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why cardboard?"
msgstr "왜 판지야?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "The sandman?"
msgstr "잠귀신?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Would you like me to give you some cardboard?"
msgstr "판지 좀 줄까?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me "
"safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it "
"hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further"
" damage."
msgstr ""
"여기저기 널려있고, 좀비들이 무서워하는 물건이니까. 그 덕에 지금까지 난 안전했던 거고. 좀비의 중심으로부터 나오는 베타선은 판지를 뚫지"
" 못하고, 판지는 베타선을 반사해 피해를 입지 않게 되지."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Kind of a question's that?  Yeah man, you got cardboard, I got a whole… a "
"whole shopping list.  Got it here."
msgstr "그걸 말이라고! 당연하지 친구. 넌 판지가 있고, 난 쇼핑 리스트가 있지. 이거 받아."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What's next on the list?"
msgstr "리스트에 적힌 다음 물건은 뭔데?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If you don't know who he is, I definitely can't tell you.  He talks to "
"everyone, if you didn't hear him that means you can't be trusted, except to "
"help me out."
msgstr ""
"잠귀신이 뭔지 모른다고? 그러면 말해도 소용없지. 누구에게나 다 잠귀신이 말을 속삭이고 있는데 넌 듣지 못한다는 건, 흠, 넌 믿을 수 "
"없다는 뜻이지. 날 도와주고 있긴 하지만."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "…<done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "…<완료된 대화 섹션>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These cowards are afraid of me.  They won't let me into their base.  I'm "
"going to build my new house and I won't let them in."
msgstr "이 겁쟁이들은 나를 무서워해. 그들은 나를 그들의 근거지로 들여보내지 않을 거야. 새 집을 지을 건데 들여보내지 않을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "You said you were building a house?"
msgstr "집을 짓는다고?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I… I can see you wearing it.  Why are you wearing that?"
msgstr "내가 보기에는 입고 있는 것 같은데. 왜 그런 걸 입어?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What was that about cardboard?"
msgstr "판지에 관한 건 뭐야?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"You ask me what I can see, but I don't tell you what you see.  Sometimes we "
"have shields up, to protect ourselves."
msgstr "네가 보기엔 그렇겠지. 내가 보기엔 좀 다르고. 서로를 보호하기 위해서는 보호막 같은 게 있어야 마땅하니."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Well… I had it all pretty together, "
msgstr "글쎄요... 저는 모든 것을 꽤 잘 해냈어요."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "but the others have left, and "
msgstr "하지만 다른 사람들은 떠났고"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "and I feel bad with all the help you've given me already, but "
msgstr "그리고 당신이 이미 나에게 준 모든 도움에 대해 기분이 나쁘긴 하지만,"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"now the masters won't let me build my sanctuary.  I know I can't build it in"
" here, they wouldn't allow it.  They won't listen to me when I ask for a "
"safe place.  They just want me to disappear, like the others.  Can you help "
"me figure them out?"
msgstr ""
"이제 주인들이 제 성소를 짓는 걸 허락하지 않아요. 여기엔 지을 수 없다는 걸 알아요. 허락하지 않을 거예요. 제가 안전한 곳을 달라고 "
"해도 들어주지 않아요. 다른 사람들처럼 그냥 사라지길 바라는 거예요. 어떻게 해야 할지 알아내는 걸 도와줄 수 있나요?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Why don't you leave this place?  Come with me, I could use some help out "
"there."
msgstr "여기를 왜 떠나지 않는 거야? 나랑 함께 가자. 내가 좀 도와줄 수 있어."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you "
"a place to go."
msgstr "물론이죠, 데이브. 마지막으로 부탁 하나 드릴게요. 스모크스한테 가서 네가 갈 곳을 찾아달라고 부탁할 수 있을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on that, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "그건 좀 생각해 봐야겠어, 데이브. 난 이미 많은 일을 했거든."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  I can hardly believe it!  This will be a "
"nicer house than I had before everything went funny.  I can watch out, I'm "
"happy to do that.  And it'll be nice to still have a bathroom!  Come see me "
"there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"지붕! 정말 높아! 정말 높아! 믿기지가 않아! 모든 게 이상해지기 전보다 훨씬 멋진 집이 될 거야. 조심할 수 있어. 난 기꺼이 할게."
" 그리고 욕실도 아직 있으면 좋겠어! 친구야, 거기로 와 봐. 절대 실망시키지 않을 거야."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll see you on the rooftop.  Good luck, Dave."
msgstr "옥상에서 만나요. 행운을 빌어요, 데이브."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"No!  I just got everything together.  I am not leaving, not now.  "
"Everything's finally coming together!"
msgstr "안 돼! 이제 막 모든 걸 정리했단 말야. 난 떠나지 않아,  지금은. 드디어 모든 게 잘 풀리고 있어!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about "
"finding you a place to go."
msgstr "좋아요, 그럼 데이브. 마지막으로 부탁 하나 드릴게요. 스모크스한테 네가 갈 곳을 찾아달라고 부탁할 수 있을 것 같아요."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on it, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "생각해 봐야겠어요, 데이브. 이미 많은 일을 했거든요."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgstr "작은 종이상자 40개 가져오기"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em."
msgstr "시작은 사소한 것부터 해야지, 응? 작은 것들은 그것대로 작은 것들을 안전하게 보관하는데 쓸모가 있어. 늘 유용하지."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em.  I need a bunch of 'em.  Little ones, you know?  Can you "
"bring me like… like… forty?"
msgstr ""
"시작은 사소한 것부터 해야지, 응? 작은 것들은 그것대로 작은 것들을 안전하게 보관하는데 쓸모가 있어. 늘 유용하지. 그러니 잔뜩 있어야"
" 해. 작은 것들 말야, 너도 알지? 어, 대충, 음, 40개쯤… 가져다줄래?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much my friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "이런 세상에, 정말 고마워, 친구. 후회하지 않을거야."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I didn't think so."
msgstr "그렇게 생각하지 않았어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Watch out, he's looking for it too."
msgstr "조심해, 그놈도 그걸 찾고 있으니까."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Got the little ones yet?"
msgstr "작은 것들 가져왔어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh this is so great, so great!"
msgstr "오 이거 굉장해, 굉장해!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad.  Guess they're eating it all."
msgstr "오 유감이야. 놈들이 다 먹어치웠나봐."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgstr "접착 테이프(200) 가져오기"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them"
" together.  Surround them, light side, dark side."
msgstr "좋아. 참 좋아. 그치만 뭔가, 응, 서로 합쳐줄게, 있어야 해. 감싸, 밝은 쪽, 어두운 쪽."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them"
" together.  Surround them, light side, dark side.  Bring me the Force!"
msgstr "좋아. 참 좋아. 그치만 뭔가, 응, 서로 합쳐줄게, 있어야 해. 감싸, 밝은 쪽, 어두운 쪽. 포스가 필요해!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "It's all around us… but did you get it in a crude matter form?"
msgstr "우리 주변에 가득해… 근데 그거 혹시 좀 조잡하지 않아?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgstr "골판지 상자 10개를 가져오세요"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well."
msgstr "더 큰 놈을 열 개 가져와줘. 목록은 거짓말하지 않아. 지금까지 잘해주고 있어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well.  I "
"got a little more on the list, but we're more than half there."
msgstr ""
"더 큰 놈을 열 개 가져와줘. 목록은 거짓말 하지 않아. 지금까지 잘해주고 있어. 목록이 조금 늘어나긴 했지만, 벌써 절반이나 왔어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Any luck?  Bigger ones?"
msgstr "어때? 큰 놈 가져왔어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'm so happy now!"
msgstr "행복해라!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgstr "큰 비닐 시트 10개 가져오기"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so "
"I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger."
msgstr ""
"여기에 설치할 수 있으면 필요 없겠지만, 저 녀석들에게 내쫓길 수도 있으니까, 혹시 모르니까 플라스틱이 필요할 것 같아. 마음에 안 "
"들어. 잠귀신은 플라스틱을 통해서 냄새를 맡을 수 있는데. 판지가 더 튼튼할 것 같아."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so "
"I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger.  Please bring "
"me some plastic sheets."
msgstr ""
"여기에 설치할 수 있으면 필요 없겠지만, 저 녀석들에게 내쫓길 수도 있으니까, 혹시 모르니까 플라스틱이 필요할 것 같아. 마음에 안 "
"들어. 잠귀신은 플라스틱을 통해서 냄새를 맡을 수 있는데. 판지가 더 튼튼할 것 같아. 플라스틱 판 좀 가져와줘."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We're almost there, now."
msgstr "이제 거의 다왔어."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "They keep a lot of this stuff in hardware stores and lumber yards."
msgstr "철물점이나 목재 판매점에 많아."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I really feel bad sending you on this one, it's dangerous.  Have you found "
"anything?"
msgstr "널 이번 일로 보내게 되어 정말 유감이야. 위험하거든. 뭐 좀 찾았어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Nice, this will do perfectly!"
msgstr "좋아, 이제 완벽해질 거야!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad."
msgstr "그거 참 안됐군."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgstr "대형 종이상자 5개 가져오기"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other "
"parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me"
" five more really big cardboard boxes?"
msgstr ""
"마지막으로 해줬으면 하는 일이 있어. 다른 부품들은 내가 직접 수거해 왔는데, 판지가 많아져서 더 쉬워졌어. 엄청나게 큰 골판지 상자 "
"다섯 개만 더 가져다 줄 수 있니?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other "
"parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me"
" five more really big cardboard boxes?  Five more cardboard boxes, as big as"
" it gets.  I have a few already stored up, that should be all I need."
msgstr ""
"마지막으로 해줬으면 하는 일이 있어. 다른 부품들은 내가 직접 수거해 왔는데, 판지가 많아져서 더 쉬워졌어. 엄청나게 큰 골판지 상자 "
"다섯 개만 더 가져다 줄 수 있니? 골판지 상자 다섯 개. 최대한 큰 걸로. 이미 몇 개쯤 비축해놨는데 그것만 더 있으면 돼."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Yes!  The home stretch!"
msgstr "좋았어! 확장 공사다!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, but we're so close!"
msgstr "아으, 거의 다 끝났는데!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Try looking in cargo storage areas."
msgstr "창고 같은 데를 찾아봐."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you bring me those last few boxes?"
msgstr "마지막 상자들 가져왔어?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Brilliant!  You're a true hero.  I'll see if I can find a place to set these"
" up now."
msgstr "굉장해! 넌 진짜 영웅이야. 이 것들을 둘 장소를 찾아볼게."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No!  Oh god, no, this can't be happening…"
msgstr "안돼! 신이시여, 안돼, 이럴 수는 없어…"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
msgstr "스모크스와 대화해서 데이브에게 집이라고 부를 수 있는 곳을 찾아주세요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me."
msgstr ""
"다 가지고 있어요. 다 가지고 있는데, 어디에 둘지 모르겠어요. 스승님께 여쭤보시겠어요? 혹시? 시도는 해봤지만 무시당하셔요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me.  I just need a place to"
" put it all, a place I can be safe, and not make anyone upset."
msgstr ""
"다 가지고 있어요. 다 가지고 있는데, 어디 둘 곳이 없어요. 스승님께 여쭤볼래요? 혹시? 해봤는데 무시당해요. 그냥 다 넣어둘 곳이 "
"필요해요. 안전하게 지낼 수 있고, 아무도 화나게 하지 않을 곳이요."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Thank you!  I'm sorry, I thought we were done, but we can do this!"
msgstr "감사합니다! 죄송해요, 다 끝난 줄 알았는데, 할 수 있을 것 같아요!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Maybe somewhere they can't see me?  Where I can just be me?"
msgstr "어쩌면 그들이 날 볼 수 없는 어딘가? 내가 그냥 나일 수 있는 그런 곳?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you ask the masters?"
msgstr "스승님께 물어보셨나요?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not "
"disappoint you."
msgstr "지붕! 정말 높아! 정말 높아! 친구야, 거기로 와 봐. 실망시키지 않을 거야."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Power Storage CBM"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/missiondef.json
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr "이해가 안되는군."

#. ~ Name of effect type id "insulted_luo"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Insulted"
msgstr "모욕당함"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Insulted"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh, you went there."
msgstr "거기 갔다왔구만."

