#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid ""
"The rate is a bit steep, but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill."
"  The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  "
"I'll need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."
msgstr ""
"요금이 좀 비싼 편이지만, 아직 채워야 할 할당량이 남아 있습니다. 통나무는 캠프 입구 차고에 놓을 예정입니다. 다음 짐을 실어 나르려면"
" 시간이 좀 걸릴 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[800 merch, 1d] 10 logs"
msgstr "[800 머크, 1d] 통나무 10개"

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "<npc_name> drops the logs off in the garage…"
msgstr "<npc_name>이 차고에 통나무를 내려놓았습니다…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[4800 merch, 7d] 100 logs"
msgstr "[머크 4800개, 7d] 통나무 100개"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "<end_talking_later> <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "<end_talking_later> <end_talking_bye>"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Woodworker"
msgstr "목공예가"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Don't have much time to talk."
msgstr "떠들 시간이 많지 않아."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid ""
"I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  "
"Maintaining the saw is a chore, but breaks the monotony."
msgstr ""
"노동자들이 가져온 통나무를 재목으로 만들어 전초기지를 확장합니다. 톱을 관리하는 건 귀찮은 일이지만, 단조로움을 깨는 일이죠."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid ""
"Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled, so "
"I'd be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most "
"people could use a hand."
msgstr ""
"통나무 운반은 비숙련자에게 맡길 수 있는 몇 안 되는 작업 중 하나라서, 제가 외주를 준다면 그들에게 손해가 될 겁니다. 하지만 주변 "
"사람들에게 물어보세요. 아마 대부분의 사람들이 도움이 필요할 거예요."

#. ~ Signage placed on map
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "Clinic"
msgstr "진료소"

#. ~ Signage placed on map
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
msgid "Extra Supplies.  Take what you need."
msgstr "추가 물품. 필요한 만큼 가져가세요."

#. ~ Signage placed on map
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
msgid "Scavenger Storage.  Stay out!"
msgstr "쓰레기 보관소. 들어오지 마세요!"

#. ~ Signage placed on map
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
msgid ""
"Your name is crudely scribbled on the sign with 'Not for commune use' below "
"it."
msgstr "당신의 이름은 '공동체 사용 금지'라는 문구와 함께 간판에 거칠게 휘갈겨 쓰여 있습니다."

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dana is a young woman who survived with her husband, but she was pregnant
#. and lost the baby.  This class def is for after she moves to Tacoma.
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "baker"
msgstr "빵 굽는 사람"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"*stands in the middle of a cramped kitchen, covered in flour.  The scene "
"looks reminiscent of easier times, but the illusion is broken as he apron "
"shifts to reveal a heavy machete and holstered pistol on  her belt.  She "
"looks up as you approach, then beams in recognition.  \"Welcome to Dana's "
"Bakery, stranger!\"  She laughs brightly.  \"Glad you made out this way.  "
"What can I do for you?\""
msgstr ""
"*밀가루가 흩뿌려진 비좁은 부엌 한가운데 서 있다. 그 모습은 마치 예전의 여유로운 시절을 떠올리게 하지만, 그의 앞치마가 움직이며 "
"허리띠에 묵직한 마체테와 권총집이 달린 권총을 차고 있는 모습이 드러나면서 그 환상은 깨진다. 당신이 다가가자 그녀는 고개를 들더니, "
"알아보고는 활짝 웃는다. \"다나의 빵집에 오신 걸 환영합니다, 낯선 분이시군요!\" 그녀는 환하게 웃으며 말한다. \"이렇게 만나서 "
"반갑네요. 뭘 도와드릴까요?\""

