#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid "Dear Diary, I was at the park today with Percy…"
msgstr "일기장에게, 나는 오늘 퍼시와 함께 공원에 갔어요..."

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Dear Diary, I was at the park today with Percy.  Danny always told me that"
" she was very sad when her dog died, so I broke Percy's neck because I "
"wanted to see how I'd feel.  I think I was sad for a little, but I kept "
"playing with him but I had to stop after too many pieces fell off and Percy "
"became gross.  I buried him in the park so mom and dad wouldn't find out, "
"but Mr. Luca and Mrs Annaliese saw me.  I'm scared they'll tell on me.  "
"Daddy thinks I don't know where he keeps the keys to his gun safe.\""
msgstr ""
"\"일기장에게, 오늘 퍼시랑 공원에서 놀았어. 대니는 퍼시네 개가 죽어서 퍼시가 속상하다고 알려줬는데 그게 뭔지 알고 싶어서 퍼시의 목을"
" 부러트렸어. 나도 퍼시처럼 속상했지만 퍼시랑 같이 노니깐 기분이 좋았어. 그런데 갑자기 퍼시의 팔이 떨어져서 징그러워서 퍼시랑 그만 "
"놀았어. 엄마 아빠가 모르게 퍼시를 공원에 묻어줬지만 루카 아저씨랑 아넬리제 아줌마가 날 봤어. 엄마 아빠에게 말할까봐 무서워. 하지만 "
"아빠는 내가 총 금고 열쇠가 어딨는지 모른다고 생각하겠지?\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Dear diary.  Mommy and dad have been making us live in the basement for "
"the last few days.  It's to keep us safe, they say, but it gets really "
"stuffy during the night and I can't sleep, so I sometimes sneak upstairs.  "
"Sometimes I talk to Aunt Maria.  She always stays in the back yard and "
"appears when the sky goes all weird and when scary noises come from outside."
"  I always ask her to come in, but she tells me she can't and that I should "
"go out instead.  I think it's because dad doesn't want her around, he always"
" told me she died in 2001.  He's a liar, and I think he wants the monsters "
"to eat her.  The door's always locked, but I can reach the garage "
"controls.\""
msgstr ""
"\"사랑하는 일기장아. 엄마 아빠가 며칠 동안 우리를 지하실에서 살게 하셨어요. 우리를 안전하게 지키기 위해서라고 하시지만, 밤에는 너무"
" 답답해서 잠이 안 와서 가끔 몰래 위층으로 올라가요. 가끔은 마리아 이모랑도 이야기해요. 이모는 항상 뒷마당에 계시다가 하늘이 이상하게"
" 변하고 밖에서 무서운 소리가 들릴 때 나타나세요. 저는 항상 이모에게 들어오라고 하지만, 이모는 안 된다며 나가라고 하세요. 아마 "
"아빠가 이모를 싫어하시는 것 같아요. 아빠는 항상 이모가 2001년에 돌아가셨다고 하셨어요. 아빠는 거짓말쟁이시고, 괴물들이 이모를 "
"잡아먹기를 바라시는 것 같아요. 문은 항상 잠겨 있지만, 차고 조종 장치에는 손이 닿아요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"I saw Mr. Henderson today, but he didn't say hi back.  His eyes were all "
"white and he didn't have his glasses on.  He just stood there in the yard "
"staring at the sky.\""
msgstr ""
"\"오늘 헨더슨 씨를 봤는데, 인사도 안 하셨어요. 눈은 하얗게 질려 있었고 안경도 안 쓰고 계셨어요. 그냥 마당에 서서 하늘만 쳐다보고"
" 계셨죠.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Mommy says we're going to grandma's house, but grandma lives in heaven.  "
"I'm confused.\""
msgstr "\"엄마는 우리가 할머니 댁에 간다고 하셨는데, 할머니는 천국에 사세요. 헷갈려요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Daddy told me to hide in the closet, but it's been forever and he hasn't "
"come back yet.  I'm really scared.\""
msgstr "\"아빠가 옷장에 숨으라고 하셨는데, 시간이 엄청 지났는데도 아빠가 아직 안 오셨어요. 너무 무서워요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Mommy locked me in the attic and said not to come out, but I can hear "
"strange noises downstairs.\""
msgstr "\"엄마가 나를 다락방에 가두고 나오지 말라고 하셨는데, 아래층에서 이상한 소리가 들려요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"I miss my friends.  I wonder if they are okay.  I hope I can see them "
"soon.\""
msgstr "\"친구들이 보고 싶어요. 잘 지내고 계시는지 궁금해요. 곧 만날 수 있으면 좋겠어요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Daddy said he will be right back, but it's been a whole day.  I hope he is"
" okay.\""
msgstr "\"아빠는 곧 돌아올 거라고 하셨는데, 하루 종일 걸렸어요. 아빠가 괜찮으시길 바라요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"I found an old photo of us at the beach.  I miss those days.  Why can't we"
" go back?\""
msgstr "\"해변에서 찍은 우리 옛 사진을 찾았어. 그때가 그리워. 왜 돌아갈 수 없는 거야?\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
msgid ""
"\"Mommy said the monsters are not real, but I saw one today.  It was in our "
"backyard.\""
msgstr "\"엄마는 괴물이 진짜가 아니라고 하셨는데, 오늘 괴물을 하나 봤어요. 우리 뒷마당에 있었어요.\""

#. ~ Snippet in category "note_child"
#. ~ The grammar and punctuation mistakes are there on purpose 9/10 times.
#. Keep in mind that those notes are supposed to be written by primary-school-
#. level children.
#: data/json/snippets/children_notes.json
