"You have a nightmare in which you walk through a river of blood, followed by"
" the dead you tried to leave behind."
msgstr "당신은 피의 강을 걸어가는 악몽을 꾸는데, 그 뒤를 당신이 뒤에 남겨두려고 했던 죽은 사람들이 따라옵니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream of slime, jiggling, wobbling, and oozing over your entire body.  "
"As you wipe at it, the flesh of your hand smears away."
msgstr "온몸에 끈적끈적한 액체가 출렁거리고, 흔들리고, 흘러내리는 꿈을 꿉니다. 그것을 닦는 순간, 손의 살이 번져 나갑니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream of standing on the Eiffel Tower, watching Paris burn.  You're too "
"far above to make out who is still alive and who isn't, though you hear the "
"screams."
msgstr ""
"에펠탑에 서서 불타는 파리를 바라보는 꿈을 꿉니다. 너무 높아서 누가 살아 있고 누가 죽었는지조차 알 수 없지만, 비명 소리는 들립니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream of a beautiful garden full of strange plants that defend you "
"against the undead.  When they've finished, their barbed tendrils turn on "
"you, paralyzing and restraining you until you wake screaming."
msgstr ""
"당신은 언데드로부터 당신을 지켜줄 기묘한 식물들로 가득한 아름다운 정원을 꿈꿉니다. 그들이 끝내면, 가시 돋친 덩굴손이 당신을 향해 "
"돌아서서 마비시키고 속박합니다. 당신은 비명을 지르며 깨어날 때까지 말이죠."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream that you're a time traveler.  You go back to tell your past self "
"about the horrors to come, but after hours of pleading, you just won't "
"listen."
msgstr ""
"당신은 시간 여행자가 되는 꿈을 꿉니다. 과거의 자신에게 다가올 끔찍한 일들에 대해 이야기하러 돌아가지만, 몇 시간 동안 애원해도 듣지 "
"않습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You have a nightmare about fighting for days against a warrior clad in bone "
"armor.  Teeth clatter gently, woven into their hair.  When finally you are "
"defeated, the warrior removes their mask, but you wake before seeing their "
"face."
msgstr ""
"뼈 갑옷을 입은 전사와 며칠 동안 싸우는 악몽을 꿉니다. 이빨이 부드럽게 부딪히며 전사의 머리카락에 얽힙니다. 마침내 패배했을 때, "
"전사는 가면을 벗지만, 당신은 전사의 얼굴을 보기도 전에 깨어납니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream you are a slug, and all is well until a child stands over you with"
" a salt shaker."
msgstr "당신은 달팽이가 되는 꿈을 꾸었고, 어린아이가 소금통을 들고 당신 위에 서기 전까지는 모든 것이 괜찮았습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream you're walking in the woods.  There's no one around and your phone"
" is dead.  That's when you spot him."
msgstr "숲 속을 걷는 꿈을 꿉니다. 주변에는 아무도 없고 휴대폰도 꺼져 있습니다. 그때 그를 발견합니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a nightmare of being slowly devoured, starting with your toes."
msgstr "당신은 발가락부터 시작해 천천히 잡아먹히는 악몽에서 깨어납니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a nightmare of being torn to pieces, lying in the filth of the"
" road and waiting for the end."
msgstr "당신은 찢어지고 길바닥에 누워 끝이 오기를 기다리는 악몽에서 깨어납니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"A seemingly endless nightmare plagues you.  Years pass, and you are always "
"struggling alone in an unforgiving world, dying in solitude of old age."
msgstr ""
"끝없이 이어지는 악몽이 당신을 괴롭힙니다. 세월이 흐르고, 당신은 늘 험난한 세상에서 홀로 고군분투하며, 늙어 외롭게 죽어갑니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream that you are the last person on Earth.  You're surrounded by "
"\"people\" but you know they aren't human anymore."
msgstr ""
"당신은 지구상의 마지막 인간이 된 꿈을 꿉니다. 주변에는 \"사람들\"이 있지만, 그들이 더 이상 인간이 아니라는 걸 알고 있습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a nightmare in which you endlessly stacked boxes in a factory,"
" overseen by an inhuman figure clothed in shadow."
msgstr ""
"당신은 공장에 끝없이 상자를 쌓아 올리는 악몽에서 깨어났는데, 그 공장은 그림자로 뒤덮인 비인간적인 인물의 감독을 받고 있었습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream of a behemoth, towering over you and covered in bony tissue, its "
"face twisted with rage.  You run for as long as you can, but when its "
"massive fist comes down, you wake."
msgstr ""
"당신은 거대한 괴물이 당신 위로 우뚝 솟아 뼈로 뒤덮인 채 분노로 일그러진 얼굴을 한 채 꿈에 등장합니다. 최대한 멀리 도망치려 하지만,"
" 거대한 주먹이 내려오는 순간 당신은 깨어납니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream of a beautiful and regal unicorn.  You feed it gems as it nuzzles "
"your hand.  When you run out of stones, it kicks you to death."
msgstr ""
"당신은 아름답고 위엄 있는 유니콘을 꿈꿉니다. 유니콘이 당신의 손을 어루만지며 보석을 먹여줍니다. 돌이 다 떨어지면 유니콘은 당신을 발로"
" 차 죽입니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a nightmare in which it had all started over again, 911 "
"ringing busy, the fires, and death in every street."
msgstr ""
"당신은 모든 것이 다시 시작된 악몽에서 깨어났습니다. 911에 전화가 바쁘게 울리고, 화재가 발생하고, 모든 거리에서 죽음이 "
"일어났습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream your boss is scolding you for allowing a zombie through security."
msgstr "당신은 좀비가 보안 검색대를 통과하도록 허용한 것에 대해 상사가 당신을 꾸짖는 꿈을 꿉니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You dream that you're a meal delivery worker, delivering a slab of flesh and"
" some sodas to a zombie house party."
msgstr "당신은 좀비 하우스 파티에 살점과 소다를 배달하는 식사 배달원이 되는 꿈을 꿉니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a nightmare just as your plane crashes.  You remember screams,"
" the lifeless eyes of a zombie child, and her unmoving mother."
msgstr ""
"비행기가 추락하는 순간, 악몽에서 깨어납니다. 비명 소리, 좀비 아이의 죽은 눈, 그리고 움직이지 않는 엄마의 모습이 기억납니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
msgid ""
"You wake from a dream.  You were on your knees, lapping blood from the "
"floor."
msgstr "꿈에서 깨어났다. 무릎을 꿇고 바닥에 떨어진 피를 핥고 있었다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "purple meteor"
msgstr "보라색 유성"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "broken line"
msgstr "끊어진 선"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "falling star"
msgstr "떨어지는 별"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "moving stars"
msgstr "움직이는 별들"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "unusual darkness"
msgstr "특이한 어둠"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "vanishing stars"
msgstr "사라지는 별들"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "shuffled stars"
msgstr "섞인 별들"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "new constellation of stars"
msgstr "새로운 별자리"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<weird_sky_thing>"
#. ~ Used within npc_socialize
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "green moon"
msgstr "녹색 달"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "So do you like cats or dogs?"
msgstr "그럼 당신은 고양이를 좋아하시나요, 아니면 개를 좋아하시나요?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "It's nice to know that the <zombies> don't feel pain."
msgstr "<zombies>들이 고통을 느끼지 않는다는 걸 아는 건 좋은 일이에요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Wherever we end up, at least we're still alive, right?"
msgstr "어디에 도착하든, 적어도 살아있으니까 괜찮지?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Somehow, I don't think I'll be going back to my old job anytime soon…"
msgstr "왠지, 저는 앞으로도 예전 직장으로 돌아가지 못할 것 같아요..."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "I am SO glad I don't need to deal with taxes or debt anymore."
msgstr "더 이상 세금이나 부채 문제를 다룰 필요가 없어서 너무 다행이에요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Geez, this is nothing like those Hollywood zombie films!"
msgstr "헐, 이건 할리우드 좀비 영화와는 전혀 다르네요!"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Do you ever think about the ethics of killing <zombies>?"
msgstr "<zombies>를 죽이는 것의 윤리에 대해 생각해 본 적이 있나요?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"Do you think living on a farm is dangerous because the roosters might "
"attract <zombies>?"
msgstr "농장에서 사는 게 위험하다고 생각하시나요? 수탉이 <zombies>를 끌어들일 수 있거든요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"I have dreamed of owning a house by the sea, but now I have nightmares of "
"what lurks beneath the waves."
msgstr "나는 바다 옆에 집을 갖는 꿈을 꾸었지만, 지금은 파도 아래에 무엇이 숨어 있는지에 대한 악몽을 꾸고 있습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"I liked walking through the forest, listening to the chirping of the birds "
"but now I am afraid that the birds might devour me."
msgstr "나는 숲을 거닐며 새들의 지저귐을 듣는 것을 좋아했지만, 지금은 새들이 나를 잡아먹을까 봐 두렵습니다."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"So you wet your toothbrush AFTER you apply toothpaste?  That's so weird."
msgstr "치약을 바른 후에 칫솔을 적신다고요? 참 이상하네요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "So is it pronounced gif or gif?"
msgstr "그럼 gif라고 발음해야 하나요, 아니면 gif라고 발음해야 하나요?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "What do you think the president is doing right now?"
msgstr "대통령께서 지금 무엇을 하고 계신다고 생각하시나요?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"What do you like to listen to?  Personally I'm into bass-heavy post-glam "
"speed polka."
msgstr "어떤 음악을 즐겨 들으세요? 저는 개인적으로 베이스가 강한 포스트 글램 스피드 폴카를 좋아해요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid ""
"Don't tell anyone else, but sometimes I like to sleep holding my teddy bear."
msgstr "다른 사람들에게 말하지 마세요. 하지만 가끔은 테디베어를 안고 자는 걸 좋아해요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Sometimes I see weird shit in the sky at night."
msgstr "가끔 밤에 하늘에 이상한 것이 보이곤 해요."

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "Did you see the <weird_sky_thing> in the sky last night, too?"
msgstr "당신도 어젯밤 하늘에 <weird_sky_thing>을 보셨나요?"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
#: data/json/snippets/npc_quips.json
msgid "I used to have a cat.  I really miss Mr. Cuddles…"
msgstr "예전에 고양이를 키웠었는데, 커들스 씨가 너무 그리워요…"

#. ~ Snippet in category "npc_socialize"
